e friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">73e4cecc-4cf9-402a-839a-4bf86d880600</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	As a trader in suburban Kano, my day starts early. I wake up before dawn to pray and then head to the market to buy fresh produce. I've been doing this for years, but lately, I've been feeling tired easily. I think it's because I'm not eating well. I often skip breakfast and rely on sugary snacks to get me through the day. My friends tell me I need to eat more vegetables and fruits, but I'm not sure what to do. I've tried a few times to change my diet, but it's hard to stick to it. I want to be healthy, but I don't know where to start. My biggest task is to manage my hypertension, and I'm not sure how to do it without giving up my favorite foods.\n\nOne day, I went to see a health worker at the local clinic. She asked me about my diet and lifestyle, and I told her about my struggles. She listened carefully and then explained that I need to eat more fruits and vegetables to help manage my blood pressure. She also suggested that I cut back on sugary snacks and eat more whole grains. I was a bit skeptical at first, but she showed me some simple recipes that I could try. She also encouraged me to take a short walk each day to help reduce stress.\n\nI decided to give it a try. I started by adding some fruits and vegetables to my meals and cutting back on sugary snacks. It wasn't easy at first, but I persisted. I also started taking short walks around the market during my breaks. I felt a bit silly at first, but it actually helped me clear my head and feel more energized. I started to notice improvements in my overall health, and it motivated me to keep going.\n\nIt's been a few months now, and I've seen significant improvements in my health. My blood pressure has decreased, and I have more energy throughout the day. I've also lost a bit of weight, which has boosted my confidence. I've learned to make healthy choices and stick to them. I'm now open to learning more about nutrition and making adjustments to my diet as needed. I'm grateful for the guidance I received from the health worker, and I'm excited to see where this new journey takes me.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/73e4cecc-4cf9-402a-839a-4bf86d880600_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storag