ile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "describe_location", "describe_food", "daily_routine", "medication", "healthcare_access", "tobacco", "alcohol", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
0fb49776-f302-4da6-9a9b-3749b270800a	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b819-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hausa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kano</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Islam</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Chinonso Okoro</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Male</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">35-44</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Trader</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Storytelling</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0fb49776-f302-4da6-9a9b-3749b270800a</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gymâ€”what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Chinonso, and I sell fruit and veggies at the market down by the station. It's a busy place, always full of people shouting and laughing. I usually start work before the sun even thinks about waking up, you know? I grab a quick piece of pap and some beans – that’s my breakfast. It keeps me going, I tell you. Sometimes I feel tired, like my legs are heavy, but I push on. I need to make enough money to pay the rent, and buy insulin for my blood pressure. It's a tough job, lugging crates and shouting prices.  Do you ever just feel like you can’t keep going?\n\nYesterday, I had to pack a big order for Mr. Maphalane, the butcher. He wanted a mountain of mangoes and pineapples. I was rushing, trying to get everything done quickly, and I forgot to take a proper break. I was so focused on getting the order right, I didn't even drink some water.  I tripped over a crate of oranges and spilled half the mangoes! Mr. Maphalane wasn’t happy, and I felt terrible. It made me realise I’m not thinking about myself at all. I need to slow down, I think. My blood pressure is always worrying me, and I need to look after my body, you know?\n\nToday, I went to see Dr. Sithole at the clinic. He’s a good man, always explaining things in a way you can understand. He told me that exercise helps with my blood pressure, and that eating healthy food – not just pap and beans all the time – can make a big difference. He said even a short walk each day can help. He also said that when I feel tired, it’s important to rest and drink plenty of water. He gave me a little booklet with some simple recipes. It felt a bit strange, talking about my health like that, but he seemed to really care.  I told him about the mangoes and the spill, and he just smiled and said, ‘Chinonso, sometimes things happen. The important thing is to learn from them.’\n\nI tried walking to the market this morning, just for fifteen minutes. It was hard at first, my legs felt wobbly, but I kept going. I even bought an apple for my lunch! It tasted really good, sweeter than usual. Mr. Maphalane still wants that big order for the weekend, and I’m going to try to do it better this time. I’m taking breaks, drinking water, and remembering what Dr. Sithole said.  It’s not easy changing habits, but I feel a little bit stronger, a little bit better. Maybe, just maybe, I can do this. I can feel myself getting a little bit more energy, and I think I’m starting to understand how important it is to take care of myself, even when I'm busy.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0fb49776-f302-4da6-9a9b-3749b270800a_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0fb49776-f302-4da6-9a9b-3749b270800a_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0fb49776-f302-4da6-9a9b-3749b270800a_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0fb49776-f302-4da6-9a9b-3749b270800a_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0fb49776-f302-4da6-9a9b-3749b270800a_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0fb49776-f302-4da6-9a9b-3749b270800a_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0fb49776-f302-4da6-9a9b-3749b270800a_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0fb49776-f302-4da6-9a9b-3749b270800a_3.mp3}	Sometimes I feel tired or discouraged—how can I stay motivated, and how does exercise help my blood sugar?	exercise	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:29:38.240722+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gemma-3-4b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Nari Kazehara is a 18-24 year old, \\nCulture: Hausa female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Entrepreneur, lives in a Rural (small community or countryside) in Kano. Disability: she has none. Religion: Islam. Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling. Activities: Socialising with family or friends. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once 