s.’  A subtle background of clinic equipment – a monitor beeping, a pen scratching on paper.", "Sound of Chinonso’s footsteps on a dusty street", "I tried walking to the market… It was hard at first, but I kept going. I even bought an apple… I feel a little bit stronger, a little bit better.’  The sound of birds chirping and distant market sounds.”"], "image_prompts": ["Wide shot of Chinonso, a 38-year-old man, standing in a bustling South African market, surrounded by colourful fruit and vegetables. He is wearing a worn, brown shirt and trousers, and has a slightly weary expression. He’s holding a crate of oranges, looking slightly overwhelmed by the activity. The lighting is bright and slightly harsh, reflecting off the fruit.  A small, worn smile plays on his lips.", "Medium shot of Chinonso, 38, kneeling amidst spilled mangoes and oranges on a dusty market floor. He looks frustrated and embarrassed, his face flushed with shame. He is wearing a stained apron. A few customers are visible in the background, looking at him with disapproval. The lighting is a warm, golden hue, highlighting the scattered fruit.", "Close-up of Chinonso, 38, sitting across from Dr. Sithole, a middle-aged, friendly-looking man in a white coat, at a simple clinic desk. Dr. Sithole is gesturing with a pen towards a colourful pamphlet. Chinonso is looking at the pamphlet with a thoughtful expression, a hint of uncertainty in his eyes. The background is blurred, showing the clinic interior with muted colours.", "Medium shot of Chinonso, 40, walking purposefully along a dusty street towards the market, carrying a bright red apple in his hand. He has a determined look on his face, and a slight spring in his step. The background shows a mix of low-income housing and small shops. The lighting is warm and slightly overcast, creating a hopeful atmosphere."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 9.490534574557573, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are easy home exercises suitable for a 35-44-year-old Hausa male trader living in urban Kano with type 2 diabetes and hypertension?\\",\\n  \\"How can I modify traditional Hausa meals to be healthier for diabetes management while keeping them halal in Kano?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community centers or social groups in Kano city where men can gather for physical activities without a gym?\\",\\n  \\"Which everyday items found in urban Nigerian households can be used for at-home workouts for someone with limited space?\\",\\n  \\"What are some culturally appropriate ways for Hausa men to stay physically active while balancing family and work responsibilities?\\",\\n  \\"How can I include my family in physical activities at home to improve our collective health in an urban setting like Kano?\\",\\n  \\"What are safe and halal-approved herbal remedies commonly used in Kano for managing hypertension alongside diabetes medication?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any Hausa storytelling traditions or gatherings in Kano that also involve physical movement or active participation?\\",\\n  \\"How much can daily walking in Kano city markets as a trader contribute to my weekly physical activity needs for diabetes control?\\",\\n  \\"What local resources or support networks exist in Kano for men with diabetes who want to stop smoking tobacco?\\",\\n  \\"What are the most common barriers for urban Hausa men in Kano to increasing their physical activity, and how can I overcome them at home?\\",\\n  \\"Are there Hausa-language online videos or guides for at-home exercises that respect Islamic values and fasting routines?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": ["city_town", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_frequency", "tobacco", "physical_activity", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
