            <td class="p-2">Suburban (near city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Trader</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Islamic study</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Spiritual or religious activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">â€” None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">11822266-9efd-4daf-8408-c217ef9fd25c</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I like to snackâ€”what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning, I wake up before the sun, grab my small breakfast — bread and a little jam — and head out to the market. I carry my bags like a soldier, and my legs feel heavy by the time I reach the shop. I used to think, 'Why should I walk if I can just run?' But today, I felt weak after my shift. My hands shook. I asked my brother, 'Why am I tired when I worked so hard?' He said, 'Maybe your body needs rest, not just work.' I didn’t listen. I thought, 'I’m fine, I’m a trader — I can handle anything.' So I stayed sitting all day, and by night, my feet felt numb. I didn’t know that walking just 10 minutes could help my blood sugar and my mind. That’s when I realized — maybe I need to move, not just stand still. But I didn’t know how long or how often.\n\nLast week, I went to the local clinic. The doctor, a kind woman named Amina, asked me, 'Nori, how are you feeling today?' I said, 'I’m fine, I just work hard.' She smiled and said, 'You need to walk — not for hours, but for 20 minutes every day. Even if it’s just around the block. You walk before you go to work, after you finish, and once in the evening. It helps your body feel strong, your blood sugar stay balanced, and your mind stay clear. You don’t need to run. You just need to walk — like a Muslim who walks to pray. It’s simple, it’s halal, and it’s good for your trade. I saw your hands shake last time — that’s a sign your body needs movement.' I said, 'But I have so much to do!' She said, 'You don’t have to do it all at once. Just start with one walk a day. And if you feel tired, stop and rest. That’s how you grow strong.' I felt calm. I said, 'I will try.'\n\nI started walking every morning — just 10 minutes. I walked past the mosque, past the fruit stall, and I saw the old man selling dates. I said, 'Good morning, Umar!' and he smiled. But on the third day, I got tired. I had a meeting and I forgot to walk. I felt dizzy. My sugar went high. I sat down and cried. I thought, 'I failed.' But then I remembered — the trade fair is coming in two weeks. I need to be strong to carry the goods, to talk to buyers, to move with confidence. So I said to myself, 'I will walk again — even if I feel weak.' I walked again, slowly, with my head down, and I felt better. I even took a deep breath and said, 'Allah, help me stay strong.' That night, I slept better.\n\nNow, I walk every day — 20 minutes. I walk before work, after work, and once after dinner. I feel strong. My legs don’t shake. My mind is clear. I even helped my cousin carry the goods to the market. I said, 'This is how I stay healthy — by walking.' I still don’t run. I don’t need to. I just walk. And when I see a young man struggling, I say, 'Try walking for 10 minutes — it helps your body and your trade.' I now know — exercise isn’t just for fitness. It’s for strength, for focus, for peace. And I will keep walking — not just for health, but for my future trade fair. I am proud. I am strong. I am alive.\n\nI used to think walking was for the weak. Now I know — walking is for the strong. And the strong are those who care for their body, like they care for their faith. I walk because I believe in Allah, in my work, and in my future. I walk every day. I walk for 20 minutes. I walk with purpose. And when I finish, I feel like a true trader — not just of goods, but of health, of energy, of peace. I will keep walking. I will keep learning. And I will share this with others — because health is not a gift. It is a choice. And I chose to walk.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/11822266-9efd-4daf-8408-c217ef9fd25c_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/11822266-9efd-4daf-8408-c217ef9fd25c_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/11822266-9efd-4daf-8408-c217ef9fd25c_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/11822266-9efd-4daf-8408-c217ef9fd25c_3.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/11822266-9efd-4daf-8408-c217ef9fd25c_4.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/11822266-9efd