ont-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegetarian</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">86c99fde-f1af-415f-9e02-ff23a4f05d3d</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up every morning, get dressed in my formal banking attire, and head to the kitchen to make some breakfast. Usually, it's something quick like oatmeal with fruit or scrambled eggs with whole wheat toast. I've been doing this for years, and it's become a routine. But lately, I've been feeling a bit sluggish, and my performance at work has been suffering. I've got a big project coming up, and I need to be on top of my game. I've been wondering, how often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health? I mean, I do try to get to the gym 5-7 days a week, but is that enough? Today, I had a small task to finish a report, but I found myself struggling to focus. I just couldn't seem to get it done, and my boss wasn't happy. I realized that maybe my lack of energy and focus was related to my health.\n\nI decided to visit my local healthcare clinic to get some advice. The health worker, Mrs. Patel, was very helpful and explained that regular exercise and a balanced diet are crucial for maintaining energy levels and focus. She told me that I should aim for at least 30 minutes of moderate-intensity exercise per day, and that I should try to include a variety of foods in my diet, including plenty of fruits, vegetables, and whole grains. I was a bit resistant at first, I mean, I've been doing okay so far, right? But Mrs. Patel was very clear and simple in her explanation, and she gave me some personalized advice that took into account my busy schedule as a banker. She also reminded me that it's always better to prevent health problems than to try to fix them later.\n\nI tried to follow Mrs. Patel's advice, but it wasn't easy. I had to adjust my routine to fit in the extra exercise, and I found myself struggling to wake up earlier in the morning. I also had to make some changes to my diet, which was hard because I love trying all the different foods at the restaurants near my office. But I knew I had to persist, because I have a big presentation coming up, and I need to be able to focus and perform well. I had a minor setback when I missed a day of exercise, but I didn't let it discourage me. I got back on track, and I started to notice some small improvements in my energy levels.\n\nIt's been a few weeks now, and I can really see the difference. I've been exercising regularly, and I've been eating a balanced diet. I feel more energetic, and I'm able to focus better at work. I was able to finish my report on time, and my boss was impressed. And when it came time for my big presentation, I was confident and prepared. I nailed it! I'm so glad I made the decision to prioritize my health. I realize now that it's not just about avoiding health problems, but about feeling good and performing well in all areas of my life. I'm open to continuing to learn and improve my health, and I'm excited to see where this journey takes me.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/86c99fde-f1af-415f-9e02-ff23a4f05d3d_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/86c99fde-f1af-415f-9e02-ff23a4f05d3d_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/86c99fde-f1af-415f-9e02-ff23a4f05d3d_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/86c99fde-f1af-415f-9e02-ff23a4f05d3d_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/86c99fde-f1af-415f-9e02-ff23a4f05d3d_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/86c99fde-f1af-415f-9e02-ff23a4f05d3d_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/86c99fde-f1af-415f-9e02-ff23a4f05d3d_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/86c99fde-f1af-415f-9e02-ff23a4f05d3d_3.mp3}	How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:10:36.078527+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "Llama-3.3-70B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Wanjiku Mwangi is a 25-34