old">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Business owner</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Reading</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Close friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up every morning, get ready for work, and head to my business. As a vegan, I thought I was eating healthy, but I never really considered how my diet and lack of exercise would affect my work. I mean, what's the connection, right? I just know I feel tired all the time. One day, I had a small task to deliver some goods to a client, but I ended up being too exhausted to even lift the boxes. I had to ask my employee to do it for me. I thought to myself, "How did I become so weak?" I knew I had to make some changes, but I didn't know where to start.\n\nI decided to visit my local healthcare clinic to get some advice. The nurse told me that as a person with diabetes, I need to be careful about what I eat and how much I exercise. She explained that regular physical activity can help control my blood sugar levels and give me more energy. She suggested I start with short walks and gradually increase the distance. I was a bit resistant at first, thinking that exercise would be too strenuous for me, but the nurse reassured me that it's safe and beneficial. She also gave me some vegan meal ideas that would help me manage my diabetes.\n\nI tried to follow the nurse's advice, but it wasn't easy. I started taking short walks, but I found it hard to stick to a routine. I would walk for a few days, then stop for a week. I also struggled to change my eating habits. I would eat healthy meals for a few days, then go back to my old habits. I had a minor setback when I slipped and fell while walking, but I didn't give up. I knew I had to keep trying because I had a bigger task coming up - a big order to deliver to a client. I needed to be strong and energetic to get it done.\n\nIt's been a few weeks since I started exercising and eating healthy, and I can feel the difference. I have more energy, and my blood sugar levels are under control. I was able to deliver the big order to my client without any problems. I'm proud of myself for making these changes, and I'm open to continuing to improve my health. I've even started reading about different types of exercises and healthy recipes to try. I feel like I've taken control of my health, and it's given me a new sense of confidence.\n\nNow, I'm looking forward to the future, knowing that I can manage my diabetes and stay healthy. I'm grateful for the support of my healthcare team and my friends and family. I know that I still have a lot to learn, but I'm excited to continue on this journey. I'm Wanjiku Mwangi, and I'm taking control of my health, one step at a time.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0_3.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0_4.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0_3.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/51e660da-670c-4933-955d-dc38c979a5e0_4.mp3}	What kinds of exercises are safe and helpful for someone with diabetes?	exercise	female	consistency	2026-03-23 13:10:36.51033+00	{"label": "GOOD", "model": "Llama-3.3-70B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Wanjiku Mwangi is a 25-34 year old, \\nCulture: Kikuyu female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she i