port network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Close friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I'm Wanjiku Mwangi, and I love my job as an accountant. I work hard every day, and when I get home, I like to relax with my friends and family. We often eat late at night, and I never thought it was a big deal. But lately, I've been feeling tired and sluggish, and my blood sugar levels have been all over the place. I've been taking my medication, but I know I need to make some changes to my diet and lifestyle. The problem is, I don't know where to start.\n\nOne day, I had a big project due at work, and I was up late trying to finish it. I ordered some pizza and ate it while I worked, but the next morning, my blood sugar levels were through the roof. I felt terrible, and I couldn't concentrate at work. I realized that I needed to make some changes, but I didn't know what to do. That's when I decided to visit my local healthcare clinic. The nurse there was very helpful, and she explained to me how eating late at night can affect my blood sugar levels. She told me that I should try to eat earlier in the evening and choose healthier foods. She also gave me some tips on how to stay active and manage my stress.\n\nAt first, it was hard for me to adjust to the new routine. I would get home from work and feel like eating something quick and easy, but then I would remember what the nurse told me. I started trying to eat earlier in the evening, and I began to choose healthier foods like vegetables and whole grains. But it wasn't easy, and there were times when I slipped up. One night, I was working late and I ordered some fried chicken, and the next morning, my blood sugar levels were high again. I felt like I had failed, but then I remembered why I was making these changes in the first place. I had a big presentation coming up at work, and I wanted to feel my best.\n\nI persisted, and slowly but surely, I started to see some improvements. My blood sugar levels were more stable, and I had more energy. I was able to concentrate at work, and I felt more confident. When the day of the presentation arrived, I was ready. I had practiced my speech, and I had eaten a healthy breakfast. I felt great, and I nailed the presentation. My colleagues were impressed, and I felt proud of myself. I realized that making these changes hadn't been easy, but it had been worth it.\n\nNow, I'm more open to continued health improvement. I've started to explore new recipes and try new foods. I've also started to exercise more regularly, and I've found that it helps me to manage my stress. I've learned that taking care of my health is an ongoing process, and it's not always easy. But I know that it's worth it, and I'm grateful for the support of my friends and family. I'm Wanjiku Mwangi, and I'm taking control of my health, one step at a time.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995_3.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995_4.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995_3.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/9162053a-e9d5-4964-a69d-e135209e7995_4.mp3}	I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? 	diet	female	consistency	2026-03-23 13:10:36