     <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up every morning before dawn to start my day as a tea farmer in Kiambu. My daily routine is packed, from tending to the tea bushes to managing the farm. I love my job, but I have to admit, I haven't been taking the best care of my health. I've been diagnosed with type 2 diabetes, and I know I need to make some changes. But it's hard when you're used to a certain way of living. I often find myself eating late at night, which I know isn't good for my blood sugar levels. Today, I had a small task to complete - to harvest a batch of tea leaves for a client. But as I was working, I started to feel dizzy and disoriented. I realized that my blood sugar levels must have been out of control.\n\nI decided to visit my local healthcare clinic to get some advice on how to manage my diabetes. The healthcare worker was very helpful and explained to me how my late-night eating habits were affecting my blood sugar levels. She advised me to start eating smaller, more frequent meals throughout the day, and to avoid eating at least two hours before bedtime. She also recommended that I start monitoring my blood sugar levels more regularly. I was a bit resistant to the idea of changing my routine, but I knew I had to try something. So, I started making some changes to my diet and exercise routine.\n\nIt wasn't easy, though. I struggled to adjust to the new routine, and I found myself slipping back into my old habits. I would often forget to monitor my blood sugar levels, or I would eat late at night because I was too tired to cook a proper meal. But I knew I had to persist. I had a larger task coming up - to harvest a large batch of tea leaves for a big client. I knew I needed to be in top shape to complete the task, so I kept trying. I started carrying a small notebook with me to track my blood sugar levels, and I made a conscious effort to eat smaller meals throughout the day.\n\nAs the days went by, I started to notice a gradual improvement in my health. My blood sugar levels were more stable, and I had more energy throughout the day. I was able to complete my tasks without feeling dizzy or disoriented. And when the day of the big harvest arrived, I was ready. I worked tirelessly from dawn till dusk, and I was able to complete the task with ease. I felt a sense of pride and accomplishment, and I knew that I owed it all to the changes I had made to my diet and exercise routine. I was open to continued health improvement, and I was excited to see where this new journey would take me.\n\nNow, I'm not perfect, and I still have my slip-ups. But I've learned to be kind to myself and to take things one step at a time. I've also learned to appreciate the small victories, like being able to complete a task without feeling exhausted. And I've learned to prioritize my health, because I know that it's essential to living a happy and fulfilling life. I'm grateful for the support of my healthcare worker and my family, and I'm excited to see what the future holds. I know that I'll always be a work in progress, but I'm ready for the challenge.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4_3.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4_4.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4_3.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4cbb3ffd-119c-4c30-88db-5fc4f34e92f4_4.mp3}	I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?	diet	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:10:37.099004+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "Llama-3.3-70B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Wanjiku Mwangi is a 25-34 year old, \\nCulture: Kikuyu female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Accountant, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Kiambu. Disability: she has none. Religion: Christianity (Methodist). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling. Activities: Socialising with family or friends. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication). Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: None. Diet restrictions: No Restrictions. Smoking: Yes. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 5-7 days. Support network: Close friends. Health goals: Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?. her food access Easy access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Wanjiku Mwangi and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in English that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I 