ties, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "social_support", "audio_prompts": ["Ambient soundscape of a rural Kenyan morning: rooster crows, distant cattle, gentle wind rustling through coffee leaves. Wanja’s voice, 22, Kikuyu female, slightly raspy and tired, begins: ‘The sun comes up early here…’ A faint rhythmic sound of hoeing in the background.", "Sound of heavy objects falling to the ground, followed by Wanja’s frustrated sigh, 22, Kikuyu female, voice slightly strained. David’s voice, 25, Kikuyu male, speaking calmly and gently in the background: ‘Wanja, you need to take care of yourself.’ The sound of footsteps on dry earth.", "Sound of a stethoscope being placed on Wanja’s arm, 22, Kikuyu female, voice hesitant. Dr. Okeke’s voice, 50s, Kenyan male, providing clear and reassuring instructions.  Subtle background sounds of clinic activity – the murmur of other patients, the clinking of instruments.", "Sound of Wanja and Mama’s voices, 22 & 55, Kikuyu female, chatting happily as they walk. The sounds of a busy market – vendors calling out prices, chickens clucking, children laughing.  A light, upbeat Kenyan folk music melody plays softly in the background."], "image_prompts": ["Wide shot of Wanja Mwangi, 22, Kikuyu female, standing in a rural Kenyan coffee field at sunrise. She wears a simple, faded blue cotton dress and a woven headscarf. Her posture is slightly slumped with fatigue, but her gaze is determined as she looks towards the distant hills. The ground is covered in damp earth and coffee seedlings. Soft, golden light illuminates the scene, creating a peaceful atmosphere.", "Medium shot of Wanja Mwangi, 22, Kikuyu female, kneeling in a muddy field, struggling to hold a heavy sack of fertilizer. Her face is etched with frustration and exertion. David, her husband, 25, Kikuyu male, stands nearby with a concerned expression, his hands raised in a gesture of support. The scene is dominated by the brown earth and the vibrant green of the coffee plants.", "Close-up shot of Wanja Mwangi, 22, Kikuyu female, sitting on a wooden stool in a small, brightly lit clinic room. Dr. Okeke, a middle-aged Kenyan male, is examining her arm with a stethoscope. Wanja’s expression is a mixture of apprehension and curiosity. The background shows shelves filled with medical supplies and a simple examination table.", "Medium shot of Wanja Mwangi, 22, Kikuyu female, walking alongside her mother, Mama, 55, Kikuyu female, towards a small market stall in a rural Kenyan village. Both women are smiling and chatting, carrying baskets filled with produce. The scene is bustling with activity, showcasing the vibrant colors of the local market and the warmth of community life."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 10.488683498822725, "task_parent_id": "5ac208d9-5475-4b18-bae0-4ad37517b356", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are effective exercise routines for young Kikuyu women coffee farmers in rural Murangâ€™a living with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can I increase my physical activity with limited resources and time as a coffee farmer in the Kenyan countryside?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local support groups or programs in Murangâ€™a for young women managing diabetes who also smoke tobacco?\\",\\n  \\"What affordable and easily available healthy food options meet Halal requirements in rural areas of Murangâ€™a with limited food access?\\",\\n  \\"How does being a high-frequency tobacco smoker affect diabetes management, especially for young adults in rural Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"What are practical ways to include more healthy habits into my daily farming and gardening activities in Murangâ€™a?\\",\\n  \\"Are there traditional Kikuyu farming or gardening methods that help improve physical health or control diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How often should someone with type 2 diabetes who is only able to exercise 1-2 days a week try to increase activity for better health outcomes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there culturally accepted herbal or traditional remedies in the Murangâ€™a area that safely support diabetes management alongside medication?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find information on Halal-certified diabetes-friendly recipes using foods grown locally in rural Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"What local health initiatives or public programs in Murangâ€™a support tobacco reduction for young women farmers with diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can I better coordinate with my local healthcare provider in rural Murangâ€™a to manage both my diabetes and smoking habits?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "ou