     <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">22511d50-234c-41cf-9153-6f65c243cc65</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensiveâ€”how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up every morning at 5 am to start my day as an agro-business owner in rural Murang'a. My daily routine is packed with managing my farm, selling produce, and taking care of my health. As a young Kikuyu woman living with type 2 diabetes, I have to be mindful of what I eat and how I take care of my body. However, I often find myself neglecting my health needs due to the demands of my work. I love traditional Kikuyu foods like githeri and irio, but I know I need to make some changes to manage my diabetes. One day, I had a small task to deliver some produce to a nearby market, but I ended up feeling too tired and had to cancel the trip. I realized that my neglect of my health was affecting my work.\n\nI decided to visit my local healthcare clinic to get some advice on managing my diabetes. The nurse was very helpful and explained to me how regular physical activity, like volleyball, can help improve my insulin sensitivity and control my blood sugar levels. She also advised me to make some changes to my diet, like eating more whole grains, fruits, and vegetables, and reducing my intake of sugary and processed foods. I was resistant at first, unsure if I could make such big changes, but the nurse reassured me that it was possible and that she would support me every step of the way. She also told me about some local recipes that are suitable for people with diabetes, like githeri and mukimo, and how I can adapt them to fit my dietary needs.\n\nI tried to follow the nurse's advice, but it wasn't easy. I had to adjust my routine to fit in time for physical activity and cooking healthy meals. I started playing volleyball with some friends, but it was tough at first. I would get tired easily and had to stop often to rest. I also struggled to change my diet, as I was used to eating traditional Kikuyu foods that are high in carbohydrates. I had a minor setback when I ate some sugary snacks and my blood sugar levels spiked. But I didn't give up. I knew I had to make these changes to manage my diabetes and achieve my goal of delivering produce to the nearby market.\n\nAs I continued to make changes to my lifestyle, I started to see gradual improvements in my health. I had more energy, and my blood sugar levels were more stable. I was able to play volleyball for longer periods without getting tired, and I even started to enjoy the physical activity. I also found some delicious and healthy recipes that fit my dietary needs, like githeri with vegetables and lean protein. I was proud of myself for making these changes and felt more confident in my ability to manage my diabetes. I finally felt ready to take on the larger task of delivering produce to the nearby market, and I was successful.\n\nNow, I feel like I have a better handle on my diabetes, and I'm more open to continuing to make healthy changes. I've learned that taking care of my health is essential to my work and overall well-being. I'm grateful for the support of my local healthcare clinic and the advice of the nurse. I'm also proud of myself for making lifestyle changes and persisting despite the challenges. I know that I still have a lot to learn, but I'm excited for the journey ahead. I'm looking forward to continuing to play volleyball, cook healthy meals, and manage my diabetes. I know that with the right support and mindset, I can achieve my health goals and live a happy and healthy life.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/22511d50-234c-41cf-9153-6f65c243cc65_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/22511d50-234c-41cf-9153-6f65c243cc65_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/22511d50-234c-41cf-9153-6f65c243cc65_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/22511d50-234c-41cf-9153-6f65c243cc65_3.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/22511d50-234c-4