            <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Football (soccer)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">â€” None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up every morning, get ready for work on my farm, and head out to tend to my crops. As a farmer, I need to be physically fit to keep up with the demands of my job. But to be honest, I haven't been taking care of my health like I should. I love playing football with my friends, but I haven't been able to join them as much as I used to. My diet consists of mostly traditional Hausa dishes like tuwo and miyan kubewa, which are delicious but not always the healthiest. I've been having some issues with my blood sugar levels, and my doctor has been reminding me to take my insulin injections regularly. But I often find myself neglecting my health needs, and it shows in my work. Just the other day, I was trying to fix a broken fence on my farm, but I ended up getting tired easily and had to leave it for another day.\n\nI decided to visit my local healthcare clinic to get some advice on how to manage my health better. The healthcare worker, Sister Fatima, was very kind and understanding. She explained to me that as a person with type 2 diabetes, I need to be mindful of my diet and physical activity. She advised me to start with small, achievable goals, like taking a 30-minute walk every day and eating more fruits and vegetables. She also reminded me to take my insulin injections on time and to monitor my blood sugar levels regularly. I was a bit resistant at first, but she reassured me that it's never too late to make a change.\n\nI tried to follow Sister Fatima's advice, but it wasn't easy. I had to adjust my routine to fit in the daily walks and healthy meals. There were times when I felt like giving up, especially when I had to sacrifice my favorite foods. But I kept reminding myself of the upcoming harvest season, when I'll need to be in top shape to work long hours on my farm. I persisted, and slowly but surely, I started to notice improvements in my energy levels and overall health. However, I did have a minor setback when I forgot to take my insulin injection one morning, and I had to deal with the consequences.\n\nIt's been a few weeks since I started making changes to my lifestyle, and I can already see the difference. I'm able to work longer hours on my farm without getting tired, and I've even started playing football with my friends again. I feel more confident and in control of my health. The harvest season is approaching, and I'm excited to tackle the challenges that come with it. I'm grateful for Sister Fatima's guidance and support, and I'm open to continuing to learn and improve my health habits. Who knows, maybe one day I'll even start a football team for farmers in my community!\n\nAs I look back on my journey, I realize that taking care of my health is not just about me, but about my community and my livelihood. As a farmer, I need to be physically fit to provide for my family and contribute to my community. I'm proud of the progress I've made, and I'm excited to see where this new path takes me. I know that I'll face challenges along the way, but I'm ready to take them on, one step at a time. And who knows, maybe one day I'll be able to share my story with others and inspire them to take control of their health too.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9_3.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9_4.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9_3.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/dbf87c97-5733-4a0d-abe3-e66f90cc3dd9_4.mp3}	I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?	exercise	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:29:34.632182+00	{"label": "GOOD", "model": "Llama-3.3-70B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Chinelo Okafor is a 35-44 year old, \\nCulture: Hausa female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Trader, lives in a Suburban (near city or town) in Kano. Disability: she has none. Religion: Islam. Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling. Activities: Socialising with family or friends. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: None. Diet restrictions: Halal. Smoking: Yes. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 5-7 days. Support network: Community or religious group. Health goals: Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?. her food access Easy access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Chinelo Okafor and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in English that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken English, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in English.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in English.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "iteration", "audio_prompts": ["Aminu Garba's voice is heard, speaking in a moderate tone, with a slight Hausa accent, saying 'I need to take care of my health, but it's hard to make changes', with some background noise of birds chirping and wind blowing.", "Sister Fatima's voice is heard, speaking in a calm and reassuring tone, saying 'You can do it, Aminu, just take it one step at a time', with some background noise of a clinic, nearby.", "Aminu Garba's voice is heard, speaking in a determined tone, saying 'I'll do it, I'll make the changes', with some background noise of footsteps and door closing.", "Aminu Garba's voice is heard, speaking in an excited tone, saying 'I'm playing football again, and I feel great', with some background noise of cheering and laughter.", "Aminu Garba's voice is heard, speaking in a reflective tone, saying 'I'm proud of myself, and I'm excited to see where this new path takes me', with some background noise of wind blowing and birds chirping."], "image_prompts": ["Aminu Garba, a 25-34 year old Hausa male, is shown walking on a dirt path, wearing a white kaftan and a cap, with a few trees and farms in the background, medium shot.", "Sister Fatima, a female healthcare worker, is shown sitting in a clinic, wearing a white coat and a hijab, with Aminu Garba sitting across from her, looking concerned, wide shot.", "Aminu Garba is shown holding a plate of fruits and vegetables, with a few traditional Hausa dishes in the background, looking determined, close-up.", "Aminu Garba is shown playing football with his friends, wearing a jersey and shorts, with a few spectators cheering them on, medium shot.", "Aminu Garba is shown standing in front of his farm, wearing a white kaftan and a cap, with a few crops and trees in the background, looking proud and confident, wide shot."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 7.72532412482471, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some easy-to-prepare, Halal, diabetes-friendly Hausa dishes with ingredients commonly available in urban Kano?\\",\\n  \\"Which traditional Hausa foods should I avoid or modify as someone with type 2 diabetes living in Kano city?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local markets or supermarkets in urban Kano where I can find affordable healthy food options for a diabetic diet?\\",\\n  \\"Can you suggest a one-week sample menu for a young male Hausa farmer with type 2 diabetes who works in Kano and observes Halal dietary restrictions?\\",\\n  \\"How can I adapt popular Hausa street foods served in Kano to be healthier for managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What are common challenges for urban Hausa farmers in Kano in maintaining healthy eating habits, and how can they be overcome?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local community support groups or healthcare programs in Kano city for young adults managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What easy meal prep strategies can I use during the farming season in Kano to stick to a healthy, diabetes-friendly diet?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best local physical activity options in urban Kano for men like me who want to stay active and control their diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can I balance fasting during Ramadan with managing my diabetes, given my active farming routine in Kano?\\",\\n  \\"Are there Hausa herbal or traditional remedies popular in Kano that are safe and effective to use alongside my prescribed diabetes medication?\\",\\n  \\"What football clubs or social sports opportunities exist in Kano for adults interested in regular physical activity for diabetes management?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format"