ural.", "Sister Agnes, a woman in her 30s, speaks in a calm, reassuring tone, nearby Wanjiku Mwangi, 45-50 years old. Agnes says, 'Wanjiku, that late-night sweet stuff isn't helping.' Her voice is clear and professional. Wanjiku responds with a hesitant, 'Oh…' her voice slightly muffled and uncertain. Background sounds of a quiet clinic – distant chatter and the hum of a fan. Wanjiku's voice shows mild resistance.", "Wanjiku Mwangi, 45-50 years old, whispers to herself, 'I really wanted that biscuit…' Her voice is filled with longing and internal conflict. The sound of rustling plastic as she resists reaching for the biscuit. A slight intake of breath as she makes a decision. Background sounds of a rural kitchen – a crackling fire and the distant sounds of livestock. Her voice is low and determined.", "Wanjiku Mwangi, 45-50 years old, laughs heartily, her voice full of genuine amusement, across the room from Man Kamau, an elderly man. She's saying, 'He was so grateful!' Her laughter transitions to a standard conversational level as she continues, '…he gave me a beautiful scarf for Njeri.' Background sounds of a bustling market – chatter, animal noises, and the sound of vehicles. Her voice is energetic and joyful."], "image_prompts": ["A candid, natural, unposed medium shot of Wanjiku Mwangi, a 45-50 year old woman, sitting on a wooden stool in a dimly lit kitchen, looking slightly frustrated as she reaches for a biscuit. The kitchen is simple, with clay walls and a corrugated iron roof. A half-empty cup of tea sits beside her. Texture of the biscuit wrapper and the rough wood of the stool are visible. Natural light filtering through a small window. Wanjiku's face shows a mixture of exhaustion and desire.", "A wide shot of Wanjiku Mwangi, 45-50 years old, sitting across from Sister Agnes, a nurse in a clean, bright clinic. Wanjiku is looking down at a handwritten menu in her hands, her brow furrowed in thought. Sister Agnes is leaning forward, speaking gently. The clinic has simple, functional furnishings. Sunlight streams through the window, illuminating dust motes in the air. The scene conveys a sense of trust and hope. Wanjiku's hands are clasped in her lap, showing slight tension.", "A candid, natural, unposed medium shot of Wanjiku Mwangi, 45-50 years old, standing in her kitchen, looking at a plate of sukuma wiki (collard greens) with a slightly disappointed expression. She is holding an orange in her hand. The kitchen is rustic and functional. The lighting is soft and diffused. Wanjiku's shoulders are slightly slumped, conveying a sense of struggle. Focus is on her face and hands.", "A candid, natural, unposed medium shot of Wanjiku Mwangi, 45-50 years old, smiling broadly as she helps an elderly man, Man Kamau, load sacks of coffee beans onto a truck. She is standing beside him, her posture strong and confident. The scene is set in a rural coffee farm, with lush green hills in the background. The lighting is warm and golden. Wanjiku's face radiates energy and satisfaction. Man Kamau is looking at her with gratitude."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 83.15678292665726, "task_parent_id": "15cba823-8a2b-4db6-ba4e-cb31c6d5a61b", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are examples of affordable, locally available healthy foods in rural Kiambu for managing type 2 diabetes and hypertension?\\",\\n  \\"Are there specific Kikuyu herbal remedies used in Kiambu to support blood sugar control, and how do they interact with oral diabetes medications?\\",\\n  \\"How does being a coffee farmer in rural Kenya affect my risk of high blood pressure or fluctuating blood sugar levels due to daily routine and physical activity?\\",\\n  \\"What meal planning strategies can a 45-54 year old female coffee farmer in rural Kiambu use to avoid eating late at night, considering limited food access?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best types of physical exercises for women in their 40s and 50s with hypertension and diabetes in small Kenyan rural communities?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find diabetes support groups or education programs near my local healthcare clinic in rural Kiambu county?\\",\\n  \\"What traditional Kikuyu foods should someone with diabetes and high blood pressure avoid or include in their diet?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local community initiatives in Kiambu that help rural farmers with access to fresh vegetables and healthy foods for chronic disease management?\\",\\n  \\"How does attending family or social gatherings in rural Kiambu influence my dietary choices and blood sugar management as a Kikuyu woman?\\",\\n  \\"What are common challenges rural Kenyan women coffee farmers face in maintaining consistent medication and lifestyle routines for type 2 diabetes control?\\",\\n  \\"How is Christian (non-mainstream) church life in rural Kiambu involved in supporting health and well-being for adult women with chronic illnesses?\\",\\n  \\"What low-cost, practical ways can I reduce sodium and unhealthy fats in traditional Kikuyu meals while cooking at home in Kiambu?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": ["city_town", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "occupation", "activities", "medication", "healthcare_access", "alcohol", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
