w would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Teacher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Horticulture</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">9daf4198-8d50-489e-90f1-a081641d2247</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gymâ€”what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning, I wake up and look after my little garden behind the house. I love my horticulture, it gives me peace and a reason to move my body, you know? I usually have sweet tea and sliced white bread with blueband for breakfast, just the way my mother liked. I think, 'If I just walk in my garden, isn't that enough exercise?' But one Tuesday, I had to clean out the storeroom for Mama’s birthday, and I got all dizzy and tired. I left everything half-done. Was walking really enough, or is there something I’m not knowing about taking care of myself when I am working?\n\nThe next day, Nurse Sarah at our local clinic saw me. She asked, 'Sawa, Wanjiku, tell me what exercise you do.' I shrugged and said, 'I walk in my shamba every day, nurse.' She smiled nicely and said, 'Walking is very good, Wanjiku, but your muscles need to work in different ways. Try gentle stretches or lifting small buckets, and do it bit by bit. Your blood sugar will thank you, and you’ll finish your work easier.' I wanted to argue – was it not enough, all this walking? But something about her words made sense.\n\nI started trying, small-small. First, I added two buckets of water from the tank to my garden chores. Eish! I felt so stiff the next day, and my arms hurt. I almost said, 'Ah, let me just go back to my easy walk.' But Mama’s birthday was coming – I needed to finish cleaning that storeroom! That big job was waiting, so I pushed myself to keep up with the new plan Nurse Sarah showed me.\n\nAfter a week, I was moving with more energy. One bright Saturday, I cleared out the whole storeroom, dusted the shelves, washed the floor, and didn’t feel tired at all. My cousins even cheered, 'Wanjiku, you are strong nowadays!' Now, I am starting to think, maybe I can try more than only walking. Maybe I'll even join the clinic’s weekend exercise group. Why not, if it helps me feel this good?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9daf4198-8d50-489e-90f1-a081641d2247_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9daf4198-8d50-489e-90f1-a081