ow would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Commercial farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Storytelling</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Close friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">2288e0a8-2c9a-4a3e-89b5-40ddb24c2767</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">What kinds of exercises are safe and helpful for someone with diabetes?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Nduta, and I work at the market in Khayelitsha. It’s a busy place, full of shouting and people selling all sorts of things – fruit, vegetables, clothes, you name it. I usually get home pretty late, around nine or ten. Sometimes, if I’m really busy, I’ll grab a sadi and some chips before I go to bed. It’s quick, and it tastes good, you know? But Mama always says, ‘Nduta, you need to look after your body.’ But I just think, ‘I’m tired, Mama. Just one small thing won't hurt.’  I don’t really think much about it, do I? I just want to get home and rest.  Do you ever feel like you just want to do something, anything, just to feel a little better?  I do. \n\nYesterday, I was helping Mr. Dlamini pack up his stall – he sells beautiful woven mats. We were trying to get everything done before the rain started, and I was so focused on lifting a heavy box of mats that I didn’t even notice my foot had twisted a little. It hurt a lot! I tried to keep working, but I kept stumbling. Mr. Dlamini said, ‘Nduta, you need to sit down! You’re not working properly.’  And he was right. I felt so silly, and I knew it was because I was pushing myself too hard.  It was frustrating, and I just wanted to get it over with. It made me think, maybe Mama was right about needing to take care of myself.\n\nToday, I went to the clinic. Nurse Zola was really nice. She asked me about my eating habits and how I felt. I told her about the late nights and the chips. She smiled and said, ‘Nduta, eating late can make your blood sugar go up and down. That can make you feel tired and grumpy, and it’s not good for your body.’ She showed me a picture of a plate with lots of vegetables and some chicken.  She said, ‘Try to eat a healthy meal before you go to bed, even if it’s just a small one.’  I promised I would, but it’s hard, you know? It's easier to just grab something quick.  It's a bit like when I’m sorting the fruit – I just want to get it done quickly, and sometimes I don't pay attention to how much I'm lifting.\n\nI tried to eat a small bowl of pap with some beans last night. It wasn’t as good as the chips, but it felt good inside.  And today, I felt…lighter.  Mr. Dlamini asked me if I was feeling better, and I said yes!  I’m still working hard at the market, but I’m more careful now. I’m even planning on helping to organize the market stall next week – a really big job!  I feel like I can do it, because I’m taking better care of myself.  It’s like, if my body feels good, I can do anything.  And Mama would be so proud.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2288e0a8-2c9a-4a3e-89b5-40ddb24c2767_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2288e0a8-2c9a-4a3e-89b5-40ddb24c2767_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2288e0a8-2c9a-4a3e-89b5-40ddb24c2767_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2288e0a8-2c9a-4a3e-89b5-40ddb24c2767_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2288e0a8-2c9a-4a3e-89b5-40ddb24c2767_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2288e0a8-2c9a-4a3e-89b5-40ddb24c2767_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2288e0a8-2c9a-4a3e-89b5-40ddb24c2767_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2288e0a8-2c9a-4a3e-89b5-40ddb24c2767_3.mp3}	I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? 	diet	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:10:42.936752+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gemma-3-4b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Wanjiku Mwangi is a 35-44 year old, \\nCulture: Kikuyu female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Business owner, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Murang'a. Disability: she has none. Religion: Islam. Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling. Activities: Socialising with family or friends. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: None. Diet restrictions: Halal. Smoking: Yes. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 0 days. Support network: Community or religious group. Health goals: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . her food access Easy access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Wanjiku Mwangi and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in English that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken English, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in English.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- Al