ht frown and a hand on her hip while holding a cup of tea. Nearby, her farm animals graze quietly. It is late afternoon with warm golden sunlight casting long shadows. She looks tired but determined, faced with the challenge of adjusting her daily eating and farming routine.", "Wide shot of Akinyi Odongo smiling warmly while fixing a wooden fence with her hands. The environment is a modest rural homestead surrounded by green crops and a few goats. She looks confident and peaceful under a bright blue sky, wearing a simple cotton blouse and headscarf. Another woman, a neighbour, stands nearby watching with encouragement. The scene feels hopeful and full of life."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 3.10124871134758, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are effective ways for a 25-34 year old female Luo Anglican farmer living in Kisumu city to stay motivated with regular exercise while managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Which vegan traditional Luo dishes are good for blood sugar control and are easy to prepare with locally available urban Kisumu foods?\\",\\n  \\"How can urban subsistence farmers like Akinyi Odongo in Kisumu balance farming activities and 1-2 days of formal exercise for better diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community exercise programs or walking groups in Kisumu city that support adults with diabetes, especially for those with limited family support?\\",\\n  \\"How does living alone as a Luo woman in urban Kisumu affect access to diabetes support networks or self-care resources?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best strategies for quitting or further reducing rare tobacco and alcohol use for diabetic women in the Luo community of Kisumu?\\",\\n  \\"How do local Anglican Christian beliefs in the Luo community of Kisumu influence attitudes toward using traditional herbal medicine versus prescribed diabetes treatment?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find vegan-friendly diabetes nutrition workshops or resources specific to urban Kisumu?\\",\\n  \\"How might seasonal farming routines in Kisumu affect blood sugar levels and motivation for regular exercise among young female farmers?\\",\\n  \\"What services do local clinics in Kisumu offer for ongoing diabetes management for those making lifestyle changes with limited family support?\\",\\n  \\"Are there Luo cultural practices or family traditions in Kisumu that help individuals with diabetes stay motivated and manage discouragement?\\",\\n  \\"How does easy access to healthy foods in urban Kisumu translate into practical meal planning for a vegan with type 2 diabetes needing to stay energized?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Alright, I’m Akinyi Odongo, a woman living with type 2 diabetes. I try my best on the farm and with my animals, but honestly, sometimes the energy just disappears right out of me. I smoke and drink, which I know isn’t great, and I only get active about once or twice a week. I know I go to the local clinic when things get rough, but I haven’t really figured out which foods out here won’t make my blood sugar go wild. I need to keep working strong, you know? But sometimes it feels so confusing.", "selected_profile_info": ["city_town", "name", "gender", "occupation", "hobbies", "health_conditions", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
