nd of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">766f1a96-3cc2-4607-864b-27174bed4b66</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	One day, I had a big fishing trip planned, but I woke up feeling really tired and my head was pounding. I thought to myself, 'I'll just take a few painkillers and be fine.' But as the day went on, I realized I was getting even more tired and my head was still pounding. I ended up having to cancel the trip, which was a big disappointment. I felt like I'd let myself and my clients down. I didn't realize at the time that my health was a big part of the problem.\n\nAfter that, I decided to visit the local health clinic to see what was going on. The nurse practitioner was very nice and listened to my concerns. She explained that my diet and lifestyle were contributing to my fatigue and headaches. She recommended that I start eating more fruits and vegetables, drinking plenty of water, and cutting back on sugary foods and drinks. She also suggested that I try to get at least 7-8 hours of sleep each night. I was a bit resistant at first, but she made it seem like it wouldn't be that hard to make these changes. She even gave me some tips on how to make healthy meals on a budget.\n\nAt first, it was tough to adjust to my new routine. I missed my sugary snacks and soda, and I didn't feel like cooking healthy meals. But I was determined to make it work because I had a big fishing trip coming up and I wanted to be in top shape. I started small, making a few healthy changes each day. I began by drinking more water and eating more fruits and vegetables. I also started exercising more regularly. It wasn't easy, but I was determined to see it through. And to my surprise, I started feeling better and better. My energy levels increased, and my headaches disappeared.\n\nThe big fishing trip came and went, and I felt like I'd aced it. I had plenty of energy, and my body felt strong and capable. I even got some new clients, which was a big bonus. I realized that taking care of my health was the best investment I could make in myself. I felt proud of myself for making these changes and for taking control of my health. I knew that I could continue to make improvements and that I had the power to 