an in a long skirt and headscarf, sitting on a low wooden stool inside a simple rural shop, her posture tired as she looks towards a dusty unswept corner; warm morning light filters through a patterned curtain, showing shelves with basic goods and bread, subtle worry on her face.", "Medium shot: Nurse Janet, a middle-aged woman in a crisp blue clinic uniform, stands next to Wanjiku Mwangi at an open shop doorway. Nurse Janet gestures encouragingly with one hand, while Wanjiku faces her with arms mildly crossed, wearing an uncertain smile; dry earth and a few green pots are outside, with both women naturally caught mid-conversation.", "A candid, wide shot of Wanjiku Mwangi stretching sideways with a broomstick in her hands in her small shaded courtyard; her body tilts as she grimaces a little, while Mama Njeri, a neighbour woman, stands in the background near a fence, watching and chuckling, chickens wander near Wanjiku’s feet, and laundry hangs on a line.", "A bright, medium shot of Wanjiku Mwangi standing in her market stall, smiling as she sweeps the floor; large colourful sacks and baskets of farm goods surround her. Wanjiku now stands tall, relaxed shoulders, with a happy, energetic expression. One customer pausing and smiling back in the edge of the frame. Dappled sunlight through simple iron roofing."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 13.32310938835144, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some traditional Kikuyu recipes from Murangâ€™a county that are suitable for someone with type 2 diabetes and are lactose-free?\\",\\n  \\"How can a 65-year-old female business owner in rural Murangâ€™a, Kenya, easily incorporate physical activity into her daily routine when she has 0 days of exercise per week?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find support groups or community programs in Murangâ€™a for older adults managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What are some healthy, local Kenyan food options that are lactose-free and easily available in rural Murangâ€™a markets?\\",\\n  \\"Are there Baptist churches or faith-based wellness groups in Murangâ€™a that offer health advice or lifestyle support for elderly women with diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How does weekly tobacco use and high alcohol consumption impact blood sugar control in elderly Kikuyu women with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What are effective strategies for reducing alcohol consumption among older women in rural Kenya who are used to high frequency social drinking?\\",\\n  \\"Which local herbal or traditional medicines used by the Kikuyu in Murangâ€™a are considered safe or unsafe when combined with insulin and metformin for diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"How can storytelling be used as a wellness activity or as a support tool in managing chronic illnesses among elderly women in rural Kikuyu communities?\\",\\n  \\"What is the frequency and quality of diabetes care services at local healthcare clinics or hospitals in Murangâ€™a rural area?\\",\\n  \\"What cultural beliefs in rural Kikuyu communities of Murangâ€™a may affect the management of diabetes for elderly businesswomen?\\",\\n  \\"Are there examples of lactose-free meal plans specifically designed for older Kenyan women with diabetes who have easy access to healthy, local foods?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "The most relevant parts of my profile are: I am Wanjiku Mwangi, a 65+ year old woman who owns a small business in a rural community. I have type 2 diabetes, eat halal, smoke sometimes, and visit the clinic regularly. I’m close to my friends, love telling stories, and want simple ideas to eat well and move more. I have no gym, do not know many home exercises, and sometimes do not see how my health links to my work.", "selected_profile_info": ["city_town", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "occupation", "hobbies", "health_conditions", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "diet_restrict