f82a72ed-b1cd-44bf-9fcf-a70a349e49ca	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b818-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Migori</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Christianity (Lutheran)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Mark Otieno</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Male</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">65+</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Fish trader</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Farming and animal keeping</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No Restrictions</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">f82a72ed-b1cd-44bf-9fcf-a70a349e49ca</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Last week, I was trying to carry a big bucket of fresh fish from the market back to my stall, thinking that was enough exercise for the day. But halfway through, my legs felt weak and my sugar was shaky. I didn’t understand why that happened—I thought as a fish trader moving around all day, I was staying active enough. To make matters worse, after dinner, I often sat outside socializing with friends and ended up snacking late into the night. Didn’t that always happen? I couldn’t see how this was harming my health or my work. So when my small task of selling all the fish quickly failed because I felt tired and slow, I shrugged it off, thinking it was just how things go.\n\nThen I visited the local health clinic in Migori for my regular check-up, and the nurse spoke to me about how to keep active without a gym. She told me that simple things like walking briskly around the market, carrying fish in smaller loads but more frequently, or even doing some squats and stretches at home using my own body weight could help. She also talked about how eating dinner earlier, like around 7 pm, and avoiding late-night snacks would stop my sugar from spiking at night. At first, I was skeptical—how different could this be from my usual ways? But her advice was clear, easy to understand, and suited to my work and home life, so I thought, maybe I could give it a try.\n\nI started waking up a bit earlier to walk around my farm before going to market, and I tried stretching while waiting for customers. But sticking to eating earlier was hard—sometimes after chatting with my family or friends, the old habit of snacking crept back in. A few nights I gave in and ate sweets or fried snacks because it felt natural. Still, I remembered the nurse’s words and that bigger task ahead: the upcoming fish delivery I must prepare for next week. That gave me a reason to keep going, even when it wasn’t easy to change lifelong habits overnight.\n\nSlowly, I noticed I was less tired at the market, and my legs didn’t feel so weak carrying fish. I managed to finish that big delivery with more energy than before, and even my blood sugar numbers were a bit steadier when I checked at the clinic. Now I’m not saying I’ve got everything perfect, but I’m more open to finding better ways to move and manage my meals. After all, if I can keep doing the work I love and be around my family longer, that’s a life worth the change, don’t you think?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f82a72ed-b1cd-44bf-9fcf-a70a349e49ca_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f82a72ed-b1cd-44bf-9fcf-a70a349e49ca_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f82a72ed-b1cd-44bf-9fcf-a70a349e49ca_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f82a72ed-b1cd-44bf-9fcf-a70a349e49ca_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f82a72ed-b1cd-44bf-9fcf-a70a349e49ca_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f82a72ed-b1cd-44bf-9fcf-a70a349e49ca_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f82a72ed-b1cd-44bf-9fcf-a70a349e49ca_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f82a72ed-b1cd-44bf-9fcf-a70a349e49ca_3.mp3}	I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?	exercise	male	consistency	2026-03-23 13:20:00.268055+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "gpt-4.1-mini", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Owiti Odhiambo is a 18-24 year old, \\nCulture: Luo male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Lecturer, lives in a Rural (small community or countryside) in Siaya. Disability: he has none. Religion: Christianity (other). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Ohangla dancing. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: None. Diet restrictions: Vegetarian. Smoking: Yes. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 3-4 days. Support network: Healthcare provider or counsellor. Health goals: How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?. his food access Limited access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Owiti Odhiambo and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in English that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken English, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in English.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- Al