n in Johannesburg. He’s interacting with the chef, X, a man in his 30s wearing a chef’s hat and apron. The kitchen is stainless steel and well-lit. Nariyuki’s posture is upright and energetic. Nariyuki Takahashi looks happy and content."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 83.51873853267767, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some vegan-friendly traditional Hausa dishes available in urban Kano, Nigeria, that are suitable for someone with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can male Hausa merchants in Kano incorporate physical activity into their daily work routine to better manage high blood sugar?\\",\\n  \\"What support groups or family-centered diabetes management programs are available in Kano for Muslims aged 45â€“54?\\",\\n  \\"What strategies have other Hausa Muslims in Kano used to reduce tobacco smoking while managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local healthcare clinics in urban Kano that offer culturally sensitive advice for vegan diabetics?\\",\\n  \\"How does regular exercise influence blood sugar levels specifically for men in their late 40s to early 50s with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Which social activities with family or friends in Kano are both culturally enjoyable and conducive to staying physically active on a vegan diet?\\",\\n  \\"Are there storytelling or social clubs in urban Kano where adults with diabetes can connect and share their experiences?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best ways for Hausa men with easy access to healthy foods in urban areas to overcome feelings of tiredness or discouragement in diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"Can lifestyle changes alone, such as increased exercise and vegan diet, help reduce reliance on insulin or oral medication for type 2 diabetics who are regular tobacco users?\\",\\n  \\"How does observing Islamic practices (like fasting during Ramadan) affect blood sugar control in middle-aged male vegans with type 