ed196584-0542-40ff-8e77-dce478550bc5	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b817-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kiambu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Islam</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Wanjiku Mwangi</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Female</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">18-24</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Suburban (near city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Banker</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Storytelling</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">1-2 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Close friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">ed196584-0542-40ff-8e77-dce478550bc5</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Wanjiku, and I live in Soweto, you know? It’s not fancy here, not like those houses with big fences and lots of cars. Most of us live in these little rondavels, the ones with the corrugated iron roofs. My job is at the spaza shop – you know, the little shop that sells everything from sugar to potatoes. I help Mama sell, counting the money and making sure the shelves are full. Sometimes, I get so busy, I forget to think about how much I’m eating. I love pap and beans for breakfast, and maybe some sad-looking vegetables if I’m lucky. Lunch is usually a loaf of bread and some cheese. It’s easy, it’s quick, and it keeps me going. But sometimes, my tummy aches, and I don’t know why.  Do you think it’s because I’m not eating properly? It’s just… hard to think about healthy food when you're trying to make enough money, isn’t it?\n\nYesterday, I had to help load a truck full of oranges. It was a really big job, and I was sweating like crazy. I was so focused on getting all the oranges in the truck, I completely forgot to drink water! By lunchtime, my head was spinning, and I felt really, really tired. Mama said I wasn’t working properly, and that I needed to take care of myself.  She told me, ‘Wanjiku, you can’t carry heavy loads if your body is tired.’ But honestly, I just wanted to finish the job and go home.  It felt like a big test, you know? Like I had to prove I could do everything, even if it meant ignoring my own body. It was a bit embarrassing, I’ll admit.\n\nThe nurse at the clinic, Nurse Zola, she was very nice. She asked me about my diet and how much I was drinking. She explained that my body needs good food to give me energy, especially when I’m working hard. She showed me pictures of fruits and vegetables – bright red tomatoes, green spinach, and juicy oranges. She said I could still have my pap and beans, but maybe add a bit more of those healthy things. She gave me a little booklet with recipes, easy ones, using things we can get at the spaza shop. It said things like ‘add some chopped onions to your pap’ and ‘make a salad with lettuce and tomatoes.’ It sounded a bit complicated, to be honest. I felt a little confused, like maybe I couldn’t do it.  I asked her, ‘But what if I don’t have money for all those fancy vegetables?’\n\nI tried making a salad with lettuce and tomatoes – it was a bit messy, and I dropped a few tomatoes! But it tasted good, really good. I started adding a little bit of spinach to my pap too. It didn’t change the taste much, but it made me feel a little bit better.  Then, the big delivery arrived – a shipment of fresh fruit for the spaza shop.  I helped unpack it, and I even ate a few mangoes. It felt good to take care of myself, and I felt stronger when I was loading the truck later that day.  It wasn’t easy, but I’m starting to see that eating healthy doesn’t have to be expensive or complicated.  It just takes a little bit of effort, and maybe a little help from Nurse Zola.  I think I’m finally starting to understand that my body is important, and I need to treat it well.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ed196584-0542-40ff-8e77-dce478550bc5_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ed196584-0542-40ff-8e77-dce478550bc5_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ed196584-0542-40ff-8e77-dce478550bc5_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ed196584-0542-40ff-8e77-dce478550bc5_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ed196584-0542-40ff-8e77-dce478550bc5_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ed196584-0542-40ff-8e77-dce478550bc5_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ed196584-0542-40ff-8e77-dce478550bc5_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ed196584-0542-40ff-8e77-dce478550bc5_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still 