oom. Nurse Zola is pointing to a colorful booklet filled with pictures of fruits and vegetables. Wanjiku looks slightly hesitant and a little unsure, her hands clasped together. Soft, diffused lighting, emphasizing the warmth of the interaction.  A concerned expression, tilted head, listening intently.", "Wanjiku, smiling broadly, holding a ripe mango in her hand. She’s standing in front of the spaza shop, surrounded by a display of fresh fruit. The sunlight is streaming through the window, illuminating her face. A joyful expression, eyes sparkling, a relaxed posture, a gentle smile."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 10.488683498822725, "task_parent_id": "261b7278-316b-4481-992a-8ff645a4ef64", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some Kikuyu-inspired gluten-free meals available in suburban Kiambu that are suitable for a young Muslim woman with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there social gathering spots near urban Kiambu where I can find healthy, low-sugar drinks for weekly meet-ups with friends?\\",\\n  \\"Which restaurants or cafes in Kiambu offer gluten-free menu options suitable for someone managing diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How do young female bankers in suburban Kenyan areas balance shift schedules with regular insulin management and dietary restrictions?\\",\\n  \\"What gluten-free snack options can I buy at supermarkets or local markets near Kiambu that won't spike my blood sugar?\\",\\n  \\"How can I make traditional Kikuyu dishes diabetes-friendly while keeping them gluten-free for weekend family gatherings?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any storytelling community groups or social events in or near Kiambu that accommodate dietary needs and promote healthy eating for young adults?\\",\\n  \\"What are the most popular physical activities for women in their early 20s living in suburban Kiambu, given my schedule only allows 1-2 days a week?\\",\\n  \\"Which local support groups or diabetes network