 you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Dairy farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Retired</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Farming and Gardening</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">1-2 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Gluten-Free</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">c91a737c-6488-477a-b738-ce520bea2964</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gymâ€”what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Hayi bo, life as a pensioner, it's not always sunshine and roses, you know? I'm Wanja Mwangi, and most days, I just want a nice, warm plate of chakalaka and pap. It fills you up, it tastes good, and it reminds me of my mama’s cooking. But lately, I’ve been feeling…slow. I promised my grandson, Thabo, I’d knit him a new jersey for the school play – a bright blue one with a lion on it, his favourite! But my hands, they just ache, and I keep dropping stitches. Honestly, it’s like they have a mind of their own. I just couldn’t get it right, the wool kept slipping, and I had to give up. What’s a grandma to do when she can’t even knit a simple jersey?\n\nOld Man Dlamini, our neighbour, he saw me looking frustrated. He said, ‘Wanja, you need to go see Sister Noma at the clinic. She’s a good woman, and she knows about these things.’ I was a bit hesitant, you see. Clinics…they always seem to have long queues and a lot of waiting. But Thabo's play was getting closer, and I really wanted to finish that jersey. So, I went. Sister Noma, she was very kind. She checked my blood pressure – said it was a little high – and asked about my food. She said, ‘Wanja, all that pap and chakalaka is lovely, but we need to add some greens, some beans, and less salt. And maybe swap some of the white pap for brown rice, it keeps you going longer.’ She gave me a little booklet with pictures of affordable, healthy foods and even showed me how to make a delicious bean stew with vegetables. It didn’t sound so bad, actually.\n\nTrying to change what you’ve eaten for seventy years, it’s not easy, let me tell you! The first few days, I missed my usual big plate of pap terribly. I tried the bean stew, but I kept adding a little extra salt, just a pinch, you understand? And then, I ran out of sugar for my tea! Oh, it was a disaster. I nearly went back to my old ways. But Thabo kept asking about his jersey, and the thought of him looking disappointed…that kept me going. I went back to the market and bought some spinach and carrots, even though they weren’t on my usual shopping list. I reminded myself, 'Just a little bit of green won’t hurt, will it?'\n\nSlowly, slowly, things started to get better. I started enjoying the bean stew, especially with a bit of pepper. I found a cheaper shop that sold brown rice, and it really did keep me fuller for longer. My hands still ached sometimes, but not as much. And guess what? I finished Thabo’s jersey! A beautiful bright blue jersey with a magnificent lion. When he put it on, his face lit up like a Christmas tree. He looked so proud, and so was I. Now, Sister Noma also mentioned something about walking every morning, and maybe cutting down on my cigarettes. Maybe… just maybe… I’ll give that a try too. After all, if I can learn to enjoy spinach, anything is possible, neh?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c91a737c-6488-477a-b738-ce520bea2964_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c91a737c-6488-477a-b738-ce520bea2964_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c91a737c-6488-477a-b738-ce520bea2964_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c91a737c-6488-477a-b738-ce520bea2964_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c91a737c-6488-477a-b738-ce520bea2964_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c91a737c-6488-477a-b738-ce520bea2964_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c91a737c-6488-477a-b738-ce520bea2964_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c91a737c-6488-477a-b738-ce520bea2964_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	female	control	2026-03-23 13:10:44.892923+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gemma-3-27b-it", "prompt": "Ou