  <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">1-2 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Lactose-free</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">21f5164b-c93a-4744-9a09-702b0725643c</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Nia, and I live out here near Murang’a, with my mama and my little brother, Kamau. We have a small dairy farm – it’s not fancy, you know? Just a few cows, and we sell the milk at the market. Most days, I wake up early, before the sun even thinks about coming up. Mama makes us chai – that’s like, super strong tea – and then it’s straight to the cows. I usually have a bit of maize porridge for breakfast, and sometimes a banana if we have any.  Sometimes, I’ll grab a few roasted peanuts from the bag, just to give me a little energy before milking.  It’s a good job, but sometimes, I feel a bit tired, like my legs are heavy.  Do you ever feel that way, like you just can’t seem to get going?\n\nYesterday, I was helping Papa fix the fence – a really long, tricky one. He needed me to hold the wire taut, but I was so sleepy, I just kept yawning. I told him I was okay, but really, I was just slowing him down.  The wire snapped, and we had to start all over again! Papa was a little cross, and I felt bad. It wasn’t my fault exactly, but I knew if I’d been more alert, we could have finished it quicker. It’s important to be strong for Papa, you know?  He works so hard.  I just wanted a little biscuit, a nice sweet one, to give me a bit of a boost. But Mama said no – ‘Nia, you need to eat proper food, not just sweets!’\n\nToday, I went to the clinic, the one in town. Nurse Njeri checked my sugar. She said it was a bit high. She told me I need to be careful about what I eat, especially the sugary things. She said I could have a little bit of fruit, like mangoes or oranges, and maybe some plain yoghurt.  She also said I need to drink lots of water, not just tea. It sounded a bit complicated, but she wrote down some things on a paper. She said I need to talk to Mama about making sure there's not too much sugar in my porridge. I wasn’t sure if I could do it, it seemed like a lot of changing. But she said, ‘Little by little, Nia, little by little.’\n\nToday, I made my porridge with less sugar than usual. Mama made a big bowl of oranges for lunch, and I ate them all!  I even drank a whole bottle of water.  Papa noticed I was feeling better and said, ‘You’re moving like a cheetah, Nia!’.  The fence is still being fixed, and this time, I helped Papa without yawning.  I felt strong and ready, and we finished it in just a few hours. It feels good to be helping, and to feel good doing it.  I’m going to try to eat a little bit healthier every day, you know? Maybe tomorrow, I'll ask Mama to make a nice, creamy yoghurt with some fruit. It’s a good feeling, isn’t it, when you feel strong and happy?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/21f5164b-c93a-4744-9a09-702b0725643c_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/21f5164b-c93a-4744-9a09-702b0725643c_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/21f5164b-c93a-4744-9a09-702b0725643c_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/21f5164b-c93a-4744-9a09-702b0725643c_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/21f5164b-c93a-4744-9a09-702b0725643c_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/21f5164b-c93a-4744-9a09-702b0725643c_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/21f5164b-c93a-4744-9a09-702b0725643c_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/21f5164b-c93a-4744-9a09-702b0725643c_3.mp3}	I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?	diet	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:10:43.510391+00	{"label": "GOOD", "model": "gemma-3-4b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Wanjiku Mwangi is a 35-44 year old, \\nCulture: Kikuyu female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Business owner, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Murang'a. Disability: she has none. Religion: Islam. Daily routine: Workin