              <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Trader</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Storytelling</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Anxiety or depression</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">b02783a9-91d2-4950-bc9b-251316a9e738</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Hai, my name is Amina Yusuf, and life as a trader in Kano market is…busy, wallahi! Every day is a hustle. I sell beautiful fabrics, Ankara and lace, you know? Bright colours, good quality. But let me tell you, thinking about what to eat is always last on my mind. Usually, it’s whatever’s quickest – maybe some masa with a little stew, or tuwo shinkafa with miyan kuka. Sometimes, if I’m lucky, some grilled fish. It fills the belly, right? Just last week, I had a big order to prepare - a wedding set! I promised the customer it would be ready on Wednesday. But I felt so tired, so sluggish, I kept making mistakes with the measurements. I had to redo a whole piece of lace! Honestly, I just thought it was stress. What does eating have to do with sewing, anyway?\n\nMy friend, Fatima, she noticed I wasn’t myself. She said I looked tired and worried about my work. She practically dragged me to the local clinic. The nurse, a kind woman named Hauwa, listened to me complain about the tiredness and the messed-up wedding order. She didn’t laugh when I said I didn’t see what food had to do with it! Hauwa explained about the sugar in my blood, about diabetes, and how it can make you feel weak and affect your concentration. She said I need to eat more vegetables, more beans, and less of the sugary things. 'Amina,' she said, 'you can still enjoy your masa and tuwo, but maybe with a bigger portion of vegetables and a smaller portion of the stew. And try to walk for at least thirty minutes most days.' It sounded…hard. But then I remembered that big order for Alhaji Ibrahim's daughter. I *had* to get it right this time.\n\nTrying to change things was…difficult, I won’t lie. I’m used to a certain way of eating, you see? The first day, I tried to make a big plate of vegetables with my tuwo. My neighbour, Auntie Aisha, came over for tea and she looked at my plate like I was eating grass! 'Amina, are you alright?' she asked, worried. I almost gave up and went back to my usual portion of stew. But then I thought about the beautiful silk Alhaji Ibrahim wanted, and how much money I would make if I didn't mess it up. So, I kept eating my vegetables, even though it felt strange. And the walking? My feet were aching! But I walked to the market and back, slowly, slowly. It wasn't easy, but I told myself, 'Just for the work, Amina, just for the work.'\n\nSlowly, things started to change. I started adding more okra and spinach to my soups, and I swapped white rice for brown rice sometimes. I even started enjoying it! The tiredness wasn't as bad, and I could concentrate on my sewing for longer. When I finally finished Alhaji Ibrahim’s wedding set, it was perfect, wallahi! Every stitch was neat, every piece of lace was measured exactly right. He was so pleased, he gave me a generous tip. And you know what? I felt proud, not just of the money, but of myself. Hauwa was right. Eating better really did help. Now, I'm thinking maybe I should try to walk a little faster, and maybe even add some fruit to my breakfast. It seems like taking care of myself isn't just about feeling good, it’s about being able to do everything I want to do, and do it well.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b02783a9-91d2-4950-bc9b-251316a9e738_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b02783a9-91d2-4950-bc9b-251316a9e738_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b02783a9-91d2-4950-bc9b-251316a9e738_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b02783a9-91d2-4950-bc9b-251316a9e738_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b02783a9-91d2-4950-bc9b-251316a9e738_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b02783a9-91d2-4950-bc9b-251316a9e738_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b02783a9-91d2-4950-bc9b-251316a9e738_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b02783a9-91d2-4950-bc9b-251316a9e738_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on 