 is fluorescent and slightly harsh.", "Amina Yusuf is preparing a meal in her modest kitchen. She is stirring a pot of soup, with a large portion of spinach and okra visible. Her neighbour, Auntie Aisha, is standing nearby, looking at the pot with a concerned expression. The kitchen is simple, with basic cooking utensils. The lighting is warm and natural, coming from a window.", "Amina Yusuf, smiling brightly, is carefully examining a beautifully finished wedding dress made of silk and lace. She is standing in her workshop, surrounded by fabrics and sewing equipment. Alhaji Ibrahim is standing in the background, looking pleased. The scene is well-lit and vibrant, showcasing the intricate details of the dress. Amina Yusuf."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 83.51873853267767, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are popular physical activity options for women aged 35-44 in urban Kano, Nigeria, that fit my busy work schedule as a trader?\\",\\n  \\"Are there culturally appropriate, lactose-free Nigerian or Hausa meal plans suitable for managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How does living alone in a Kano city environment impact stress management and mental health for Muslim women my age?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best places or groups in Kano for women who enjoy storytelling and socializing to connect and reduce isolation?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any Hausa cultural traditions or community events in Kano that promote physical activity for adult women?\\",\\n  \\"What is the recommended exercise routine for a 40-year-old Muslim woman with anxiety and type 2 diabetes in Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"How can I manage diabetes and anxiety while balancing the demands of running a trading business in Kano city?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find support groups for women dealing with diabetes and mental health challenges in northern Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"What local health clinics or hospitals in urban Kano 