5723de5f-8ab0-4e64-8556-b990620e2eae	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b817-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kiambu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Christianity (other)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Wanjiku Mwangi</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Female</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">45-54</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Suburban (near city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Civil servant</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Farming and Gardening</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5723de5f-8ab0-4e64-8556-b990620e2eae</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I like to snackâ€”what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Ai, life, isn’t it something? I’m Wanjiku, and I work for the government, mostly filing things and making sure the offices run smoothly. It’s steady work, but these days, even walking to the bus stop feels like climbing a mountain. I love my chai with milk and a couple of biscuits in the morning, and a hearty lunch of ugali and fish. Sometimes, I sneak a sweet soda too, just to give me a boost. Last week, my boss asked me to take the minutes at a big meeting with people from Nairobi, a really important job! But halfway through writing, my head started swimming, my hands went shaky, and I just…froze. Couldn't write another word. Everyone stared. It was embarrassing, honestly. My colleague, Njeri, had to finish for me. I just thought I was tired, you know? A bit stressed.\n\nAfter that meeting, Njeri took me aside. She's a good woman, Njeri. She told me I should go to the clinic, said I looked unwell. I resisted a little, ‘It’s just tiredness,’ I said. But she insisted, and I went. The nurse, a kind woman named Mama Zawadi, checked my sugar and my pressure. ‘Wanjiku,’ she said, looking serious, ‘your sugar is high, and so is your blood pressure. You have diabetes and hypertension.’ I knew about those things, of course, everyone does, but I never thought…me? She explained, very gently, that the sugary drinks and biscuits, even the soda, were making things worse. She said I could still enjoy my ugali and fish, but smaller portions, and to add lots of greens. And she showed me a handful of groundnuts, saying those are good for a snack, but not too many. ‘And the cigarettes, Wanjiku,’ she said, ‘and the little bit of beer with your friends on weekends? Those need to go, or at least be cut way back.’ It felt like a lot to take in, but Mama Zawadi explained it all so clearly. She said getting my health in order would help me do my job better.\n\nTrying to change things has been…difficult. I started taking the medicine Mama Zawadi prescribed, and I’m trying to eat more sukuma wiki with my ugali. But those biscuits in the morning… they call to me! And yesterday, my friend Muthoni invited me over for tea, and she had those lovely mandazis. I told myself just one wouldn’t hurt, but then I had two. My sugar felt a little high later, and I felt sluggish. I sighed. It's hard to break old habits, isn’t it? But that big meeting is coming up next month, and I *need* to be able to focus. I don’t want to let my boss down again. So, I reminded myself that I need to be strong and keep trying. I even started walking a little further to the bus stop each day, just to get some exercise.\n\nIt’s been a few weeks now, and I’m starting to feel…better. I still have my chai, but I’ve swapped the biscuits for a small handful of groundnuts. And I've started carrying carrot sticks in my bag for a snack. It's not the same as a soda, but it keeps me going. I've cut down on the cigarettes, too, just having a few a day instead of a pack. The biggest surprise? I actually have more energy! Last week, the big meeting came, and I was asked to take the minutes again. This time, I didn’t freeze. I wrote everything down, clear as day, and even offered to help with the follow-up work. My boss was impressed! Mama Zawadi was right – taking care of my health *does* help me do my job better. Now, I'm thinking maybe I'll ask her about some of those Kikuyu herbs she mentioned, just to see if they can help me feel even stronger. Maybe this is just the beginning.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5723de5f-8ab0-4e64-8556-b990620e2eae_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5723de5f-8ab0-4e64-8556-b990620e2eae_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5723de5f-8ab0-4e64-8556-b990620e2eae_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5723de5f-8ab0-4e64-8556-b990620e2eae_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5723de5f