istant market vendors calling, light wind rustling leaves, low hum of a nearby generator, Wanjiku", "Mrs. Njeri speaks gently to Wanjiku, voice clear and warm, saying 'Just walk for 10 minutes,' with a soft pause, Wanjiku replies softly, 'But I have so much to do,' breathing slightly deeper, background sound of a clock ticking, soft music from a radio in the background, Mrs. Njeri and Wanjiku", "Wanjiku walks slowly, breathing in short bursts, voice low and tired, saying 'I walked only 5 minutes,' with a pause, then a soft sigh, background sound of customers chatting, shop bell ringing, distant children playing, Wanjiku", "Wanjiku walks with her cousin, voice steady and confident, saying 'I feel better now,' with a warm smile in tone, background sound of birds chirping, light wind, distant laughter, clear and natural, Wanjiku and her cousin"], "image_prompts": ["Wanjiku standing in front of her small shop in the early morning light, holding a basket of maize and beans, her feet slightly tired, one hand on her waist as if holding herself up, the shop sign visible with faded paint, dusty ground with small stones, morning sun casting long shadows, texture of concrete and mud floor, soft golden light, Wanjiku", "Wanjiku sitting on a plastic chair in a clinic waiting room, her hands resting on her lap, looking at a clipboard with a small glucose test strip in front of her, a nurse named Mrs. Njeri standing nearby, both wearing simple white clothes, soft morning light through a window, a small poster of a walking woman on the wall, natural background with plants and a small table, Wanjiku and Mrs. Njeri", "Wanjiku walking slowly around her shop after closing, her sister nearby on a mat, both in simple clothes, one hand on a small basket, the shop crowded with customers, sunlight filtering through the open door, dust in the air, her posture slumped slightly, looking tired but determined, Wanjiku and her sister", "Wanjiku walking with her cousin in the afternoon, both in bright kanga clothes, the path leading to a village hall, sunlight warm and soft, green trees on both sides, their feet on a dusty path, Wanjiku smiling slightly, her hands in her pockets, looking ahead with confidence, Wanjiku"], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 62.298312187194824, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are the best exercise routines for women aged 18-24 with type 2 diabetes living in suburban areas near Murangâ€™a, Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"How can I follow a kosher diet using locally available healthy foods in Murangâ€™a as a Kikuyu business owner?\\",\\n  \\"What traditional Kikuyu storytelling events or groups exist near Murangâ€™a for young women interested in connecting with their culture?\\",\\n  \\"Are there cultural or community support groups for young Christian Kikuyu women with type 2 diabetes near Murangâ€™a?\\",\\n  \\"Which types of physical activities commonly done in Murangâ€™a suburban areas are safe and effective for women managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How do I balance running a small business with regular physical activity and diabetes management in Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"What recent guidelines do local healthcare providers in Murangâ€™a recommend for exercise frequency and duration for young adults with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What challenges might a young female business owner face in accessing diabetes care in Murangâ€™a, and what solutions exist locally?\\",\\n  \\"Are there social or family gatherings in Kikuyu culture that encourage healthy eating or active lifestyles for young women?\\",\\n  \\"Is it possible to get kosher foods easily in Murangâ€™a, and which markets are best for sourcing them?\\",\\n  \\"How does the suburban environment near Murangâ€™a influence access to exercise facilities or walking paths for young adults?\\",\\n  \\"What resources or healthcare services are available locally to support mental health and social c