upport network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">203980fa-70e9-40c9-a22b-94cedfefe594</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	The sun beats down hard on Kisumu, same as always. My days are pretty simple – wake up, a quick cup of chai, then off to the office. I mostly work with the community, helping people understand how to get support for their businesses. Lunch is usually ugali with some beans, sometimes a bit of sukuma wiki if I’m feeling fancy. Honestly, I don’t really think much about my health, not like that. Work is busy, and there's always something needing attention. Last week, I was supposed to deliver a report to the council – a really important one about getting more resources for the local market. I’d planned to finish it before noon, but I got caught up helping a farmer fix his tractor, and by the time I got back, I was exhausted and the report was half-finished. It was a mess, and I had to rush, and it just wasn't good enough.\n\nI went to the Aga Khan Hospital clinic, like I should have. Dr. Okello, he’s a good man, listened to my story and took a look at my blood pressure. He said my diet and lack of regular exercise were probably the main reason I felt so drained. He didn't lecture me or anything, just explained that too much ugali and not enough fresh vegetables, combined with sitting at my desk all day, was taking a toll. He gave me a simple list – smaller portions of ugali, more greens, and a walk for at least 30 minutes, three times a week. He also said I needed to talk to my doctor about my insulin, just to make sure it was still right for me. It seemed easy enough, but honestly, it felt a little overwhelming. I've always just done things my way, and changing that felt…hard.\n\nI tried to follow his advice, I really did. I started taking a walk after lunch, but then I’d get distracted by a problem at the office and forget. And the ugali… well, it's just so comforting! I tried to make it smaller, but then I’d just end up eating more beans. Yesterday, I was helping a group of women set up a stall at the market, and I completely forgot about my walk. By the time I remembered, it was getting dark. I felt a bit frustrated, like I was failing. It’s not easy to change habits, especially when you're used to doing things a certain way. But then I remembered the bigger task – presenting the report to the council. I couldn’t let myself fail at that, not after all the work I’d put in.\n\nThis week, I’ve been sticking to the plan. The walks are becoming easier, and I actually feel a bit more energetic. I even managed to make a small portion of ugali, and it tasted just as good as the big one! The report went really well at the council meeting – they were impressed with the data, and they agreed to look into getting more funding for the market. I feel…lighter, somehow. Not just physically, but mentally too. It’s not about being perfect, it’s about taking small steps, one day at a time. Maybe Dr. Okello was right. Maybe taking care of myself is the best way to help everyone else, too. I’m even thinking about joining that walking group they have at the park – it might be good to have some company.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/203980fa-70e9-40c9-a22b-94cedfefe594_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/203980fa-70e9-40c9-a22b-94cedfefe594_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/203980fa-70e9-40c9-a22b-94cedfefe594_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/203980fa-70e9-40c9-a22b-94cedfefe594_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/203980fa-70e9-40c9-a22b-94cedfefe594_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/203980fa-70e9-40c9-a22b-94cedfefe594_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/203980fa-70e9-40c9-a22b-94cedfefe594_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/203980fa-70e9-40c9-a22b-94cedfefe594_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I s