 would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Fisher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Ohangla dancing</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine, Not yet started any treatment</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">ec9ac0e5-7140-4ab9-9dae-a475af31de29</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	The lake… it always calls to me. Being a fisherwoman, it's in my blood, you know? My grandmother, my mother, now me. We wake before the sun, mend the nets, and head out. But lately, everything feels… heavy. Not just the nets. I love a good snack while I’m working – usually mandazi and a sweet tea. Keeps me going, I tell myself. Yesterday, I was supposed to deliver a big catch to Mama Njeri at the market, a good one that would earn us enough for school fees. But halfway there, my legs started cramping up, a dull ache that just wouldn't go away. Had to rest three times, and by the time I got there, the fish weren’t so fresh anymore. Mama Njeri wasn’t pleased. She said, 'Achieng, you’re usually more reliable. What happened?' I just shrugged. Felt like my body had betrayed me.\n\nI finally went to the clinic, mostly because my mum kept nagging. Nurse Agnes, she’s a good woman, always patient. She checked my sugar, and well… it wasn't good. She explained about the diabetes, how the sweet things I love are actually working against me, making me tired and weak. She didn't scold, just explained, in a way that made sense. 'Achieng,' she said, 'Your body is like a boat. You need the right fuel to keep it running smoothly. Too much sugar is like throwing rocks in the engine.' She told me to swap the mandazi for fruit, maybe a mango or a banana, and to walk for at least thirty minutes each day. Walk! Me, walk when I could be resting? But she said it would help with the cramps and give me more energy for the fishing. She also said, 'Think about that big catch, Achieng. You need your strength for that.'\n\nTrying to change things is harder than I thought. I packed a mango with my tea yesterday, but I still craved that sweet, fluffy mandazi. Ended up eating both! And the walking… Oy! I tried to walk along the shore after mending the nets, but it felt so slow, so pointless. My legs ached, and I kept thinking about how much faster I could be getting things done. I almost gave up, but then I remembered Mama Njeri's face, and the school fees. I *need* to be strong for that next delivery. So, I pushed myself, just a little bit further each day. The first few days were terrible. I felt even more tired, and my legs complained with every step. But I kept reminding myself: school fees. School fees.\n\nIt’s been a few weeks now, and something is changing. I still enjoy my tea, but I'm choosing fruit more often, and surprisingly, I don’t feel as sluggish afterward. The walking… well, I actually look forward to it now. The sunrise over the lake is beautiful, and I feel… lighter, somehow. Stronger. Last week, I delivered an even bigger catch to Mama Njeri, and she smiled, a real smile. 'You’re back, Achieng,' she said. 'That’s my reliable fisherwoman!' I felt a pride I hadn't felt in a while. Nurse Agnes says I’m still managing my sugar, but it's getting better. Maybe… maybe taking care of myself isn’t such a bad thing after all. Maybe this is just the beginning.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ec9ac0e5-7140-4ab9-9dae-a475af31de29_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ec9ac0e5-7140-4ab9-9dae-a475af31de29_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ec9ac0e5-7140-4ab9-9dae-a475af31de29_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ec9ac0e5-7140-4ab9-9dae-a475af31de29_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ec9ac0e5-7140-4ab9-9dae-a475af31de29_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ec9ac0e5-7140-4ab9-9dae-a475af31de29_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ec9ac0e5-7140-4ab9-9dae-a475af31de29_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ec9ac0e5-7140-4ab9-9dae-a475af31de29_3.mp3}	I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?	diet	fema