 in concentration, while Nurse Agnes speaks to her with a kind expression. A medical chart is visible on the desk between them. The lighting is fluorescent, casting a slightly sterile glow. Achieng's body language shows a slight hunch and a hesitant gaze.", "Wide shot of Achieng Odhiambo, 23, walking along the rocky shoreline of Lake Victoria in Homa Bay, Kenya. She is wearing simple clothes and worn sandals. Her posture is slightly hunched, and her face shows a determined but weary expression. She is looking towards the horizon. The lighting is harsh midday sun, creating strong shadows. The background shows the vast expanse of the lake and distant hills.", "Medium shot of Achieng Odhiambo, 24, smiling confidently while delivering a large basket of fish to Mama Njeri, a middle-aged Kenyan woman, at a bustling market in Homa Bay. Achieng is standing tall with a strong posture, her face radiating pride. Mama Njeri is examining the fish with a pleased expression. The lighting is warm and vibrant, capturing the energy of the market. The background shows other vendors and customers."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 83.03575225976797, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are the most recommended types of physical activities for young Luo women with Type 2 diabetes living in urban Homa Bay, Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"How can I safely start an exercise routine as a 22-year-old female fisher in Homa Bay with Type 2 diabetes and high tobacco and alcohol use?\\",\\n  \\"Are there Ohangla dance classes or fitness groups in Homa Bay that are suitable for young adults wanting to manage diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What local Homa Bay resources or clinics offer personalized fitness coaching for diabetic patients, especially working women with busy schedules?\\",\\n  \\"How does daily alcohol and tobacco use impact my diabetes management as a young Luo Baptist woman, and are there culturally accepted ways to reduce these habits in Homa Bay?\\",\\n  \\"Which healthy traditional Luo foods easily available in Homa Bay urban markets can help manage Type 2 diabetes without dietary restrictions?\\",\\n  \\"What exercise guidelines do Kenyan health professionals recommend for female fishers who have not been active and want to control diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community support groups for young women with diabetes in Homa Bay that also address mental health and social activities?\\",\\n  \\"How can my family in Homa Bay support me in making sustainable exercise and lifestyle changes for diabetes control?\\",\\n  \\"Is herbal or traditional medicine commonly used alongside insulin or oral medication for diabetes management in Homa Bay, and is it effective?\\",\\n  \\"What is the best way to balance demanding fishing work with starting regular physical activity, considering the local climate and safety in urban Homa Bay?\\",\\n  \\"Are there faith-based Baptist programs or church initiatives in urban Kenya that support young women in healthy living and diabetes care?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
