r area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Trader</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Storytelling</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">â€” None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No Restrictions</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5cb6b98b-9737-4f38-a66b-943d5f6797b8</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">What kinds of exercises are safe and helpful for someone with diabetes?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	One day, I decided just to walk around the block for exercise, thinking that’s all I needed. After all, walking is easy and free, right? But during a small market event, I felt tired and couldn’t keep up with some customers. I blamed the heat and the long day, but maybe it was because I thought just walking was enough. I didn’t want to slow down, but my body was telling a different story. How was I going to make it through a bigger event next week if I was already struggling now?\n\nI went to the local clinic to talk with the nurse, and she explained patiently that walking is good, no doubt, but mixing other exercises can help my muscles, heart, and blood sugar more. She said things like simple stretches, some light exercises to strengthen my legs and arms, and even a little dance with my community group. It sounded hard at first, but she broke it down so I could do a little every day. I was still thinking, "Is this really necessary?" but her calm voice made me trust her more.\n\nSo I tried adding some new moves to my routine, like stretching before setting up my stall and doing some arm lifts while waiting for customers. It felt strange and tiring at first, and one morning I almost skipped it all because of how stiff I felt. But then I remembered the big market event coming up, where I wanted to sell more and show my community what I could do. That kept me going, even when it was tough to change my ways.\n\nSlowly, my body felt a bit stronger and less heavy when I walked. When the big event arrived, I was able to move around better and even chat happily with more customers without feeling wiped out. I realized this exercise mix was helping me not just for work but also for life. Now, I’m even excited to keep improving, knowing I can take care of myself and still chase my dreams in this lively town.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5cb6b98b-9737-4f38-a66b-943d5f6797b8_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5cb6b98b-9737-4f38-a66b-943d5f6797b8_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5cb6b98b-9737-4f38-a66b-943d