ey persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "crisis_avoidance", "audio_prompts": ["Sounds of busy urban market with chatter and footsteps; Chimamanda Okafor’s breath slightly heavy and pacing slowing as she talks softly about feeling tired while walking; background calls of vendors selling goods; natural street ambiance with occasional distant car noises.", "Quiet clinic room with faint shuffle of papers and distant voices; nurse, a calm female voice, gently explaining exercise advice to Chimamanda Okafor who responds with thoughtful pauses and hesitant words; soft ambient hum from medical equipment in background adding gentle realism.", "Early morning market sounds with birds chirping and slow conversations; Chimamanda Okafor’s voice firming up as she describes her new stretching routine; male customer nearby speaking encouragingly; footsteps and rustling of fabric heard close by.", "Lively market event with many voices and laughter around Chimamanda Okafor; her voice bright and confident sharing her success; customers’ footsteps and calls clearly heard nearby; ambient sounds of busy stalls and intermittent music from a community group in the distance."], "image_prompts": ["Chimamanda Okafor, a young woman trader, walking slowly with a tired expression down an urban market street filled with colorful stalls and busy people; warm midday lighting highlighting the textures of her casual clothing and the rough pavement; candid medium shot showing her slightly hunched posture from fatigue.", "Chimamanda sitting attentively across from a female nurse in a small, bright local clinic room; the nurse is explaining with hand gestures while Chimamanda listens with a mix of curiosity and slight doubt; natural window light softly illuminating the clinical space; medium shot capturing their engaged facial expressions.", "Chimamanda standing beside her market stall early morning, stretching her arms upward with a determined look, while a middle-aged male customer observes kindly from nearby; soft morning light casting long shadows on the urban setting; wide shot showing both people and their surroundings naturally.", "Chimamanda smiling confidently as she moves energetically through a crowded market during a busy event, interacting with customers with open gestures; vibrant colors of fresh produce and fabrics around her; warm afternoon sunlight enhancing the liveliness of the scene; candid medium shot focusing on her joyful expression and active posture."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 3.40064914226532, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some popular low-sugar traditional Hausa foods available in urban Katsina that are suitable for female traders with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Which community or Christian church-based diabetes support groups meet regularly in Katsina city for young adult women?\\",\\n  \\"How can I balance my weekly alcohol consumption with diabetes management as a socially active 18-24 year old living in Katsina?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any exercise classes or fitness groups for women ages 18-24 in Katsina city that focus on diabetes-friendly routines?\\",\\n  \\"What lifestyle tips are recommended for young female traders in urban Northern Nigeria to manage type 2 diabetes while maintaining easy access to healthy foods?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find storytelling or cultural events in Katsina that are welcoming to urban Christian Hausa women?\\",\\n  \\"How does participation in African Independent Churches influence diabetes self-care and community support in Katsina?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best markets or shops in urban Katsina for affordable diabetes-friendly groceries for traders with busy work routines?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local Hausa herbal or traditional remedies in Katsina commonly used by young women for managing type 2 diabetes alongside prescribed medications?\\",\\n  \\"What physical activities are most popular among urban Hausa women in Katsina who exercise 5-7 days a week for diabetes control?\\",\\n  \\"How do other young women in Katsina with type 2 diabetes manage regular healthcare visits around their trading schedules?\\",\\n  \\"What are the cultural perceptions or stigmas about diabetes among Hausa communities in Katsina, especially for young Christian women?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "My name is Chimamanda Okafor, and I’m a young trader 18 years old living in the heart of a buzzing urban town. Every day, I wake early, head to the market, and spend hours selling my goods. My routine is busy, just like many here, and I take my insulin injections regularly because of my diabetes. I don’t know much about how doing different types of exercise might help me, but I do know I need to stay strong for my work and my community group that keeps me going.", "selected_profile_info": ["city_town", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "occupation", "daily_routine", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "tobacco", "physical_activity", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
