would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Sugarcane farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Farming and animal keeping</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Lifestyle changes only (no medication)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">82e6e705-5c1e-4ac7-8254-07a40cd86fa3</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensiveâ€”how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Hayi, man, life is busy, you know? I'm Jared, and I work the land. Farming isn't easy work, especially when you're trying to get everything ready for market. We grow mealies and veggies mostly, and I look after the cows too. But lately, I've been feeling… sluggish. Like my energy just disappears by lunchtime. I usually grab a vetkoek with polony for breakfast – quick and easy! – and then maybe some pap and chakalaka for lunch. Dinner? Well, if we have a good harvest, maybe some meat, but often it's just more pap. Yesterday, I was supposed to fix the fence around the kraal before the cattle got out. Simple job, right? But I just didn’t have the oomph. Ended up having to chase Bessie halfway across the field! A man wonders, can a body really run on vetkoek and hope?\n\nOld Man Themba, he's the clinic health worker, saw me looking tired at the shop. He asked what was wrong, and I just shrugged and said, 'Life, man, life.' But he insisted I come to the clinic. He didn’t scold, just explained things slowly. Said my body needs more than just filling food. It needs food that *gives* energy. He showed me a little chart – things like beans, spinach, even adding some carrots to the chakalaka. He said, 'Jared, you're strong, but even a strong bull needs good grazing.' He even wrote down a simple plan: porridge with a little milk for breakfast, beans and veggies with a small piece of fish for lunch, and maybe some chicken and sadza for supper. Sounded… different. But he said it would help with the bigger job – getting the whole field ploughed before the rains came. I thought, well, what harm could it do to try?\n\nTrying to change things, now that's a story! My wife, Nomusa, she's a good cook, but she's used to making things the way her mother taught her. She looked at me funny when I asked for more spinach in the chakalaka. 'What's gotten into you, Jared?' she asked. And the porridge… I'm used to something a bit more substantial, you see? The first morning, I was still hungry an hour later! Almost went back to the vetkoek, I tell you. But then I remembered the field. The ploughing. If I couldn’t even manage breakfast, how would I manage the whole field? So, I added a boiled egg, and that helped. It wasn't easy, but I pushed through, thinking about getting the work done.\n\nSlowly, slowly, things started to change. The porridge, with a bit of fruit, actually started tasting good. The beans and veggies gave me energy that lasted. I even started helping Nomusa in the garden, planting some more spinach and carrots! When it came time to plough the field, I wasn't dragging my feet. I felt… lighter. Stronger. I finished the job in three days, a whole day faster than last year! Nomusa was amazed. She even started experimenting with new recipes, adding lentils to the stew. Now, I'm thinking, maybe Old Man Themba was right. Maybe food isn't just about filling your stomach. Maybe it's about giving your body what it needs to do the things you love. And who knows, maybe next year, we'll even have a bigger harvest, all thanks to a little bit of healthy eating.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/82e6e705-5c1e-4ac7-8254-07a40cd86fa3_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/82e6e705-5c1e-4ac7-8254-07a40cd86fa3_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/82e6e705-5c1e-4ac7-8254-07a40cd86fa3_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/82e6e705-5c1e-4ac7-8254-07a40cd86fa3_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/82e6e705-5c1e-4ac7-8254-07a40cd86fa3_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/82e6e705-5c1e-4ac7-8254-07a40cd86fa3_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/82e6e705-5c1e-4ac7-8254-07a40cd86fa3_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/82e6e705-5c1e-4ac7-8254-07a40cd86fa3_3.mp3}	Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?	diet	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:20:04.10309+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gemma-3-27b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: David Otieno is a 25-34 year old, \\nCulture: Luo male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Medical doctor, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Siaya. Disability: he has none. Religion: Christianity (Anglican). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Ohangla dancing. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication). Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: None. Diet restrictions: Lactose-free. Smoking: No. Alcohol drinking: Yes. Physical activity: 5-7 days. Support network: Close friends. Health goals: Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?. his food access Easy access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of David Otieno and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in English that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken English, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This wi