 and a faded notice board. The light is fluorescent and slightly harsh. Jared is looking at Old Man Themba with a slight look of uncertainty.", "Medium shot of Jared Odhiambo standing in a small, simple kitchen. He is looking at a pot on the stove with a slightly confused expression, while his wife, Nomusa, stands nearby, arms crossed, looking at him questioningly. The kitchen is sparsely furnished, with basic cooking utensils visible. Warm, natural light from a window illuminates the scene. Jared is slightly hunched over, looking at the pot.", "Wide shot of Jared Odhiambo walking confidently behind a tractor ploughing a field. He is wearing work clothes and a cap, and he has a determined expression on his face. The field is lush and green, and the sky is blue with fluffy clouds. The light is bright and sunny. Jared is looking forward, a slight smile on his face."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 83.03575225976797, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What affordable, lactose-free traditional Luo dishes are suitable for a 55-year-old male sugarcane farmer with type 2 diabetes in Siaya, Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find local markets or shops in suburban Siaya that offer fresh, healthy foods suitable for managing diabetes on a tight budget?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community programs or support groups for diabetes management specifically for men my age in Siaya county?\\",\\n  \\"How can I modify popular Luo foods like ugali, sukuma wiki, or tilapia to fit a lactose-free, diabetic-friendly diet?\\",\\n  \\"What are some safe and culturally acceptable forms of physical activity for middle-aged men in suburban areas near Siaya, especially for those who are very busy with farming?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any government or NGO initiatives in Siaya that help small-scale farmers access affordable nutritious foods?\\",\\n  \\"How do other Luo men with diabetes in rural or suburban Kenya manage their condition while continuing physically demanding work like sugarcane farming?\\",\\n  \\"What local ingredients or crops common in Siaya can help maintain stable blood sugar and fit a lactose-free diet?\\",\\n  \\"Can you suggest cost-saving tips or meal plans for a Luo household aiming to eat healthily with someone who has type 2 diabetes and lactose intolerance?\\",\\n  \\"What are some faith-based or church-related health resources in Siaya for Christians wanting lifestyle guidance for diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How often should a male sugarcane farmer with type 2 diabetes in Siaya get medical checkups, and which clinics near towns are recommended?\\",\\n  \\"Has anyone in the Luo community shared success stories about managing type 2 diabetes and still enjoying traditional gatherings or foods in suburban Kenya?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "healthcare_access", "culture", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
