                   <td class="p-2">Rural (small community or countryside)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Limited access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Trader</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Storytelling</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No, I do not drink alcohol</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">26cc5bc7-5bab-4174-95e7-208dc3e47691</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gymâ€”what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up every morning before sunrise to start my day as a trader in our small community in Katsina. My daily routine is always packed, and I often find myself grabbing whatever food is available to eat on the go. I love traditional Hausa dishes like tuwo and miyan kubewa, but I know I need to be careful with my diet because of my Type 2 Diabetes. However, it's hard to resist the temptation of delicious foods, especially when I'm busy and don't have time to think about what I'm eating. One day, I had to cancel a important business meeting because I wasn't feeling well, and I realized that my neglect of my health needs was affecting my work.\n\nI decided to visit our local healthcare clinic to get some advice on how to manage my diet and health. The health worker, Sister Fatima, was very kind and helpful. She explained to me that eating healthy doesn't have to be expensive, and that there are many traditional Hausa foods that are nutritious and good for me. She advised me to start by making small changes to my diet, like eating more fruits and vegetables, and to try to cook at home using healthy ingredients. She also reminded me to take my insulin injections regularly and to monitor my blood sugar levels. I was a bit resistant at first, but Sister Fatima's advice was clear and simple, and she showed me how to make healthy choices that fit my lifestyle and budget.\n\nI tried to follow Sister Fatima's advice, but it wasn't easy. I had to adjust my routine and make time to cook healthy meals, which was a challenge. I also had to deal with cravings for unhealthy foods, and there were times when I slipped up and ate things I shouldn't have. One day, I had a minor setback when I ate a large portion of tuwo with a lot of sugar, and my blood sugar levels skyrocketed. I felt discouraged and frustrated, but I remembered Sister Fatima's words of encouragement and the importance of persisting. I knew I had to keep trying, especially since I had a big business project coming up that required me to be in top shape.\n\nAs I continued to work on my health, I started to notice gradual improvements. I had more energy, and my blood sugar levels were more stable. I was able to focus better and work more efficiently, which helped me to complete my business project successfully. I realized that taking care of my health was not just about managing my diabetes, but also about being able to live a full and productive life. I became more open to learning about healthy habits and making positive changes in my life. I started to enjoy cooking healthy meals and experimenting with new recipes, and I even shared my experiences with my friends and family, who were inspired by my progress.\n\nNow, I feel more confident and in control of my health. I know that I still have challenges ahead, but I'm ready to face them. I've learned that eating healthy is not just about the food I eat, but also about the habits I keep and the choices I make. I'm grateful for the support of my family and friends, and for the guidance of Sister Fatima and our local healthcare clinic. I'm excited to continue on this journey of health and wellness, and I know that I'll be able to achieve my goals and live a happy and healthy life. As I always say, "Ilmi dai ya yi mana alheri" - knowledge is power, and I'm grateful for the knowledge and wisdom that has helped me to take control of my health.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/26cc5bc7-5bab-4174-95e7-208dc3e47691_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/26cc5bc7-5bab-4174-95e7-208dc3e47691_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/26cc5bc7-5bab-4174-95e7-208dc3e47691_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/26cc5bc7-5bab-4174-95e7-208dc3e47691_3.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/26cc5bc7-5bab-4174-95e7-208dc3e47691_4.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/26cc5bc7-5bab-4174-95e7-208dc3e47691_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/stor