g at Sister Fatima with a slightly skeptical expression, while she gestures towards a colorful chart with pictures of healthy foods. The clinic is clean but shows signs of regular use. Nura is wearing a traditional Hausa outfit, and Sister Fatima is in a nurse's uniform. The light is fluorescent, but softened by the curtains.", "Medium shot of Nura Amin, 48, walking slowly along a dusty road in Kano, looking slightly uncomfortable. He's wearing simple athletic shoes and a traditional Hausa outfit. He's glancing at his watch with a frustrated expression. The sun is setting, casting long shadows. His posture is slightly hunched, and his pace is slow and deliberate. The surrounding environment is typical of an urban Kano neighborhood.", "Medium shot of Nura Amin, 48, smiling genuinely while walking alongside Malam Musa, a man in his 60s, in a park in Kano. They are engaged in conversation, and Nura's posture is more upright and energetic. The park is green and well-maintained, with trees providing shade. Nura is wearing a clean, pressed Hausa outfit. The light is warm and golden, suggesting late afternoon."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 83.51873853267767, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are the best exercise recommendations for a 45â€“54 year old male with type 2 diabetes living in urban Kano, Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"How can a practicing Muslim in Kano balance daily insulin injections with fasting during Ramadan?\\",\\n  \\"Which community or religious groups in Hausa-speaking urban areas of Kano offer support or programs for diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"What physical activities are commonly practiced in urban Kano for adults with diabetes who only exercise 1-2 days per week?\\",\\n  \\"Are there storytelling clubs or social events in Kano city where someone with diabetes can participate safely?\\",\\n  \\"What healthy, locally available Hausa foods are suitable for t