ms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">9499ac13-1ec0-47d5-a695-6441576dacea</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up early, like every day, and I go to my little shop near the market. My name is Wanjiku, and I’m a woman who sells fresh vegetables. I used to think, 'Why should I move my body when I have so much to do?' I eat mostly what’s cheap and easy — beans, maize, and a bit of sweet potato. I don’t eat much fruit or greens. I know I have diabetes, but I don’t really know how it affects my hands or legs. I just feel tired. When I work, I carry heavy baskets, and I don’t feel strong. One day, I tried to walk to the market after work, but I felt dizzy and my feet hurt. I stopped. I thought, 'Maybe I don’t need to move — I just need to keep selling.' But then I asked myself, 'If I don’t move, how will I keep my body strong for my shop?' That’s when I knew I had to try something new.\n\nAt the health clinic, a nurse named Lila looked at me and said, 'Wanjiku, you need to walk every day — just 15 minutes. Not long, not hard. Just walk with your feet on the ground, like you’re going to the market. It helps your sugar go down and your legs feel better.' I said, 'But I have so much to do — I can’t leave my shop!' She smiled and said, 'You don’t have to leave. Just walk after your work. Even 15 minutes. And you can do it in the morning or after the sun goes down.' I hesitated. I didn’t know if I could do it. But I thought, 'If I don’t try, I’ll never know if I can.' So I said yes.\n\nI started walking after work. I walked to the corner shop and back. But on the second day, I felt my feet hurt more. I didn’t want to go. I thought, 'Maybe I’m not strong enough.' I stayed home. But then I remembered — next week, I have to help my cousin build a small fence for her new house. She needs someone to carry bricks and help with the work. I told myself, 'If I don’t get stronger, I won’t be able to help her. And that’s important to me.' So I got up. I walked slowly. I took deep breaths. My feet ached, but I kept going. I did it for 10 minutes. Then I did it again. I felt better.\n\nAfter a week, I could walk 20 minutes without feeling tired. I started walking before work too. My feet feel lighter. I even noticed my hands don’t shake as much when I sell vegetables. I still eat beans and maize, but now I add a little spinach and banana. I don’t feel dizzy anymore. When my cousin asked me to help with the fence, I said yes — and I did it with confidence. I walked to the site, carried bricks, and helped build it. At the end, I said to myself, 'I didn’t just get stronger — I became more like myself. I can do more. I can keep going. And I know — I can keep walking every day, even when I’m tired.'	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9499ac13-1ec0-47d5-a695-6441576dacea_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9499ac13-1ec0-47d5-a695-6441576dacea_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9499ac13-1ec0-47d5-a695-6441576dacea_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/9499ac13-1ec0-47d5-a695-6441576dacea_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/9499ac13-1ec0-47d5-a695-6441576dacea_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/9499ac13-1ec0-47d5-a695-6441576dacea_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/9499ac13-1ec0-47d5-a695-6441576dacea_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/9499ac13-1ec0-47d5-a695-6441576dacea_3.mp3}	How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:10:46.546166+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: \\nCulture: None female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. Disability: she has none. Religion: None. Hobbies: Storytelling. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Her