uld you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Fish trader</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Storytelling</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D â€” Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">4515be6d-c14a-46d8-b2cb-282ca20235bc</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">What kinds of exercises are safe and helpful for someone with diabetes?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Achieng, and I live here in Kisumu, near the lake. It’s a busy place, always bustling. I sell fish – mostly tilapia – at the market. It’s hard work, from the early morning when I wake up to haggle with the fishermen, to the afternoon when I’m packing up and counting my money. I mostly eat ugali and some fish, sometimes beans if I’m lucky. Sometimes, I just have a sad piece of bread. I don't really think much about how my food makes me feel, you know? I just need to sell enough fish to buy more food. It’s a simple life, but it’s my life.  Sometimes my legs feel a bit tired, but I just keep going. I don't really listen to my body, do I?\n\nToday, I was helping my nephew, Samuel, carry a big crate of fish back to the stall. It was heavier than usual, and my legs were already feeling a bit weak. I pushed too hard, and suddenly… *oof*! I stumbled and the crate spilled, scattering fish everywhere! Samuel just laughed and said, ‘Achieng, you need to take it easy!’ But I just brushed myself off and started gathering the fish, feeling a bit embarrassed. It was a good day for sales though, so I told myself it didn't really matter. I just hoped no one would notice I was struggling. It's a good thing my stall is near the main road – people always pass by.\n\nDr. Okoth at the clinic told me I need to look after myself better. She said my legs feeling tired all the time isn’t normal. She said I need to move my body, even just a little bit, to make my legs stronger. She also said I need to eat more vegetables and fruits, not just fish all the time. It sounded like a lot of work, and honestly, I felt a bit confused. She gave me a pamphlet with pictures of people exercising, but I just stared at it.  She said I needed to start small, just fifteen minutes a day.  She explained that even a short walk could make a difference. I thought, ‘Fifteen minutes? That’s nothing!’ But she looked at me so kindly, like she really wanted me to feel better. \n\nSo, I started walking to the market every morning before I set up my stall. It was only ten minutes, but it felt good. My legs didn’t feel quite so tired by lunchtime.  Then, I started adding a few pieces of mango to my lunch. It wasn't easy, of course. Sometimes I just wanted to go straight back to my usual ugali and fish. But then I remembered Samuel’s laugh and the spilled fish. I knew I had to keep trying.  The next big thing is helping my son, David, build a stronger stall for the upcoming fish festival. It’s a big job, and I need to be strong to help him.  I’m starting to feel stronger, and I know I can do it.  Maybe, just maybe, taking care of myself is the best way to help my family.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4515be6d-c14a-46d8-b2cb-282ca20235bc_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4515be6d-c14a-46d8-b2cb-282ca20235bc_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4515be6d-c14a-46d8-b2cb-282ca20235bc_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4515be6d-c14a-46d8-b2cb-282ca20235bc_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4515be6d-c14a-46d8-b2cb-282ca20235bc_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4515be6d-c14a-46d8-b2cb-282ca20235bc_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4515be6d-c14a-46d8-b2cb-282ca20235bc_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4515be6d-c14a-46d8-b2cb-282ca20235bc_3.mp3}	How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:20:03.831435+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "gemma-3-4b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Akinyi Odhiambo is a 55-64 year old, \\nCulture: Luo female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Public health officer, lives in a Suburban (near city or town) in Kisumu. Disability: she has none.