I just… I get tired.’ Samuel’s voice is clear and playful.  Subtle sounds of market activity – fish being unloaded, vendors bargaining – create a busy backdrop.", "Dr. Okoth, a calm, professional voice, 50s, speaking gently to Achieng, 38. The sound of a clinic – quiet medical equipment, hushed voices – is present. Dr. Okoth says: ‘Achieng, it’s important to listen to your body… even a little movement can make a big difference.’ Achieng’s voice is hesitant and questioning, with a slight rise in pitch at the end of phrases.  A soft, reassuring background melody plays.", "Sound of Achieng", "I’m going to help my son with the stall… and I’m going to be strong.’  The overall atmosphere is peaceful and optimistic.”"], "image_prompts": ["Achieng, a 38-year-old Luo woman, stands in a bustling Kisumu market, surrounded by colorful fish and shouting vendors. She is carefully weighing a tilapia, her face etched with determination and a hint of weariness. The lighting is bright and warm, highlighting the vibrant colours of the market. Focus on the textures of the fish scales and the patterned fabric of her dress.", "Medium shot of Achieng, 38, kneeling on the dusty ground, surrounded by scattered tilapia fish after a clumsy stumble. Her nephew, Samuel, a young boy of 10, is laughing and pointing at her. The scene is chaotic and slightly messy, reflecting the busy market environment. Capture the dust motes dancing in the sunlight.", "Close-up of Achieng's hand, 38, holding a pamphlet with colourful illustrations of people exercising. Her expression is thoughtful and slightly hesitant. The background is blurred, showing the interior of a brightly lit clinic with a friendly, middle-aged doctor observing her. The lighting is soft and clinical.", "Wide shot of Achieng, 38, walking purposefully along a dusty road leading to the market, carrying a small woven basket. The sun is setting, casting long shadows. She is wearing a simple but colourful dress, and her posture is upright and confident. The landscape includes a glimpse of Lake Victoria in the distance."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 9.96361825405023, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some effective and culturally appropriate diabetes exercise options for a 35-44-year-old Luo woman living in urban Kisumu with limited support?\\",\\n  \\"How can a fish trader in Kisumu balance a vegetarian diet with daily insulin injections for managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any safe group exercise programs in Kisumu urban areas tailored for women with diabetes who have little time due to work?\\",\\n  \\"Which traditional Luo storytelling events in Kisumu might also provide opportunities for social or light physical activity suitable for diabetics?\\",\\n  \\"What diabetes-friendly vegetarian meal options are commonly available in urban Kisumu markets?\\",\\n  \\"How can Methodist Christian beliefs and practices in Kenya support diabetes self-care and mental well-being for women living alone?\\",\\n  \\"Are there city parks or community centers in Kisumu suitable for beginners to start low-impact exercise routines for diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"What resources or support groups exist in Kisumu urban areas for women with type 2 diabetes who live independently?\\",\\n  \\"How does daily alcohol consumption impact diabetes management in Luo women, and are there culturally relevant strategies to reduce intake?\\",\\n  \\"How can a busy working adult in Kisumu integrate more physical activity into daily routines when they have no regular exercise days and limited family support?\\",\\n  \\"What local clinics or health centers in Kisumu offer specialized counseling for diabetes management in working women?\\",\\n  \\"Are there Luo herbal or traditional remedies commonly used in Kisumu for diabetes support, and what are their interactions with insulin and oral medications?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
