al photo.", "Amina Bello walking slowly on a dusty street in urban Kano in the late afternoon, looking slightly tired but determined, marketplace visible in the background, wearing modest clothing suitable for exercise, one hand loosely holding a small bag, medium shot, natural unposed photo.", "Amina Bello smiling confidently while standing outside her market stall during a busy family gathering day, vibrant decorations and relatives in the background, morning light highlighting her joyful expression and relaxed posture, medium shot, candid photo."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 3.40064914226532, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are the best gluten-free Hausa traditional foods available in Kano city markets that I can include in my diet as a young female trader with type 2 diabetes and hypertension?\\",\\n  \\"How can I find group exercise activities or support for young adult women in Kano, Nigeria, who live alone and want to improve blood sugar control?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any Islamic community wellness programs in urban Kano that help support females with type 2 diabetes and hypertension to stay motivated to exercise regularly?\\",\\n  \\"How does keeping animals as a hobby in Kano city affect my physical activity level and help manage my blood sugar as a Hausa woman with diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What local social events or family-centered gatherings in Kano could help me stay socially active while managing diabetes-friendly food options and my gluten-free diet?\\",\\n  \\"Are there Hausa-specific motivational stories or advice from young women in Kano who manage type 2 diabetes and hypertension successfully while balancing work as traders?\\",\\n  \\"What are the recommended times for safe outdoor exercise for women in urban Kano, Nigeria, considering cultural expectations and safety, for better blood sugar control?\\",\\n  \\"How do most female traders in Kano, especially those from the Hausa culture, manage taking insulin or oral medications during busy market hours?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local healthcare clinics or hospitals in Kano that offer diabetes management support in Hausa language for young women who feel isolated or lack family support?\\",\\n  \\"What low-cost, culturally accepted exercise routines can a young woman living alone in urban Kano adopt to boost motivation and improve hypertension as well as diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there specific animal rearing practices among Hausa women in Kano that contribute to physical wellness or help in the management of type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can I maintain my faith and integrate regular prayers into stress management and motivation for exercise, as a young Hausa Muslim woman with diabetes in a big city?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Relevant fields: Age (18-24 years), Female, Hausa culture, Urban trader in Kano, Type 2 Diabetes, Regular healthcare access, Medication (Insulin injections), Hypertension, Diet restrictions (Halal), Physical activity (1-2 days), Support network (limited), Health goal (feeling tired or discouraged, seeking motivation and understanding of exercise's role in blood sugar). Work responsibilities as a trader and daily routine also important.", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
