ting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "iteration", "audio_prompts": ["Kenji sits alone by the rice paddy. The ambient sounds of distant calls to prayer, birds chirping, gentle wind rustling leaves, and soft footsteps in damp earth. Kenji breathes heavily, his breath ragged and uneven, occasionally sighing. Plastic bowl shifts with a quiet clatter when his hand moves. The spade lands onto the ground with a dull thud. Kenji mutters softly to himself, voice slightly shaky, 'Why am I tired, Kenji?' in South African English accent.", "Aisha, a female nurse, stands nearby in the bright clinic. Medium shot audio perspective. The quiet hum of a ceiling fan, light chatter from a hallway, and a pen tapping the desk. Aisha’s voice is clear, warm, with gentle pauses and careful pronunciation, 'Kenji, for your diabetes, try brown rice, beans, and always vegetables.' Kenji listens, breathing slow, replies softly, slightly hesitant, 'Alright, Nurse… I will see.' Their voices echo lightly on the clinic's hard floor.", "Kenji is alone in his humble kitchen at night. Ambient noise includes a kettle hissing gently in the background, the distant radio from a neighbor’s window, and a faint clink of spoon against the plate. Kenji’s hand rubs over his chin and he exhales through his nose, breath slow and deliberate. He quietly pushes his plate forward, whispering with doubt and determination, 'Brown rice, Kenji… You can do it.' The room feels close and still.", "Kenji works outside with his brother, Musa—a young male in his mid-20s—standing a short distance away. Wide shot audio. The rhythmic scraping of a spade on dirt, leaves crunching underfoot, birds calling from nearby trees. Musa laughs softly in encouragement, 'Kenji, you strong man now!' Kenji laughs too, a little out of breath but proud, 'Musa, I’m getting there,' his confidence bright as the breeze stirs around them. The canal water flows gently in the background."], "image_prompts": ["Kenji, a Hausa male in his late 20s, sits on a narrow ridge between lush green rice paddies on the outskirts of Kano. He is dressed in a faded navy shirt and loose trousers, feet firmly planted in the dirt, his plastic lunch bowl beside him, half-eaten rice and bread visible. Morning sunlight gives a soft golden glow to his face, sweat beading on his brow. Kenji's posture is slumped, one hand gripping his knee, the other arm limp as he stares at the spade lying in the field. Texture of worn farm tools, earth, green rice, and simple housing roofs in the distance.", "Aisha, a female nurse in her 30s, stands beside Kenji in a sunlit rural clinic room. Medium shot. Kenji sits on a simple wooden chair, hands on his lap, eyes lifted up, expression a mix of confusion and slight hope. Aisha stands nearby with a gentle look, holding a pamphlet written in Hausa and pointing at some foods drawn on it. Bright, indirect daylight filters through a window, and a white curtain hangs unevenly. The walls are painted light blue but peeling in some corners, and an old weighing scale is visible along the wall.", "Kenji is alone in his modest kitchen, a light blue plastic table with a simple brown rice meal and sliced cucumbers in front of him. Kenji’s hand hovers hesitantly over his new meal, eyes narrowed, lips pressed as if unsure. His other hand reaches for a stainless cup of water. Overhead fluorescent light creates a cool, even glow, with shadows under Kenji's chin and hands. On the shelf behind him are a Quran and spice jars, and the window is open to let in the faint evening breeze.", "Kenji, now smiling, stands stronger and more upright beside a muddy irrigation canal in his field, holding a spade confidently. Wide shot. His brother, a younger man in an old football shirt, stands a few paces away with arms crossed, grinning at Kenji’s work. The ground is freshly dug, and the afternoon sun makes long shadows over the green rice. Nearby, an old blue jerry can and two battered water bottles rest against the edge of the canal. Both men’s faces show relief and pride."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 1.9408850491046905, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some vegan-friendly Hausa recipes using easily available ingredients in suburban Kano, Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"How can a rice farmer in the suburbs near Kano manage type 2 diabetes with local, affordable foods and a vegan diet?\\",\\n  \\"What are practical daily exercise routines for someone with type 2 diabetes who currently does not exercise and works as a farmer in Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local football (soccer) clubs or groups in suburban Kano that accept adults over 25 interested in physical activity for health?\\",\\n  \\"What is a nutritionally balanced, simple daily vegan meal plan tailored for a young Hausa Muslim male with type 2 diabetes in Kano?\\",\\n  \\"How can I use traditional Hausa herbs or remedies alongside my diabetes medication safely in northern Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find support groups or community resources for young adults with diabetes in Kano, especially among the Hausa population?\\",\\n  \\"What healthy Nigerian rice-based dishes can be made without animal products and are suitable for diabetics?\\",\\n  \\"How can I maintain my blood sugar during Ramadan fasting as a vegan diabetic male in Kano, Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"What are some supermarkets or local markets near Kano with the best vegan food options for diabetics?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any cultural considerations or taboos around eating vegan within Hausa Muslim communities in Kano?\\",\\n  \\"What is the recommended frequency and type of physical activity for a male rice farmer with type 2 diabetes who has not been physically active recently in northern Nigeria?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Relevant fields: Daily routine (working adult, rice farmer), Health knowledge (limited idea regarding foods for blood sugar), Insulin injections, Easy access to healthy foods, Support network (close friends), Religion (Islam, Halal diet), Exercises little, Health resources (online, digital).", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
