td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">eea08ae4-d607-4b69-85de-84b8109c5485</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Sometimes I feel tired or discouragedâ€”how can I stay motivated, and how does exercise help my blood sugar?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up every morning in my small apartment in Sokoto, getting ready for another busy day as a butcher. My diet mainly consists of traditional Hausa dishes like tuwo and miyan kubewa, which are delicious but not always the healthiest. I've been noticing that I get tired easily, especially after a long day of work, but I never thought it could be related to my diet or health. One day, I had to cancel a big order at the market because I wasn't feeling well, and that's when I realized that my health might be affecting my work.\n\nI decided to visit our local healthcare clinic to see if they could help me understand what was going on. The nurse there was very kind and explained to me that I have type 2 diabetes. At first, I was resistant to the idea of changing my diet and exercise routine, but she assured me that it was necessary to manage my condition. She gave me some simple tips on how to eat healthier and stay active, and even recommended some traditional Hausa dishes that are good for me, like grilled fish with vegetables.\n\nIt wasn't easy to adjust to my new routine at first. I had to start taking insulin injections and monitoring my blood sugar levels regularly. I also had to make some changes to my diet, which was hard because I love eating traditional Hausa food. But I knew I had to do it if I wanted to feel better and be able to work without getting tired all the time. I had a small setback when I accidentally ate some sugary snacks at a tea spot, but I didn't give up. I knew I had to stay on track, especially since I had a big order coming up at the market.\n\nAfter a few weeks of sticking to my new routine, I started to feel like myself again. I had more energy, and I was able to work without getting tired. I even started enjoying some of the healthier traditional Hausa dishes that the nurse had recommended. When the big order came up, I was able to fulfill it without any problems, and my customers were happy with the quality of the meat. I realized that taking care of my health wasn't just about managing my diabetes, but also about being able to do my job well and provide for my family.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/eea08ae4-d607-4b69-85de-84b8109c5485_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/eea08ae4-d607-4b69-85de-84b8109c5485_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/eea08ae4-d607-4b69-85de-84b8109c5485_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/eea08ae4-d607-4b69-85de-84b8109c5485_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/eea08ae4-d607-4b69-85de-84b8109c5485_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/eea08ae4-d607-4b69-85de-84b8109c5485_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/eea08ae4-d607-4b69-85de-84b8109c5485_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/eea08ae4-d607-4b69-85de-84b8109c5485_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:29:35.300189+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "Llama-3.3-70B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: \\nCulture: None female. Religion: None. Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Football (soccer). Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections. Regular healthcare access: Yes. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 0 days. Health goals: What kinds of exercises are safe and helpful for someone with diabetes?. Tone of the output: classic_change.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Amina Suleiman and understanding the persona's needs (\\"Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?\\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in English that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?. \\n Use spoken English, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a classic_change tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in English.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in English.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "resistance", "audio_prompts": ["Fatima Bello's voice, sounding tired and frustrated, with a hint of a Hausa accent, saying 'I don't understand why I'm always so tired', with some background noise of a bustling market.", "Fatima Bello's voice, sounding concerned and uncertain, with a hint of a Hausa accent, saying 'I don't know if I can do this', with some background noise of a clinic.", "Fatima Bello's voice, sounding determined and upbeat, with a hint of a Hausa accent, saying 'I can do this', with some background noise of a market.", "Fatima Bello's voice, sounding happy and relieved, with a hint of a Hausa accent, saying 'I did it', with some background noise of a bustling market and chatter of customers."], "image_prompts": ["Fatima Bello, a young woman, sitting on a couch, looking tired, with a disappointed expression, in a small apartment in Sokoto, with traditional Hausa dishes on the table in front of her, in a medium shot.", "Fatima Bello, standing in a clinic, listening to a nurse, who is explaining something to her, with a mix of confusion and concern on her face, in a wide shot.", "Fatima Bello, walking in a market, looking determined, with a basket of vegetables in her hand, and a few traditional Hausa dishes in the background, in a medium shot.", "Fatima Bello, smiling, standing in front of her butcher shop, with a big order of meat on display, and a few customers chatting with her, in a wide shot."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 2.3471117496490477, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some exercise routines suitable for a young Hausa Muslim woman with type 2 diabetes living in suburban Sokoto, Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"How do local Sokoto tea spots impact social support and motivation for women trying to manage diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any cultural or religious considerations in Sokoto for women butchers trying to balance work and diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"What easy and healthy food options are commonly available in suburban areas near Sokoto for someone with no dietary restrictions?\\",\\n  \\"How can I stay motivated to exercise regularly when I feel tired or discouraged as a working adult in Sokoto?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best ways to manage rare tobacco use for a female, young adult Muslim with type 2 diabetes in Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community groups or local support systems in Sokoto that help young Muslim women manage diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How does regular physical activity influence blood sugar control specifically for young adults with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What tips do other Hausa women in Sokoto have for maintaining energy and avoiding discouragement when managing diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What facilities or resources does the local healthcare clinic in my Sokoto suburb offer for diabetes education and motivation?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any Islamic teachings or Hausa cultural practices in Sokoto that encourage staying active and healthy for young women?\\",\\n  \\"How can chatting and debating at Sokoto tea spots fit into a balanced lifestyle with type 2 diabetes for a social, working woman?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
