                <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Trader</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Traditional wrestling</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">â€” None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Occasionally (less than once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">20f4eada-cc8a-4529-abec-10b921831da5</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Chinonso, and I'm a trader here in Kano. Every day is busy, busy, busy! I sell kola nuts at the market, you know, the ones people chew to stay awake and feel strong. I like to start my day with strong, sweet tea and maybe a puff of cigarette – gets me going, right? Then, it’s straight to the market. Today, I had a small order to fill for Alhaji Musa, just fifty kola nuts for a wedding. Easy work, I thought. But halfway through sorting them, I felt… *weak*. Like my legs were made of water. I had to sit down, and even then, my hands were shaking. I just couldn’t seem to focus, and I messed up the order, giving Alhaji Musa the wrong count. He wasn’t happy, not happy at all. I wondered, what was going on with me?\n\nOld Mama Aisha, the woman who sells dates next to my stall, saw me looking pale. She’s a wise woman, that one. She told me, 'Chinonso, you need to go see Doctor Ibrahim at the clinic. You look like you're running on empty.' I didn’t want to go, honestly. Clinics are for sick people, and I'm a strong man! But Mama Aisha insisted, saying, 'It’s not about being strong, it's about being *smart* strong.' So, I went. Doctor Ibrahim checked me, asked about my tea and cigarettes, and told me about my sugar. He said it was too high, and that's why I was feeling weak. He didn't tell me to stop everything, just to be careful. 'Eat more things like beans and maize, Chinonso,' he said. 'They release sugar slowly. And maybe swap some of that sweet tea for water, eh?' It sounded… doable. I could try, couldn't I?\n\nTrying to change things is hard, I tell you! The first day, I tried to have beans with my tea. It just didn't taste right! I missed the sweetness. And the cigarette… oh, the cigarette called to me all morning. I almost gave in, but then I remembered Alhaji Musa's wedding. I had a bigger order coming up – two hundred kola nuts for a naming ceremony. If I messed *that* up, my reputation would be ruined. So, I forced myself to eat the beans, even though my face was making funny shapes. I drank water with my tea, and it felt… bland. But I kept at it. It was tough, really tough, but I told myself, 'Just for the naming ceremony, Chinonso. Just until you finish the work.'\n\nSlowly, slowly, things started to get better. The beans didn't taste so bad after a few days. I even started adding a little pepper to them, like Mama Aisha does. And I cut back on the cigarettes, having only one or two instead of a pack. I still had my sweet tea, but I drank less of it. When the day of the naming ceremony came, I felt… different. I wasn't shaky, and my head was clear. I sorted those two hundred kola nuts quickly and accurately, and the family was very pleased. Alhaji Ibrahim, the father of the new baby, even gave me a generous tip! After that, I started thinking, maybe Doctor Ibrahim was right. Maybe eating better and cutting back on the cigarettes isn't just about the work, it’s about feeling good *all* the time. Maybe, just maybe, I should learn more about what I can eat to stay strong, for a long time.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/20f4eada-cc8a-4529-abec-10b921831da5_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/20f4eada-cc8a-4529-abec-10b921831da5_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/20f4eada-cc8a-4529-abec-10b921831da5_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/20f4eada-cc8a-4529-abec-10b921831da5_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/20f4eada-cc8a-4529-abec-10b921831da5_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/20f4eada-cc8a-4529-abec-10b921831da5_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/20f4eada-cc8a-4529-abec-10b921831da5_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/20f4eada-cc8a-4529-abec-10b921831da5_3.mp3}	Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?	diet	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:29:37.197594+00	{"label": "GOOD", "model": "gemma-3-27b-it", "p