tor Ibrahim. You're looking very pale.' Chinonso's voice responds, hesitant and slightly muffled: 'But Mama Aisha, I'm a strong man... I don't need a doctor.' The scene includes the ambient sounds of a busy market, but the voices are clear and distinct. Mama Aisha's voice has a warm, reassuring quality.", "Chinonso Okafor, speaking to himself with a frustrated sigh: 'Ugh, these beans... they just don't taste right.' followed by the sound of him reluctantly chewing. The audio also includes the faint sound of a cigarette lighter flicking, then quickly being extinguished. Chinonso’s voice is strained and slightly resentful, with a noticeable pause before he starts chewing. The background is quiet, emphasizing his internal struggle.", "Chinonso Okafor’s voice, sounding energetic and confident, saying 'Alhaji Ibrahim, here are your kola nuts, all counted and sorted.' Alhaji Ibrahim, a man in his 50s, responds from across the room with a booming laugh and a cheerful 'Excellent work, Chinonso! You are a true professional!' The audio is filled with the lively sounds of a bustling market, but Chinonso’s voice is clear and proud. Chinonso's tone is upbeat and enthusiastic."], "image_prompts": ["A candid, natural, unposed medium shot of Chinonso Okafor, a Hausa man in his 30s, sitting on a low stool amidst a pile of kola nuts at a bustling Kano market. He’s clutching his head with one hand, looking distressed, with a slightly blurred background of vendors and shoppers. The lighting is warm and diffused, suggesting late morning. Focus on the texture of the kola nuts and the worn fabric of his clothing. Chinonso’s posture is slumped, conveying weakness.", "A wide shot of Chinonso Okafor, looking hesitant, standing outside a small, brightly painted local healthcare clinic in Kano. He is wearing a traditional Hausa cap and a simple, patterned shirt. Old Mama Aisha, a woman in her 60s with a kind face, is gently guiding him towards the entrance, her hand lightly on his arm. The scene is bathed in the harsh sunlight of midday. Chinonso’s expression is a mix of apprehension and trust.", "A candid, natural, unposed close-up of Chinonso Okafor, seated at a small table in his home, reluctantly eating a plate of beans with a spoon. His face is contorted in a slight grimace, but he’s determinedly taking a bite. The background is simple – a bare wall and a small rug. The lighting is soft and slightly dim, highlighting his expression. Chinonso’s jaw is clenched, showing his effort.", "A candid, natural, unposed medium shot of Chinonso Okafor, smiling confidently while carefully sorting kola nuts at the Kano market. He’s interacting with Alhaji Ibrahim, a well-dressed man in his 50s, handing him a neatly arranged pile of nuts. The background is bustling with market activity. The lighting is bright and cheerful. Chinonso’s posture is upright and energetic."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 83.51873853267767, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some common vegetarian dishes in Kano city that are suitable for someone with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Which Hausa traditional foods can I include in my diet as a trader managing type 2 diabetes and following vegetarian restrictions?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find reliable diabetes education or support groups for men in their 20s-30s in urban Kano?\\",\\n  \\"How does the climate and food availability in Kano influence healthy vegetarian meal planning for diabetics?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local Kano-based herbal or traditional medicines that are safe and effective to incorporate with insulin for diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"What tips exist for Hausa Muslim traders in Kano to balance Ramadan fasting with type 2 diabetes and insulin injections?\\",\\n  \\"Which traditional or contemporary physical activities are recommended for young Hausa men with diabetes living in cities, especially for those who rarely exercise?\\",\\n  \\"How can I access affordable diabetes-friendly vegetarian foods near Sabon Gari market or other major markets in Kano?\\",\\n  \\"What are the benefits and risks of occasionally consuming tobacco and alcohol for male diabetics in northern Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"Are there practical ways to prepare low-sugar vegetarian meals using locally available ingredients in Kano?\\",\\n  \\"How can I adjust my busy trading schedule in Kano city to include physical activities without compromising my diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"What government or NGO programs in Kano offer support or counseling for young adults with type 2 diabetes who live alone?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
