isa walks through a park, her voice calm and clear, saying, 'I can do this. Just for the lesson,' while the sound of children laughing in the distance, birds singing, and wind blowing through leaves, her breathing is smooth and steady, her voice slightly rising at the end of the sentence, showing confidence.", "Adisa walks down a quiet street, her voice soft and warm, saying, 'I can do this. I am strong. I am healthy. I am Adisa,' while the sound of wind in trees and birds flying, her breathing deep and even, a long pause after the last word, followed by a soft, natural breath, like a quiet smile."], "image_prompts": ["Adisa stands on a wooden back step in a suburban home, wearing a simple cotton dress and a white headscarf, holding a banana and a glass of milk in her hands, her feet slightly apart, looking down at the fruit with a tired expression, sunlight filtering through the trees behind her, the garden in the background with small herbs growing in clay pots, soft morning light on the wooden floor, dust motes floating in the air, her posture shows fatigue and slight slouching.", "Adisa walks slowly down a narrow suburban path with her shoes on, arms swinging slightly, her hands in her pockets, wearing a blue tunic and a headscarf, the sun warm on her skin, a small loaf of bread in her hand, the path lined with old trees and flower pots, wind gently blowing her hair, her posture is relaxed but slightly hunched, the ground has a mix of dry grass and gravel, her face shows mild concentration as she walks.", "Adisa walks through a small park near a suburban house, wearing a light grey dress, her arms swinging naturally, her head up, sunlight hitting her face from the side, a group of children playing in the distance, the path is paved with small stones, grass growing between them, she is walking with a steady pace, her feet touching the ground gently, her expression calm and focused, a small smile on her lips.", "Adisa walks down a quiet suburban street with her hands in her pockets, wearing a simple cotton dress, her head slightly tilted, sunlight streaming through the trees, birds flying in the background, the wind gently blowing her hair, her posture is upright and relaxed, the street has old houses with painted doors, the sky is clear blue, she looks ahead with quiet confidence, a small smile forming on her face."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 63.62262771068475, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some effective home workout routines suitable for a Nigerian woman living in suburban Kano who doesnâ€™t have gym equipment?\\",\\n  \\"How can I adapt traditional Hausa household items for exercise to help manage my diabetes as a Qurâ€™anic teacher?\\",\\n  \\"What vegan meal options are common in suburban Kano, Nigeria, especially among Hausa Muslims, and how do they support blood sugar control?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any local support groups or community programs in Kano for Muslim women with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can I balance fasting during Ramadan with managing type 2 diabetes and staying active near Kano?\\",\\n  \\"What simple physical activities can I do 1-2 days a week at home in suburban areas to help with diabetes, given my easy access to healthy foods?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find culturally appropriate, Hausa vegan recipes that fit within Islamic dietary guidelines and support diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any community walking groups, womenâ€™s fitness classes, or park facilities near suburban Kano that are respectful of Islamic dress and customs?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best ways to replace tobacco and alcohol habits with healthy, faith-aligned activities for a Muslim woman in northern Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"How can I engage my close friends in staying active and healthy while respecting our Islamic faith and Hausa traditions?\\",\\n  \\"Are there recommended prayers, Qurâ€™an recitation postures, or spiritual activities that also promote light physical movement for female Qurâ€™anic teachers in Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"What should I discuss with my local healthcare clinic in Kano regarding medication, traditional remedies, and lifestyle changes for diabetes as a young Muslim woman?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "name", "gender", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "activities", "healthcare_frequency", "t2d_status", "alcohol", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
