oung Luo male farmer, standing tired with hand on hip in a sorghum field at sunrise, wearing faded work clothes and a cap, with dry earth and green sorghum plants around, subdued morning light casting soft shadows, medium shot capturing his thoughtful gaze towards the horizon.", "Ogola Odhiambo sitting in a simple rural health clinic consultation room conversing with a female nurse in uniform, nurse explaining with a smile holding nutritional pamphlet, natural daylight from window illuminating their faces, natural unposed moment showing Ogola’s curious yet hesitant expression, medium shot.", "Ogola Odhiambo attempting to eat sweet potatoes at a rustic outdoor kitchen area, glancing longingly towards a nearby market stall selling fried foods, smoke rising faintly in background, wearing casual shirt and trousers, body posture showing mild temptation but determination, wide shot including surrounding village environment.", "Ogola Odhiambo dancing energetically with a male friend at an outdoor community event in Migori, both smiling broadly and dressed in casual, colorful clothes, evening golden light highlighting movement and joy, natural candid moment of lively Ohangla dancing, medium shot capturing dynamic poses."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 3.10124871134758, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are the best vegetarian Luo dishes available in Migori that support blood sugar control for someone with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can a young male sorghum farmer in suburban Migori manage high tobacco use while also controlling type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community exercise groups or Ohangla dance events near Migori town that are suitable for beginners and people with diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What culturally relevant methods do Luo communities in Migori use to stay motivated for regular physical activity?\\",\\n  \\"How does regular Ohangla dancing help lower blood sugar levels for active young adults with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find diabetes-friendly vegetarian food options in Migoriâ€™s local markets or restaurants?\\",\\n  \\"Are there Migori-based community support groups specifically for young men with type 2 diabetes who do not practice religion?\\",\\n  \\"Which lifestyle changes have proven most effective for Luo atheists with diabetes in Kenyan suburban areas?\\",\\n  \\"How does tobacco smoking affect energy levels and exercise motivation in young adults with type 2 diabetes in rural Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"What are the most effective strategies for staying motivated with daily exercise routines for male sorghum farmers in Migori?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any government or NGO programs in Migori focused on supporting youth farmers with diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"How can regular checkups with healthcare providers in Migori help young Luo men maintain consistent exercise and nutrition habits for diabetes?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Relevant persona fields are: Daily routine: Working adult; Type 2 Diabetes status: Yes; Sorghum farmer; Regular healthcare access: Yes, at least once a year; Health goals: Sometimes I feel tired or discouraged—how can I stay motivated, and how does exercise help my blood sugar?; Diet restrictions: Kosher; Support network: Healthcare provider or counsellor; Physical activity: 5-7 days; Hobbies: Ohangla dancing; Smoking and alcohol use; Food access: Easy access to healthy foods.", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "lab