b624c591-60ef-4c26-adea-71e61ff372b4	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b818-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Migori</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Christianity (Anglican)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Odhiambo Okoth</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Male</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">18-24</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Fisher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Ohangla dancing</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Once per month (weekends/festivals)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D â€” Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">b624c591-60ef-4c26-adea-71e61ff372b4</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gymâ€”what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up early like every day, before the sun even shows. I go to my little shop in Migori town — selling fish and fresh vegetables. My hands are always busy, my feet are tired. I don’t think much about my body — just how much fish I can catch, how many customers I can serve. But one day, I felt weak. My legs didn’t move right. I thought, ‘Is this just tiredness?’ I didn’t know it was my body telling me something. I just kept working. I didn’t stop. What if I could just walk? What if walking helps me do better at work? I don’t know. Maybe I’m too busy to care.\n\nThen one Sunday, I went to the local clinic. A nurse, Miss Wanjiru, looked at me and said, ‘Odhiambo, your sugar is high. You need to move more. Not just walk — but move in a way that feels good, not like a punishment.’ I said, ‘But I don’t have time. I have to sell fish every day.’ She smiled and said, ‘You don’t need a gym. You just need to walk with your fish basket — walk while you carry it. Even 10 minutes a day. That’s enough.’ I didn’t believe her at first. I thought, ‘Can walking really help me sell more fish?’ But she said, ‘Yes. Your body will feel strong. And strong people work better.’\n\nI tried it. I walked with my fish basket from the shop to the market. I walked to the river, then back. I felt tired. My legs hurt. I didn’t like it. I thought, ‘Why should I walk when I can just rest?’ Then I remembered — next week, I have to carry fish to the big festival in the village. The festival is big. Many people come. I have to carry the fish, and I have to dance with the Ohangla music. I said to myself, ‘If I don’t feel strong, I won’t be able to dance well. I won’t be able to carry the fish properly.’ So I started walking again. I did it slowly. I did it every day. I didn’t do it perfectly, but I kept going.\n\nNow, I walk every morning. I walk with my fish basket, and I listen to the Ohangla music. My legs feel stronger. I can carry more fish. I can dance better at the festival. At the festival, people said, ‘Odhiambo, you moved like a man with power.’ I smiled. I didn’t think I could do it. But I did. Now I know — walking is not just for health. It’s for work. It’s for life. And I know I can do more. I can keep walking. I can keep being strong. I can even teach others how to walk with joy.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b624c591-60ef-4c26-adea-71e61ff372b4_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b624c591-60ef-4c26-adea-71e61ff372b4_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b624c591-60ef-4c26-adea-71e61ff372b4_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b624c591-60ef-4c26-adea-71e61ff372b4_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b624c591-60ef-4c26-adea-71e61ff372b4_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b624c591-60ef-4c26-adea-71e61ff372b4_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b624c591-60ef-4c26-adea-71e61ff372b4_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b624c591-60ef-4c26-adea-71e61ff372b4_3.mp3}	Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?	exercise	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:20:06.32948+00	{"label": "GOOD", "model": "Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Akinyi Odhiambo is a 55-64 year old, \\nCulture: Luo female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Journalist, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Kisumu. Disability: she has none. Religion: Christianity (African Independent Churches). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling. Activities: Socialising with family or friends. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at lea