cing with my need to increase physical activity as a young male civil servant in Kisumu?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community or Methodist church programs in Kisumu that support young adults with type 2 diabetes in managing diet and exercise?\\",\\n  \\"What are smart grocery shopping tips to help young professionals in Kenyan suburban areas like Kisumu eat healthy on a budget?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find local markets or vendors in Kisumu with the best prices for fresh, healthy, diabetes-friendly foods?\\",\\n  \\"How can I modify favorite Luo dishes to be lactose-free and suitable for diabetes management while still retaining traditional flavors?\\",\\n  \\"Is smoking common among young Luo males in Kisumu, and what support exists locally for those trying to reduce tobacco use due to diabetes risks?\\",\\n  \\"Can I participate safely in ohangla dance sessions with type 2 diabetes, and are there recommendations for beginners with low current physical activity?\\",\\n  \\"What are popular, easy-to-cook, healthy meals for young working adults in Kisumu who need to avoid lactose and manage diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any government or health initiatives in Kisumu providing nutrition education or subsidized healthy foods to young civil servants?\\",\\n  \\"How do young Christians (Methodist) in Kisumu integrate their faith and community support into managing chronic health conditions like diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local Luo herbal or traditional remedies for diabetes that are safe to use alongside medical treatments, and what do clinics in Kisumu say about them?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Relevant persona fields: Daily routine (Working adult), Type 2 Diabetes status (Yes), Currently taking Medication (Insulin injections, Oral medication, Herbal medicine), Physical activity (0 days), Support network (Community or religious group), Health goals (Eating healthy on a tight budget, enjoying traditional foods), Health resources accessed (Local healthcare clinic), 