uld you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Civil servant</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Ohangla dancing</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Anxiety or depression</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Gluten-Free</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">250d2031-1d17-4575-b885-53dea381bdd4</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gymâ€”what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Owiti, and I live in Khayelitsha, you know, near the big mall? I work at the spaza shop, selling sweets and chips. It’s alright work, keeps me busy. Most days, I just grab a packet of biscuits and a bottle of cold Red – that’s my lunch. Sometimes, if I’m really hungry, I’ll buy a big chicken neck from the butcher. It’s cheap, and it fills me up. I don't really think about food much, just what tastes good, right? I mean, what’s the point of eating healthy when you’re just trying to get through the day, eh?\n\nYesterday, Mr. Dlamini, he’s the boss at the warehouse where I’m helping out this week, he asked me to sort through all the boxes of fruit. Said it was important for the new juice company. I was tired, see? Just finished my shift at the shop, and I was feeling a bit sluggish. I figured I’d grab a quick snack – a banana and a handful of peanuts – and get it done. But, I tripped! Right in the middle of the boxes. I spilled everything everywhere, and Mr. Dlamini was really cross. He said I wasn't paying attention, and that I needed to be more careful. It made me feel bad, I tell you.\n\nDr. Mbeki, she works at the clinic down the road, she told me something interesting. She said that eating properly, even just a few fruits and vegetables a day, could help me feel better and work faster. She gave me a little booklet with some easy recipes – things like a salad with tomatoes and lettuce, or a stew with potatoes and beans. She said it’s important to drink plenty of water too, not just the Red. It sounded a bit complicated, to be honest. I thought, ‘How am I supposed to change my whole life just because of a doctor’s advice?’ But Mr. Dlamini’s face kept popping into my head, and I figured, maybe she was right.\n\nI tried making a salad with some tomatoes I bought from the market. It wasn’t bad, actually! And I even had a small bowl of beans for dinner. It took a few tries, and I still sometimes crave a packet of chips, but I’m feeling much better. I have more energy, and I’m not as tired at the end of the day. Sorting those fruit boxes today was easy, I didn't even spill a single one. Mr. Dlamini smiled at me, and it felt good. I think I’m starting to understand that looking after myself is important, not just for work, but for everything.  Maybe I’ll even try to dance a little more at the shebeens, eh?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/250d2031-1d17-4575-b885-53dea381bdd4_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/250d2031-1d17-4575-b885-53dea381bdd4_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/250d2031-1d17-4575-b885-53dea381bdd4_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/250d2031-1d17-4575-b885-53dea381bdd4_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/250d2031-1d17-4575-b885-53dea381bdd4_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/250d2031-1d17-4575-b885-53dea381bdd4_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/250d2031-1d17-4575-b885-53dea381bdd4_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/250d2031-1d17-4575-b885-53dea381bdd4_3.mp3}	Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?	diet	male	control	2026-03-23 13:20:01.87679+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gemma-3-4b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Akinyi Odhiambo is a 55-64 year old, \\nCulture: Luo female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Public health officer, lives in a Suburban (near city or town) in Kisumu. Disability: she has none. Religion: Christianity (Zion Christian Church). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Ohangla dancing. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication). Regular healthcare access: Yes. how 