ad, actually.’  The sound of a rhythmic, gentle beat – perhaps a distant shebeen song."], "image_prompts": ["Medium shot of Owiti Odhiambo, a young man with a slightly weary expression, standing in front of a brightly colored spaza shop in Khayelitsha. He’s holding a packet of biscuits and a bottle of Red, looking thoughtfully at the camera. The background shows other people browsing the shop. Warm, slightly hazy lighting.", "Wide shot of Owiti Odhiambo, mid-fall, surrounded by a chaotic pile of fruit boxes in a warehouse. He’s sprawled on the floor, looking embarrassed and slightly frustrated, with a spilled banana beside him. The warehouse is dimly lit, with crates stacked high in the background.  A concerned-looking man, Mr. Dlamini, stands nearby.", "Medium shot of Dr. Mbeki, a kind-faced woman in a white clinic coat, handing Owiti Odhiambo a small booklet. Owiti looks at the booklet with a hesitant expression, a slight frown on his face. The clinic is clean and brightly lit, with plants in the corner.  A subtle feeling of hopefulness.", "Close-up of Owiti Odhiambo, smiling slightly, holding a bowl of salad with tomatoes and lettuce. He’s sitting at a small table in his small apartment, sunlight streaming through the window. A simple, slightly worn wooden table and chair are visible in the background."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 9.96361825405023, "task_parent_id": "05f4300b-7644-4839-b768-46db602273bd", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some effective home-based exercise routines suitable for a young male civil servant living in urban Homa Bay, Kenya who has type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any Luo cultural activities or dances similar to Ohangla that can help me stay physically active at home?\\",\\n  \\"Which everyday household items common in urban Kenyan homes in Homa Bay can I safely use for resistance training or workouts?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best foods available in Homa Bay's urban markets for managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How do Luo dietary traditions align with recommendations for type 2 diabetes, and are there local dishes I should focus on or avoid?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community-based support groups or exercise groups in Homa Bay for young adults managing anxiety, depression, and diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What resources are available through local clinics in Homa Bay for civil servants with diabetes looking for mental health and counseling support?\\",\\n  \\"Given my high alcohol consumption, what are the specific risks for type 2 diabetes and mental health in the Luo community of urban Homa Bay?\\",\\n  \\"Are there online or app-based exercise programs popular in Kenya that don't require gym equipment and are suitable for my age and health needs?\\",\\n  \\"How can I incorporate Ohangla dancing routines as a regular cardio workout at home to help manage my diabetes and stress levels?\\",\\n  \\"What government or employer wellness programs exist for civil servants in Homa Bay to support regular physical activity and mental health?\\",\\n  \\"How can I balance my job as a civil servant, my cultural activities, and regular exercise without access to a gym in a typical Homa Bay city environment?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": ["city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "tobacco", "alcohol", "diet_restrictions", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
fea1f284-6e43-4c7f-9ad3-cba8e07d8f67	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b818-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kisumu</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Atheism</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Achieng Onyango</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Female</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">35-44</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Fish processor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Ohangla dancing</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D â€” Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">fea1f284-6e43-4c7f-9ad3-cba8e07d8f67</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Ai, life, isn't it something? I'm Achieng, and I work down at the fish market in Kisumu. Every morning, bright and early, I’m sorting tilapia, making sure the best ones go to the restaurants. It's hard work, you know? Standing on your feet all day, lifting those heavy crates… but it pays the bills. I usually grab a mandazi and strong chai to start the day. Gives you a quick boost, right? Today though, oh lord, today was a mess. I had to sort a whole extra crate of omena, tiny little fish, and halfway through, my head started swimming, my hands felt shaky. I had to sit down, and old man Omondi had to finish my work! Shameful, really. I just thought I was tired. But maybe… maybe it wasn’t just tiredness?\n\nOld Man Omondi, he’s a wise one. He told me I needed to go see Nurse Akinyi at the clinic. 'Achieng,' he said, 'you're working too hard on an empty tank.' I was a bit stubborn, I admit. I thought, what does a nurse know about sorting fish? But he insisted. Nurse Akinyi was kind, she asked me about what I eat, how I feel. She explained about sugar, how too much sweet things can make you weak and tired. She said the mandazi and chai, lovely as they are, can cause trouble. She suggested swapping the mandazi for some boiled sweet potatoes and a little bit of grilled fish. And to drink water, lots of water! 'Small changes, Achieng,' she said,'small changes can make a big difference.' It sounded… doable, I suppose.\n\nTrying to change things is harder than it sounds, let me tell you. The first morning with sweet potatoes, I missed my mandazi something fierce! It just didn't feel right. I almost gave up and ran for one, but then I remembered the big order coming next week - a whole shipment of Nile perch for a wedding. If I'm weak and shaky, I won’t be able to handle it. So I forced myself to eat the sweet potatoes, and they weren't *that* bad, especially with a little bit of salt. But by mid-morning, I was craving something sweet again. I had a small piece of mango, Nurse Akinyi said a little fruit was okay. It helped, a little. It’s a struggle, but I have to think about that perch!\n\nSlowly, slowly, things started to get better. I started drinking water with every meal, and I found I didn’t crave the chai as much. The sweet potatoes actually started to taste good, especially with some greens. And you know what? I sorted that Nile perch shipment, and I didn't even feel tired! I worked the whole day, and my hands didn’t shake, my head didn't swim. Old Man Omondi even gave me a smile and said, 'See, Achieng? I told you.' It feels good, this feeling of strength. I think… I think maybe Nurse Akinyi was right. Maybe small changes really *can* make a big difference. I’m even thinking about trying to learn some new recipes, healthier ones, you know? This is just the beginning, I think.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fea1f284-6e43-4c7f-9ad3-cba8e07d8f67_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fea1f284-6e43-4c7f-9ad3-cba8e07d8f67_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fea1f284-6e43-4c7f-9ad3-cba8e07d8f67_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fea1f284-6e43-4c7f-9ad3-cba8e07d8f67_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fea1f284-6e43-4c7f-9ad3-cba8e07d8f67_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fea1f284-6e43-4c7f-9ad3-cba8e07d8f67_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fea1f284-6e43-4c7f-9ad3-cba8e07d8f67_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fea1f284-6e43-4c7f-9ad3-cba8e07d8f67_3.mp3}	Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?	diet	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:20:04.670672+00	{"label": "GOOD", "model": "gemma-3-27b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: David Otieno is a 25-34 year old, \\nCulture: Luo male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Medical doctor, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Siaya. Disability: he has none. Religion: Christianity (Anglican). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Ohangla dancing. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication). Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: None. Diet restrictions: Lactose-free. Smoking: No. Alcohol drinking: Yes. Physical activity: 5-7 days. Support network: Close friends. Health goals: Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?. his food access Easy access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of David Otieno and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in English that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken English, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in English.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in English.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "iteration", "audio_prompts": ["Achieng Onyango, 36, sighs heavily as she speaks, her voice slightly breathless from exertion. The sound of a bustling fish market fills the background – shouting vendors, the flapping of fish, the clatter of crates. 'Ai, this tiredness… it just comes and goes. I don't understand it.' Her voice trails off, filled with a hint of frustration. A distant radio plays faint Ohangla music.", "Nurse Akinyi, 40, speaks with a calm, reassuring tone, nearby Achieng Onyango. 'Now, Achieng, it's important to understand how food affects your energy levels.' Her voice is clear and professional, with a gentle cadence. Achieng responds with a hesitant, slightly questioning tone, 'But… I’ve always eaten like this. Is it really that bad?' The sounds of a quiet clinic environment, faint beeping of medical equipment, are present.", "Achieng Onyango, 40, mutters under her breath, her voice laced with a slight grumble. 'Sweet potatoes… honestly.' She pauses, a distinct chewing sound, then a sigh. 'It’s just… not the same.' The sound of a pot boiling in the background, and faint chatter from neighbors can be heard. She takes a deep, slightly resigned breath.", "Achieng Onyango, 43, speaks with a newfound energy and confidence, her voice clear and strong. 'You know, I actually feel good today!' The sounds of a busy fish market are present, but Achieng's voice cuts through the noise. She laughs, a genuine and hearty sound, then continues, 'Old Man Omondi was impressed! Maybe this healthy eating thing isn’t so bad after all.'"], "image_prompts": ["Achieng Onyango, 38, sits on a wooden stool amongst crates of silver-colored tilapia at a bustling fish market in Kisumu, Kenya. She looks slightly slumped, hand resting on her forehead, eyes closed, with a half-eaten mandazi in her other hand. The background is filled with people moving, sunlight filtering through a corrugated iron roof, creating strong shadows. Focus on the texture of the fish scales and the worn wood.", "Medium shot of Achieng Onyango, 39, sitting opposite Nurse Akinyi, 40, in a brightly lit but simple clinic room in Kisumu. Achieng is leaning forward slightly, listening intently with a questioning expression. Nurse Akinyi is gesturing with a pen, a chart visible on the table between them. The room has pale green walls and basic medical posters. Achieng’s face shows a mix of uncertainty and curiosity.", "Achieng Onyango, 41, stands in her small kitchen, looking slightly frustrated as she stares at a plate of boiled sweet potatoes. The kitchen is simply furnished, with worn linoleum flooring and metal shelves. A half-eaten mango sits on the counter. She's holding a fork loosely, her shoulders slightly hunched. Soft morning light streams through a small window.", "Wide shot of Achieng Onyango, 42, confidently sorting a large pile of Nile perch at the fish market in Kisumu. She is standing tall, with a determined expression, efficiently packing the fish into crates. Old Man Omondi, 65, is visible in the background, smiling at her. The scene is filled with activity, but Achieng appears focused and energized. The lighting is bright and vibrant."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 83.03575225976797, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some easy vegetarian meal ideas suitable for a Luo woman with type 2 diabetes living in Kisumu city?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find local urban Kisumu markets that sell fresh, healthy vegetarian foods suitable for diabetes and hypertension management?\\",\\n  \\"Are there sample daily menus or meal plans for Luo women over 35 with high blood pressure and type 2 diabetes, emphasizing vegetarian options?\\",\\n  \\"Which local Luo dishes or Kisumu city foods can be adapted to be vegetarian and diabetic-friendly?\\",\\n  \\"What are common physical activity groups or exercise classes, like Ohangla dancing, available for women in Kisumu city?\\",\\n  \\"How can I balance a vegetarian diet with high protein needs as a fish processor in urban Kisumu, while managing type 2 diabetes and blood pressure?\\",\\n  \\"Are there support networks or resources in Kisumu for working women living alone with diabetes who want to maintain a vegetarian diet?\\",\\n  \\"Is it safe to use herbal or traditional Luo medicine alongside insulin and oral medications for diabetes and hypertension in Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"What are the effects of high alcohol consumption on women with type 2 diabetes and hypertension, and are ther