 Warm, natural lighting.", "Achieng Onyango, 60s, is walking slowly along a dirt path between rows of sugarcane, looking determined but slightly out of breath. Her hand is on her side, and her face shows a mix of effort and resolve. The sun is beating down, and the scene is dusty and warm. Achieng's worn farming shoes are visible in the foreground. Wide shot, showing the vastness of the sugarcane field.", "Achieng Onyango, 60s, is smiling broadly while working alongside her daughter, Atieno, 20s, in the sugarcane field during harvest. They are both cutting sugarcane with machetes, their movements coordinated and efficient. The scene is filled with energy and laughter. Warm, golden hour lighting. Medium shot, capturing their joyful interaction."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 83.03575225976797, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some culturally appropriate home exercises for a 55-64 year-old Luo woman living in urban Kisumu with type 2 diabetes and hypertension?\\",\\n  \\"How can sugarcane farmers in Kisumu manage physical activity safely when they have high blood pressure and diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What traditional Luo foods can support healthy blood pressure and blood sugar levels for someone who already has easy access to healthy foods in Kisumu?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community-based exercise groups or walking clubs for older women in Kisumu, especially those following a Christian (ZCC) faith?\\",\\n  \\"What are safe, daily farm activities or chores for someone managing both hypertension and diabetes, without requiring gym equipment?\\",\\n  \\"Which herbal or traditional medicines are commonly used by Luo people in Kisumu for diabetes or blood pressure, and are they effective?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local programs in Kisumu offering free or low-cost diabetes management support for urban farmers?\\",\\n  \\"How effective are household objects (like water jugs or sacks) as alternatives for strength training exercises at home in a Kenyan urban setting?\\",\\n  \\"What resources do local healthcare clinics in Kisumu provide for exercise routines or group activities tailored to older women with diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can a woman from the Zion Christian Church in urban Luo communities stay motivated to exercise alone at home?\\",\\n  \\"What risks should I consider if I smoke tobacco rarely while managing diabetes and hypertension in Kisumu city?\\",\\n  \\"What lifestyle changes beyond medication are recommended for older Luo women with type 2 diabetes in urban Kenya?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
