e Luo community integrate faith and social activities to support diabetes self-care?\\",\\n  \\"Which board games or social activities are popular among Luo men aged 65+ in Homa Bay for staying mentally and socially active?\\",\\n  \\"What resources are available in Homa Bay for elderly vegans to easily access healthy, affordable foods suitable for diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What is the prevalence of type 2 diabetes among Luo men in Homa Bay, and how do most retirees manage it without a strong support network?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local events or organizations in Homa Bay focused on diabetes education and community support for seniors?\\",\\n  \\"How can someone with no tobacco or alcohol consumption optimize their lifestyle changes for diabetes in a suburban Luo community?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
cab6162a-60c2-43f4-8ab0-f65a9e973a33	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b818-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Homa Bay</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Christianity (Zion Christian Church)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Achieng Odinga</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Female</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">35-44</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Subsistence farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Farming and animal keeping</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D â€” Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Lactose-free</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">cab6162a-60c2-43f4-8ab0-f65a9e973a33</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I like to snackâ€”what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I’m Achieng, and I wake up early like every day, before the sun is high. I go to my farm, feed the goats, and plant maize. I work till midday, then go back to the house to cook. I eat my meals at the right time—breakfast, lunch, dinner. But sometimes, when the sun goes down, I feel tired. My body is weak, and I just want something to eat. So I eat a piece of bread with a bit of milk. I don’t think about it much—just ‘I’m hungry, so I eat’. But I wonder… if I eat late at night, will my body get sick? Will my sugar go up? I don’t know. I just eat. And last week, I forgot to check my blood sugar after eating late. My son said I looked tired and my hands were shaky. I thought, ‘Oh, it’s just tiredness’. But then I saw the nurse at the clinic, and she said, ‘Achieng, your sugar is high’. I didn’t understand. I just said, ‘I didn’t mean to eat late’. But she said, ‘You did. And that’s dangerous’. I felt bad. I didn’t know it could hurt me. That night, I tried to stop, but I was too tired. The next day, I went to the farm again, and I forgot to take my insulin. I felt weak. I just wanted to rest. I didn’t know what to do. That’s when I thought—maybe I need to change how I eat, not just when I eat.\n\nSo I went to the clinic the next week. I saw Sister Nalwoga, a kind woman with glasses and a warm smile. She said, ‘Achieng, you’re doing good work, but your body is telling you something. Eating late at night makes your sugar go up, and it can hurt your health’. I said, ‘But I’m just tired, and I don’t have time to plan’. She said, ‘No, you don’t have to plan. Just eat before you go to bed. And if you’re hungry, eat something small and healthy’. She gave me a list—like boiled beans, a piece of banana, or a slice of banana with a spoon of honey. She said, ‘No sugar, no milk, no fried food’. I said, ‘But I don’t have those things’. She said, ‘You do. You have maize, you have beans, you have vegetables. Just cook them simple’. She said, ‘And if you eat late, just eat a small snack, not a big meal’. I said, ‘I can try’. I didn’t believe it would work. But she said, ‘You’ve got a strong heart. You’ve worked hard. You can do this’. I felt hopeful. I thought, ‘Maybe I can change’. So I said, ‘Yes, I will try’. I told my brother, and he said, ‘Good, Achieng. You’re doing the right thing’.\n\nI tried the next day. I cooked a small bowl of boiled beans and a piece of banana. I ate it before bed. I felt better. But the next day, I was tired, and I thought, ‘I’ll just eat a piece of bread with a bit of milk’. I didn’t want to change. I felt lazy. My hands were shaky again. I didn’t take my insulin on time. I felt weak. I looked at my son and he said, ‘Mama, you look tired’. I said, ‘I just need a little food’. But I knew I was making a mistake. I remembered Sister Nalwoga’s words. I thought, ‘I can’t keep doing this’. So I said to myself, ‘I must go to the church meeting tomorrow’. The church is where we plan for the next season. We grow maize and beans together. I said, ‘I will bring a small pot of boiled beans to share’. I didn’t think it would help. But I knew—this is my chance. If I do it right, maybe I can grow healthy food for the whole group. I will show them how to cook simple, healthy meals. I will prove that eating late at night is not okay. I will do it for my family, for my health, and for the next season of farming.\n\nNow, I eat before bed. I cook a small bowl of boiled beans or a piece of banana. I don’t eat late. I feel strong. My hands don’t shake. I check my blood sugar every morning and every night. I tell my son and brother. I share with the group at church. Last week, we planted a new garden. I taught the women how to cook healthy snacks. I said, ‘You can eat boiled beans, or a banana, or a piece of sweet potato with a little oil’. They all said, ‘Yes, Achieng, that’s good’. I felt proud. I didn’t just fix my body—I helped others. I know I can keep going. I still eat sometimes, but now I know when and what. I don’t feel weak. I feel strong. I feel like I am protecting my health, my family, and my work. I know I can do more. And I will. Because I believe in God, and I believe in my body. And I believe in small changes that lead to big things.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/cab6162a-60c2-43f4-8ab0-f65a9e973a33_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/cab6162a-60c2-43f4-8ab0-f65a9e973a33_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/cab6162a-60c2-43f4-8ab0-f65a9e973a33_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/cab6162a-60c2-43f4-8ab0-f65a9e973a33_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/cab6162a-60c2-43f4-8ab0-f65a9e973a33_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/cab6162a-60c2-43f4-8ab0-f65a9e973a33_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/cab6162a-60c2-43f4-8ab0-f65a9e973a33_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/cab6162a-60c2-43f4-8ab0-f65a9e973a33_3.mp3}	I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? 	diet	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:20:07.26569+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Akinyi Odhiambo is a 55-64 year old, \\nCulture: Luo female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Fish processor, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Kisumu. Disability: she has none. Religion: Christianity (other). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Ohangla dancing. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Lo