8541e3fe-3889-4787-a476-e8eb1956e74c	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b819-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hausa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kano</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Islam</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Aminu Bello</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Male</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">35-44</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Trader</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Football (soccer)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Occasionally (less than once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">8541e3fe-3889-4787-a476-e8eb1956e74c</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every day for me, Aminu Bello, is early rising and rushing to the Sabon Gari market, hoping today’s trade will go well. Wallahi, as a trader in Kano, you know the bustle does not wait for anybody. Sometimes, work makes me eat late—maybe tuwo shinkafa with a quick splash of soup after I close, tired and thinking, ‘If I miss food, how will I get the strength for tomorrow?’ I remember one night last week, I stayed till late counting my money, ate my heavy food close to midnight, and drifted off to sleep. The next morning, my body was heavy, my head spun, and my sugar shot up. I couldn’t open my stall in time and lost some early customers. Can you imagine how just one meal at the wrong time can spoil business?\n\nNot long after, at the health clinic near my mosque, I met Nurse Aisha during my insulin refill. She asked about my meal times, and I laughed it off, ‘Business is busy, nurse, man must hustle!’ She shook her head, ‘Aminu, late eating can push your blood sugar up overnight and make you weak. Try to eat your main meal by Maghrib, two hours before sleep, and keep some fruit or water if hunger comes late. This will help your insulin work and give you energy for trading. You want to win at the next big Sallah market, ba?’ Her advice was simple, like advice from a big sister I wish I had listened to earlier.\n\nThat night, I did my best to close shop early. The smell of masa at the roadside tempted me, but I reached home and ate rice and fresh ugu stew before the call for Isha prayer. The first days were not easy. Sometimes I felt hunger while packing up goods or watching football highlights at home. One time, I almost grabbed a late suya stick, but then I remembered I still had a larger order to supply next week—how will I do that if I am sick now? I forced myself to try fruits or just drink water if night hunger talked too much.\n\nTwo weeks later, I felt lighter when waking up, and my mornings carried less dizziness. That big order from the electronics dealer came, and, walahi, I finished it without missing a customer. My sugar stayed steady, and I found I could join my friends for an early football game on the weekend. Seeing how these small changes made my big work go easier, I now want to learn even more ways to keep strong and healthy. Maybe good health, like good trade, grows bit by bit if you do the right thing every day.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/8541e3fe-3889-4787-a476-e8eb1956e74c_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/8541e3fe-3889-4787-a476-e8eb1956e74c_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/8541e3fe-3889-4787-a476-e8eb1956e74c_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/8541e3fe-3889-4787-a476-e8eb1956e74c_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/8541e3fe-3889-4787-a476-e8eb1956e74c_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/8541e3fe-3889-4787-a476-e8eb1956e74c_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/8541e3fe-3889-4787-a476-e8eb1956e74c_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/8541e3fe-3889-4787-a476-e8eb1956e74c_3.mp3}	I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? 	diet	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:29:33.572235+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "gpt-4.1", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Chinonso Okafor is a 18-24 year old, \\nCulture: Hausa male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Trader, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Kano. Disability: he has none. Religion: Islam. Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Traditional wrestling. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: Anxiety or depression. Diet restrictions: Halal. Smoking: No. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical acti