just water, Aminu, be patient, tomorrow is another busy day…’ His words are interrupted by a stomach growl, the sound of cutlery, and a distant suya seller’s call. He closes with a resolute, ‘Insha Allah,’ voice steadier now.", "Early morning atmosphere: Chirping birds, faint calls to prayer in the background, laughter from men warming up. Aminu Bello, breathing easily, voice warm and lively, joking with friends after stretching: ‘Today’s energy is better, wallahi, I’ll score two goals!’ Friends nearby respond with supportive shouts, their words blending naturally. Aminu’s voice is clear, confident, with laughter that fades into happy chatter echoing on the open field."], "image_prompts": ["Candid, medium shot of Aminu Bello, a Hausa man in his late 30s, sitting on a worn concrete bench under the dull yellow lighting of Sabon Gari market at night. Aminu is hunched forward, fatigue evident in his slouched shoulders, his face shadowed and eyes half-closed as he eats a plate of tuwo shinkafa and miyan kuka from a simple plastic container on his lap. Nearby, his small market stall with stacks of goods is barely visible in the background, highlighting the late trading hour. The scene texture includes the reddish dust on his trousers, the faded fabric of his shirt, and the ambient clatter of other traders packing up.", "Aisha, a friendly female nurse in a crisp white hijab, stands beside Aminu Bello in a brightly lit hospital corridor. Medium shot, candid and unposed: Aminu, holding his medication bag, rests his hand uncertainly on his hip while Aisha gestures warmly with a pen, smiling reassuringly. Aminu’s eyebrows are slightly raised, showing mild resistance but engagement. The clinic’s tiled walls and waiting bench with a poster about healthy eating are visible behind them.", "Candid, medium shot of Aminu Bello at home, illuminated by the overhead bulb and moonlight through the window. Aminu stands near his small kitchen counter, one hand covering his mouth in hesitation, facing a covered plate of rice and fresh ugu stew set on a plain table. Beside him, his phone screen shows a football highlight paused. His posture is upright but tense, with his free hand gripping his market apron—body facing the food but eyes tempted toward the open window and sounds of a suya vendor outside.", "Wide shot, candid outdoor photo of Aminu Bello on an asphalt football pitch at dawn. Aminu, energized, stretches his arms above his head after a light warm-up; he’s laughing, body open and relaxed, with his market friends in the background setting down plastic water bottles and sports bags. The city skyline and minaret are visible, bathed in soft blue morning light, reflecting hope and new beginnings. Aminu’s face glows with relief and confidence."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 1.9408850491046905, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are the best exercise routines for men aged 35-44 with hypertension and type 2 diabetes living in urban Kano, Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find affordable, healthy, and kosher food options suitable for someone with hypertension and diabetes in Kano city?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any local Hausa community support groups in Kano that help men manage diabetes and hypertension?\\",\\n  \\"How does alcohol consumption, even rarely, affect diabetes and blood pressure for middle-aged men in northern Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"What is the typical availability of insulin injections and oral diabetes medication in Kanoâ€™s healthcare clinics?\\",\\n  \\"Which traditional Hausa herbal medicines are commonly used for hypertension or diabetes, and are they safe to use with my current medications?\\",\\n  \\"Are there football (soccer) clubs or exercise groups in Kano for adults who need to balance fitness with health conditions like hypertension and diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What recommendations do Islamic scholars in Kano offer for fasting during Ra