 Bay that are suitable for someone managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How does Ohangla dancing as a form of exercise impact blood sugar control for people with type 2 diabetes in Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"Are there support groups for Muslim women with diabetes in the Homa Bay region?\\",\\n  \\"What locally available traditional Luo herbal remedies are used alongside modern medication for diabetes by suburban sorghum farmers?\\",\\n  \\"How can I stay motivated to exercise regularly as a young female sorghum farmer with limited support in suburban Homa Bay?\\",\\n  \\"What are safe strategies for moderate alcohol consumption on a weekly basis for Muslims with type 2 diabetes in Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"Which physical activities are most popular or effective for women aged 25-34 in Homa Bay dealing with diabetes and following a vegan diet?\\",\\n  \\"What resources or programs exist in Homa Bay for diabetes management specifically tailored to Luo women living alone?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local exercise groups or fitness events near Homa Bay town that accommodate Muslims and promote social connection?\\",\\n  \\"How does access to healthy foods in suburban Kenya affect diabetes management choices for vegan women farmers?\\",\\n  \\"What role does regular attendance at a local healthcare clinic in Homa Bay play in controlling blood sugar for residents with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How do other young, urban-adjacent women in the Luo community overcome feelings of discouragement while managing diabetes?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Relevant persona fields: Daily routine as a working adult; physically active as a sorghum farmer; lives alone or with limited support; experiences tiredness and needs motivation; has type 2 diabetes and takes insulin, oral medication, and sometimes herbal remedies; follows Halal diet; lives in suburban Homa Bay with easy access to healthy foods; limited health knowledge about exercise for blood sugar and no formal gym access.", "selected_profile_in