6b42dfc9-1ef1-46aa-9cd2-6d22c51ddef8	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b816-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Eastern Cape</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Atheism</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Sibongile Mvula</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Female</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">45–54</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Rural (small community or countryside)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Limited access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Civil servant</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Traditional dancing (e.g. umxhentso, intlombe)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5–7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">6b42dfc9-1ef1-46aa-9cd2-6d22c51ddef8</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	One morning, I tried to quickly pack little snack boxes for the crèche before heading to a dance practice. I made homemade pap with cheap cabbage and onions, but before we finished, I felt dizzy. Did I skip my insulin? Was it the heat, or did I not eat enough? I thought I knew how to look after myself, but I keep thinking, how does eating right matter when you’re moving non-stop? Hearing a child ask for a sandwich, I almost laughed—how am I supposed to afford bread for myself, let alone extras? When I sat down to rest, the small task wasn’t finished. The kids went without snacks, and I felt like I’d failed them.\n\nLater that week, Sister Dudu, our local clinic nurse, noticed I wasn’t myself at the taxi rank. She greeted me, ‘Sibongile, you’re so quiet today, is everything all right?’ I shrugged. ‘Eating healthy is too expensive, nurse. And I’m tired!’ She listened and told me that even with little money, I could make healthy choices at home—like mabele porridge instead of pap, using tinned beans and fresh tomatoes, lots of water, and adding amadumbe or sweet potatoes if I can find them. She said, ‘It’s not about fancy food, just balancing what you have. And you can still cook your traditional dishes, just use less oil and salt. Small changes, Sibongile.’ Eish, could it be that simple?\n\nThe next days, I tried her ideas. I boiled amadumbe with spices and made a big pot of vegetable stew. But let me tell you, my body wanted bread and fried things, the way I used to make. I got tired and nearly gave up. Still, there was a big crèche event coming—a cultural dancing day for the kids—and I wanted to be strong for my dancing, and to prepare enough for everyone. Every time I felt like eating amagwinya, I remembered the nurse’s words. I slipped once, buying a vetkoek from Auntie Zanele, but I reminded myself, change is hard. Ek se, won’t life reward me if I just keep going?\n\nSlowly, things began to get easier. I started feeling lighter. My energy lasted through umxhentso practice and I finished all the snacks for the big event, this time with bean stew, carrot sticks, and slices of fruit I got from the hawker. Seeing the kids smile and sharing my food with them made my heart happy. I even taught them a dance! Now, I’m thinking—maybe I really can keep eating better and feeling good, even with little money. Who would have thought a clinic nurse’s simple advice would help me so much?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6b42dfc9-1ef1-46aa-9cd2-6d22c51ddef8_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6b42dfc9-1ef1-46aa-9cd2-6d22c51ddef8_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6b42dfc9-1ef1-46aa-9cd2-6d22c51ddef8_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6b42dfc9-1ef1-46aa-9cd2-6d22c51ddef8_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6b42dfc9-1ef1-46aa-9cd2-6d22c51ddef8_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6b42dfc9-1ef1-46aa-9cd2-6d22c51ddef8_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6b42dfc9-1ef1-46aa-9cd2-6d22c51ddef8_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6b42dfc9-1ef1-46aa-9cd2-6d22c51ddef8_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:02:21.203605+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gpt-4.1", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Lwazi Nkosi is a 18–24 year old, \\nCulture: IsiXhosa male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Entrepreneur, lives in a Suburban (near city or town) in Eastern Cape. Disability: he has none. Religion: Agnosticism. Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Traditional dancing (e.g. umxhentso, intlombe). Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Med