ass="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">b404fb12-840f-4753-8581-e1018e031b40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I'm Amahle, a teacher from the Eastern Cape, and I love playing football in my free time. But lately, I've been feeling really tired and sluggish, and I just can't seem to keep up with my students or my teammates. I know I have type 2 diabetes, but I never really thought about how it affects my daily life. I just take my medication and hope for the best. But yesterday, I had a big test to grade, and I just couldn't focus. I kept getting distracted and my blood sugar levels were all over the place. I ended up having to stay up all night to finish the test, and I was exhausted. What's wrong with me, I thought? Why can't I just get my work done like I used to?\n\nI decided to visit my healthcare provider at the local clinic, and she sat me down and explained that my diet and exercise habits were affecting my blood sugar levels. She told me that as a vegan, I need to make sure I'm eating the right foods to keep my blood sugar stable. She gave me a list of foods that are good for me, like brown rice, quinoa, and leafy greens, and told me to avoid sugary drinks and refined carbohydrates. I was a bit resistant at first, I mean, I love my sugary teas and bread, but she explained that it's all about balance and making small changes. She also told me that I need to start exercising more regularly, and that even just walking for 30 minutes a day can make a big difference. But I'm not sure, I thought, can I really do this?\n\nI tried to follow the advice, but it was harder than I thought. I mean, I'm used to eating what I want, when I want, and exercising only when I feel like it. But I knew I had to make a change, especially with the big football tournament coming up. I started by making small changes, like switching to brown rice and taking a short walk after dinner. But then I had a setback, I ate a whole loaf of bread by myself, and my blood sugar levels skyrocketed. I felt so discouraged, but then I remembered what my healthcare provider said, that it's all about balance and making small changes. So I got back on track, and I started to feel a bit better.\n\nIt's been a few weeks now, and I can already see the difference. My blood sugar levels are more stable, and I have more energy. I'm still not perfect, but I'm getting there. And the best part is, I'm starting to enjoy the healthy foods and exercise. I even started a small garden in my backyard, where I grow my own leafy greens and herbs. It's amazing how much of a difference it's made. And with the football tournament coming up, I'm feeling more confident than ever. I know I can do it, and I know that my health is worth it.\n\nI'm so grateful for my healthcare provider's advice, and I'm excited to continue making healthy changes. I realize now that taking care of my health is not just about me, it's about being able to do the things I love, like teaching and playing football. And I know that I can do it, one small step at a time. I'm Amahle, and I'm taking control of my health, one healthy meal and one walk at a time. What's next, I wonder? Maybe I'll start a healthy cooking club at school, or maybe I'll even start a football team for people with diabetes. The possibilities are endless, and I'm excited to see what the future holds.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b404fb12-840f-4753-8581-e1018e031b40_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b404fb12-840f-4753-8581-e1018e031b40_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b404fb12-840f-4753-8581-e1018e031b40_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b404fb12-840f-4753-8581-e1018e031b40_3.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b404fb12-840f-4753-8581-e1018e031b40_4.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b404fb12-840f-4753-8581-e1018e031b40_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b404fb12-840f-4753-8581-e1018e031b40_1.mp3,h