d">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Teacher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Traditional dancing (e.g. umxhentso, intlombe)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3–4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">013706ef-ca82-48a8-864b-eebf3e17ae75</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Sometimes I feel tired or discouraged—how can I stay motivated, and how does exercise help my blood sugar?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Hayi, life is busy, neh? I’m Thandeka, and I work at the taxi rank, selling vetkoek and chips. It's hard work, standing all day, and the smell of the oil… well, it sticks to you. I love my work, it puts food on the table, but lately, I’ve been feeling… sluggish. Like my legs are made of lead after a long day. I usually grab a kota for lunch – quick and easy! – and maybe a cool drink. Last week, Old Man Mkhize asked me to count all the money from the day, a big job he usually does. I was so tired, my head was spinning, and I messed up the counting! He wasn’t happy. He said, 'Thandeka, you need to focus!' But how can I focus when my body feels like it’s fighting me?\n\nI went to the clinic, you know, just to check. Nurse Zanele, she’s a good woman, looked at my file and said, ‘Thandeka, your sugar is a little high.’ Sugar? I thought that was just for sweet things! She explained about how vetkoek and kota, even though they taste good, can make things tricky. She said I needed to eat more greens, more beans, and less oil. 'It doesn’t mean you can’t enjoy your food, just… a little bit different,' she said. She gave me a list of cheap, healthy foods – spinach, lentils, sweet potatoes. Honestly, I was a bit skeptical. Could I really feel better just by changing what I eat? It sounded… difficult.\n\nOkay, so I tried. I really did. I swapped some of the vetkoek dough for mashed sweet potato, hoping to make them a bit healthier. But the first batch? They tasted like… nothing! My customers weren’t impressed. I almost gave up. Then I remembered Old Man Mkhize is trusting me with the end-of-month takings soon. A much bigger job! If I messed that up, I could lose my job. So, I tried again. This time, I mixed the sweet potato with a little butternut squash, and added some spices. Better! Still not perfect, but better. It's hard, changing what you've always done, you know? But I had to try.\n\nSlowly, things started to change. I started adding a side of chakalaka – tomato and bean relish – to the plates. It’s cheap, it’s tasty, and it fills people up. I even started drinking more water instead of those sugary drinks. And you know what? I *felt* better. Not right away, but after a few weeks, my legs didn't ache so much. When I counted Old Man Mkhize’s money at the end of the month, I didn’t make a single mistake! He smiled, a real smile, and said, ‘See, Thandeka? Focus comes with a clear head.’ Maybe Nurse Zanele was right. Maybe eating healthy isn’t just about feeling good, it’s about being able to *do* good, too. I'm still learning, but now I think, maybe, just maybe, I can enjoy my food *and* take care of myself.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/013706ef-ca82-48a8-864b-eebf3e17ae75_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/013706ef-ca82-48a8-864b-eebf3e17ae75_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/013706ef-ca82-48a8-864b-eebf3e17ae75_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/013706ef-ca82-48a8-864b-eebf3e17ae75_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/013706ef-ca82-48a8-864b-eebf3e17ae75_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/013706ef-ca82-48a8-864b-eebf3e17ae75_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/013706ef-ca82-48a8-864b-eebf3e17ae75_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/013706ef-ca82-48a8-864b-eebf3e17ae75_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:02:28.247616+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gemma-3-27b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Akhona Ndlovu is a 45–54 year old, \\nCulture: IsiXhosa female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Teacher, lives in a Urban (city or to