       <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Gluten-Free</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">fdee4a7c-d0db-4cbb-8dd0-89c973419bc6</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Sinethemba, and I’m fifty-eight. I work at the market, selling vegetables. It’s honest work, but it’s tiring, you know? Most days, I eat pap and beans – that’s all I can really afford. Sometimes, if I’ve got a good day, I’ll add a bit of meat, maybe some mielie. It keeps me going. But I don't really think much about *why* I need to be strong, you know? It just… is.  Didn’t always feel this tired, though. I used to love dancing, umxhentso, really get my energy out.  But lately, my legs ache something fierce after just a few stalls. I just brush it off, say it's old age.  Do you think it’s just old age, really?\n\nYesterday, I was helping Mr. Nkosi load his truck – he’s a carpenter, a good man. He needed a strong back to lift a big piece of wood. I tried to help, but my legs just wouldn’t cooperate. I stumbled, and the wood fell, nearly hitting him! Mr. Nkosi was so worried. He said, ‘Sinethemba, you need to take care of yourself. You’re not getting any younger.’  It made me feel a bit silly, I must admit. I just shook my head and mumbled something about being tired. It was a small thing, but it made me realize something. Maybe he was right.  I need to listen to my body, but it's hard, isn't it?\n\nToday, I went to the clinic. It wasn’t fancy, just a small building near the hospital, but the nurse, Miss Zola, was kind. She checked my blood pressure – it was a bit high, she said. She told me about eating healthy, about fruits and vegetables. She said things like, ‘Pap and beans are good, Sinethemba, but you need more colour in your plate.’ She gave me a little booklet with simple recipes – things like spinach and tomato stew, and butternut squash.  It sounded… complicated.  And expensive! I asked her about traditional foods, like umdibi, and she said, ‘You can still have umdibi, but maybe just a little bit, and with a side of something healthy.’ It felt like a lot to think about.  I just nodded and thanked her, feeling a bit lost, to be honest.\n\nI tried making the stew today. It was okay. Not brill