ressing internal thoughts about struggle and persistence.", "Lively sounds of traditional Xhosa music playing, rhythmic clapping and drum beats, Lihle Mthembu and her friend laughing and chatting nearby, both voices bright and joyful, mixed with festive crowd noises softly fading in and out, capturing celebration and confidence."], "image_prompts": ["Lihle Mthembu, a middle-aged isiXhosa female trader, carries heavy boxes early morning outside a busy urban market in the Eastern Cape. Her posture shows slight fatigue and strain, sunlight casting long shadows on the dusty street, with colorful market stalls and bustling pedestrians in the background, medium shot.", "Lihle Mthembu sitting inside a bright and clean local healthcare clinic room, listening attentively to a female nurse (Xhosa, mid-30s), who gently explains exercise options for diabetes. Natural light filters through a window, soft textures of the clinic walls, both showing calm and focused expressions, medium shot.", "Lihle Mthembu walking slowly on a quiet sidewalk in her urban neighborhood, pausing with a hand on her chest, catching her breath after a light exercise session. Surrounding environment shows small shops and paved streets with late afternoon golden light, reflecting a mix of tiredness and determination on her face, medium shot.", "Lihle Mthembu joyfully dancing traditional umxhentso steps with a younger female friend (mid-20s) at a community festival in an open urban square. Both wear colorful traditional attire, smiling and moving with lively energy under bright daylight, festive crowd blurred in the background, wide shot."], "language_code": "en-ZA", "avg_time_taken": 5.38300901055336, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What traditional isiXhosa foods common in the Eastern Cape are suitable for a lactose-free, diabetes-friendly diet?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any support groups in urban areas of the Eastern Cape for women traders managing type 2 diabetes and anxiety or depression?\\",\\n  \\"How does eating late at night impact blood sugar levels specifically for adults aged 45-54 using both insulin and oral medication?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find local counselling services or mental health resources in my city in the Eastern Cape for managing diabetes-related stress?\\",\\n  \\"What are some tips for fitting physical activity like traditional dancing (umxhentso, intlombe) into a working adult woman’s routine in urban South Africa?\\",\\n  \\"How can urban lifestyles in the Eastern Cape affect healthy food choices for female traders with easy access to fresh produce and a lactose-free diet?\\",\\n  \\"Are there affordable traditional medicine practitioners in my area who advise on managing type 2 diabetes alongside conventional treatments?\\",\\n  \\"Which Christian (Lutheran) community events in Eastern Cape towns support holistic health for middle-aged women?\\",\\n  \\"What late-night healthy snack options, readily available in urban South Africa, suit someone with type 2 diabetes and lactose intolerance?\\",\\n  \\"How does regular exercise, 3–4 days a week, influence blood sugar control for South African women in their late 40s or early 50s?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best ways to coordinate visits to a local healthcare clinic or hospital in the Eastern Cape for regular diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"Are there isiXhosa-language resources about managing both type 2 diabetes and mild mental health conditions like anxiety for women traders in South Africa?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Lihle Mthembu is a hardworking trader in her early fifties living in an Eastern Cape town. She lives a busy life, moving about the urban streets selling her wares, but sometimes she forgets how important her health is for her work. She knows a bit about diabetes from her clinic visits but often questions how much exercise she really needs or what’s safe since she takes insulin and other medicines. She sometimes eats late, thinking it won’t affect her work, and wonders if dancing and exercising could help her manage better.", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
