dio_prompts": ["Thandekile Mzamane's voice, slightly weary and with a South African English accent, recounting her day. Sound of a tea kettle whistling faintly in the background. She sighs occasionally, a slight rasp in her voice. Her pacing is moderate, slowing down when describing her fatigue. A gentle, melancholic tone. '...and then I just sat there, staring at the tree, wondering what was wrong with me.'", "A female voice, Mama Nomusa, 60s, nearby, speaking with a warm, concerned tone in Xhosa, then switching to South African English. Thandekile Mzamane’s voice responds quietly, hesitant. Sound of gentle chatter and shuffling feet in the background of a home setting. 'Thandekile, my child, you need to go to the clinic. It’s important.' Thandekile: 'But Mama Nomusa, I’m just tired…'", "Thandekile Mzamane’s voice, sounding slightly flustered and breathless, as she describes searching for a snack. Sound of rustling plastic bags and the faint chatter of colleagues in the background. A quickened pace with a frustrated tone. ‘Oh no, where did I put it? I knew I should have packed something…’. A slight pause, followed by a determined sigh.", "Thandekile Mzamane’s voice, now brighter and more energetic, speaking with a cheerful South African English accent. Sound of children laughing and playing in the background, along with the faint sound of music. A clear, confident tone. 'Miss Dlamini was so pleased! And I had enough energy to help with the costumes. It’s not perfect, but I’m learning.' "], "image_prompts": ["Medium shot of Thandekile Mzamane, a woman in her early thirties, sitting at a wooden kitchen table in a modestly furnished home in East London, South Africa. She is slumped slightly forward, staring at a half-eaten biscuit and a cup of tea. The kitchen is small, with patterned linoleum flooring and mismatched chairs. Sunlight streams in through a window, illuminating dust motes in the air. Her expression is one of fatigue and slight frustration. ", "Wide shot of Thandekile Mzamane sitting on a plastic chair in a brightly lit but crowded clinic waiting room in East London, South Africa. She is looking down at a pamphlet about healthy eating, her brow furrowed in concentration. A nurse in a white uniform is visible in the background attending to another patient. The room is filled with people of various ages, some looking anxious, others resigned. Thandekile is holding her handbag tightly in her lap.", "Medium shot of Thandekile Mzamane standing in a school classroom, surrounded by colorful children's artwork. She is rummaging through her handbag with a slightly panicked expression, looking for a snack. A half-eaten apple is visible in her hand. The classroom is simple but tidy, with desks arranged in rows. Thandekile's posture suggests a sense of urgency and mild frustration.", "Wide shot of Thandekile Mzamane, smiling brightly, standing beside a completed backdrop painting for a school play. She is standing with X, a middle-aged woman, also smiling. The backdrop depicts a vibrant green tree. The scene is set in the school hall, decorated with colorful banners and balloons. Thandekile appears energetic and proud of her work, her posture upright and confident. "], "language_code": "en-ZA", "avg_time_taken": 84.23266913340642, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some traditional IsiXhosa gluten-free recipes that are healthy for someone with type 2 diabetes in Eastern Cape urban areas?\\",\\n  \\"Are there diabetes support groups or community workshops specifically for women in their 20s and 30s in Eastern Cape cities like Mthatha or East London?\\",\\n  \\"How does late-night eating impact blood sugar levels for urban working adults with type 2 diabetes who follow a gluten-free diet in South Africa?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find local healthcare resources or clinics in the Eastern Cape that provide specialized counselling for diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"How can I incorporate iintsomi (storytelling) and izibongo (praise poetry) into social gatherings while maintaining healthy habits for blood sugar control?\\",\\n  \\"What exercise options or classes are available 3-4 days per week for urban women in the Eastern Cape trying to manage type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there culturally relevant, Christian Apostolic support networks in Eastern Cape urban communities for individuals managing diabetes and high tobacco use?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best urban supermarkets or stores in Eastern Cape cities for easy access to affordable, gluten-free and diabetes-friendly foods?\\",\\n  \\"How can high tobacco use among young female teachers with type 2 diabetes in IsiXhosa communities affect overall health outcomes?\\",\\n  \\"How do socialising patterns with family or friends in Eastern Cape cities impact healthy lifestyle routines for women managing diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What are some effective strategies for replacing high-frequency smoking habits with stress-reducing activities tailored for women with type 2 diabetes in urban South Africa?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any urban community events or health programs in the Eastern Cape that blend storytelling, culture, and diabetes education for young adults?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
