ass="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Limited access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Administrator</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Journaling or diary writing</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3–4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5c8ddb5f-5329-4af2-8085-6d079353e48f</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up early, like every day, and go to work at the local clinic. I'm an administrator, so I have to manage papers and help the nurses. My job is important, and I don’t want to miss a day. But I don’t really think about how my body feels. I eat what’s on the table — samp and beans, sometimes with a bit of salt and oil. I don’t know much about blood sugar or blood pressure. I just eat because it’s what we do. My husband says I should be more careful, but I don’t listen. I think my body is strong. I don’t believe I need to change anything. I just want to finish my work and go home.\n\nOne day, the clinic nurse says, 'Lihle, you’ve been coming for years, but your blood pressure is going up. Your doctor says you need to eat less salt and more greens. You can cook with pumpkin leaves or spinach — they’re cheap and good for your heart.' I say, 'But I don’t have time. I have work to do. And my family eats the same food.' She says, 'You don’t need to change everything. Just one thing — make a green stew one day a week. It’s simple, and it helps your blood.' I nod, but I don’t believe it will work. I just want to keep doing what I know. I don’t trust that a new food will make me feel better.\n\nI try to make the green stew. I go to the market and buy pumpkin leaves. I chop them and cook with a little oil. It tastes bitter at first. I don’t like it. I eat it with my porridge, but I feel tired. The next day, I forget. I go back to eating beans and samp with salt. My son says I look tired. I tell him I’m fine. I think the work is more important than food. But then I hear that the clinic is starting a group for older women — a cooking class — and it’s on the next week. I feel a little scared. I don’t want to fail again. But I know if I don’t go, I’ll miss the chance to learn how to cook healthy food for my family.\n\nI go to the cooking class. The woman teaches us how to cook with greens, beans, and maize. I try again — this time with spinach and a little onion. It’s not perfect, but I like it. I cook it for my husband and son. They say it tastes better than before. I feel strong. I don’t feel tired anymore. I start making it every week. I even share the recipe with my neighbour. I don’t think I’ll ever stop. Because now I know — my body is not just a machine. It’s part of my work, my family, my life. And I can take care of it, even when I’m busy.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5c8ddb5f-5329-4af2-8085-6d079353e48f_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5c8ddb5f-5329-4af2-8085-6d079353e48f_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5c8ddb5f-5329-4af2-8085-6d079353e48f_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5c8ddb5f-5329-4af2-8085-6d079353e48f_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5c8ddb5f-5329-4af2-8085-6d079353e48f_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5c8ddb5f-5329-4af2-8085-6d079353e48f_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5c8ddb5f-5329-4af2-8085-6d079353e48f_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5c8ddb5f-5329-4af2-8085-6d079353e48f_3.mp3}	I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?	exercise	female	consistency	2026-03-23 13:02:34.111568+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Sizwe Mbeki is a 25–34 year old, \\nCulture: IsiXhosa male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Teacher, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Eastern Cape. Disability: he has none. Religion: Christianity (Presbyterian). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Rugby. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication). Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: Anxiety or depression. Diet restrictions: Vegetarian. Smoking: Yes. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 3–4 days. Support network: I live alone or have limited support. Health goals: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . his food access Easy access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Sizwe Mbeki and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in English that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken English, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in English.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in English.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "resistance", "audio_prompts": ["Lihle Dlamini speaks softly in a mid-range natural tone, her voice slightly low and tired, breathing slowly, the sound of a distant market bell and wind rustling through dry grass in the background, she says, 'I just eat what’s on the table, no need to change,' her voice pauses briefly, then continues with a slow, deliberate pace, the sound of a spoon tapping on a bowl can be heard faintly.", "Lihle Dlamini and a nurse in a clinic room, the nurse speaks clearly and gently, her voice is moderate and calm, Lihle responds with a slight hesitation, her voice is soft and slightly strained, there is a soft hum of a fan in the background, the sound of pages turning in a notebook is heard, Lihle says, 'But I don’t have time,' her voice drops slightly, then rises with a small pause.", "Lihle Dlamini stands in a backyard, her voice is breathless and slightly shaky, she says, 'It tastes bitter,' her breathing is shallow, a chicken caws in the distance, the sound of wind through dry leaves, her son replies, 'You look tired,' Lihle doesn’t respond immediately, her voice is quiet and hesitant, then she says, 'I’ll try again,' with a small pause.", "Lihle Dlamini stirring a pot in a kitchen, her voice is clear and steady, slightly rising at the end of phrases, the sound of a stove hissing, a child laughing from outside, the background has soft clinking of utensils, she says, 'This tastes better,' her tone is warm and inviting, her breathing is calm, and she smiles softly."], "image_prompts": ["Lihle Dlamini standing in a small rural kitchen in the Eastern Cape, wearing a faded blue dress, holding a bowl of samp and beans, her hands slightly trembling as she stirs the pot, sunlight filtering through a dusty window, the walls are made of clay and wood, a single hanging light bulb flickers, a small table with a notebook open beside her, she looks tired but focused, her eyes slightly closed as if thinking about work.", "Lihle Dlamini sitting on a wooden chair in a clinic waiting room, a nurse in a white uniform speaking to her, both facing forward, the room is dimly lit with a single overhead lamp, a poster about diabetes is on the wall, Lihle’s hands are folded on her lap, her face is neutral with slight hesitation, a small notebook lies open on the table between them, the background shows a rural clinic with a sign that says 'Eastern Cape Health Clinic'.", "Lihle Dlamini standing in a small backyard, holding a bowl of green stew made from pumpkin leaves, her hands are slightly shaking, the ground is muddy, a few chickens are nearby, her son is standing behind her, looking at the food with doubt, sunlight is coming from the side, the air is warm and still, Lihle’s shoulders are slumped, showing tiredness, her eyes are downcast.", "Lihle Dlamini cooking in a small kitchen, wearing a clean cotton apron, stirring a pot of spinach and maize porridge, her hands are steady, sunlight coming through a window, a small wooden table with a notebook open beside her, her son is sitting nearby, watching with a smile, the kitchen is simple but clean, the walls have painted patterns of traditional Xhosa designs, she looks calm and confident, her posture is upright."], "language_code": "en-ZA", "avg_time_taken": 59.339460287338646, "task_parent_id": "79de9404-2a8f-4351-aaf8-df2a3a5bcb19", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are affordable, lactose-free traditional IsiXhosa recipes suitable for someone with Type 2 diabetes and hypertension living in a rural Eastern Cape community?\\",\\n  \\"How can I find locally available healthy foods in small rural towns of the Eastern Cape with limited access, especially for people managing high blood pressure and diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any community support programs or groups in the A - Eastern Cape focused on promoting healthy lifestyle changes for older women over 55?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I buy affordable fresh vegetables and lactose-free dairy alternatives near rural areas in Eastern Cape, South Africa?\\",\\n  \\"Which traditional IsiXhosa dishes can I safely adapt for a lactose-free diet and still support blood sugar and blood pressure control?\\",\\n  \\"How do rural clinics in Eastern Cape help patients with diabetes manage their dietary needs on a limited budget?\\",\\n  \\"What practical tips are there for South African administrative workers to fit in 3–4 days of physical activity per week, especially in small rural communities?\\",\\n  \\"How does frequent alcohol consumption affect diabetes and hypertension management for older women, and are there culturally relevant alternatives for social occasions?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any local Eastern Cape community events or groups for older women interested in journaling or diary writing that also focus on health and wellness?\\",\\n  \\"How can I balance my preference for socializing with family with eating healthier, budget-friendly meals in the context of IsiXhosa culture?\\",\\n  \\"What are some accessible herbal or traditional medicines used by rural IsiXhosa communities for managing diabetes and hypertension safely?\\",\\n  \\"Which public health resources or financial assistance are available in the Eastern Cape for buying medication like insulin or Metformin for diabetic patients living in rural areas?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
5caad600-2e8f-4eb2-9a96-3f7d61d0da43	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b818-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Homa Bay</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Christianity (Methodist)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Akinyi Onyango</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Female</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">45-54</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Rural (small community or countryside)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="