       <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">1-2 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegetarian</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5caad600-2e8f-4eb2-9a96-3f7d61d0da43</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up every morning before sunrise to tend to my cattle and work on my farm. As a cattle trader, my days are filled with physical activity, but I never thought about how my health affects my work. I eat what I can, when I can - mostly traditional Luo dishes like fish from Lake Victoria and vegetables from my farm. But lately, I've been feeling tired easily, and my blood sugar levels have been all over the place. Today, I was supposed to deliver a batch of cattle to a client, but I had to postpone because I wasn't feeling well. What's going on with my body?\n\nI decided to visit our local healthcare clinic to get some advice. The health worker, Sister Agnes, told me that I need to be more mindful of my diet and exercise routine. She explained that as a diabetic, I need to avoid certain foods that can spike my blood sugar levels. She gave me a list of healthy, vegetarian options that I can easily incorporate into my daily meals. She also suggested that I start with short, manageable physical activities like brisk walking or bodyweight exercises that I can do at home. But, I'm not sure if I can stick to this new routine. What if I get bored or tired?\n\nI tried to follow Sister Agnes' advice, but it's not easy. I started taking short walks around my farm, and I've been trying to eat more vegetables and less sugary foods. But, old habits die hard, and I found myself slipping back into my old routine. I missed a day of walking, and I ate some fried fish that my sister cooked. I felt guilty and frustrated, but then I remembered that I have a big task coming up - I need to prepare for the annual cattle auction. If I can get my health back on track, I'll have more energy and confidence to negotiate with buyers. So, I'm going to keep trying.\n\nIt's been a few weeks since I started making changes to my diet and exercise routine. It's not perfect, but I've noticed a gradual improvement in my energy levels and blood sugar control. I've been able to work on my farm without getting tired easily, and I've even started doing some bodyweight exercises at home. The annual cattle auction is approaching, and I'm feeling more confident and prepared. I realize that taking care of my health is not just about managing my diabetes, but also about being able to do my job and provide for my family. I'm open to continuing to learn and make changes to improve my health.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5caad600-2e8f-4eb2-9a96-3f7d61d0da43_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5caad600-2e8f-4eb2-9a96-3f7d61d0da43_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5caad600-2e8f-4eb2-9a96-3f7d61d0da43_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5caad600-2e8f-4eb2-9a96-3f7d61d0da43_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5caad600-2e8f-4eb2-9a96-3f7d61d0da43_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5caad600-2e8f-4eb2-9a96-3f7d61d0da43_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5caad600-2e8f-4eb2-9a96-3f7d61d0da43_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5caad600-2e8f-4eb2-9a96-3f7d61d0da43_3.mp3}	I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:19:57.018668+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "Llama-3.3-70B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Achieng Odhiambo is a 45-54 year old, \\nCulture: Luo female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Sugarcane farmer, lives in a Suburban (near city or town) in Homa Bay. Disability: she has none. Religion: Islam. Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Visiting friends and extended family. Activities: Socialising with family or friends. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifest