access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">NGO worker</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Ohangla dancing</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Only when necessary</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">4c9479a4-79d7-4154-a9f9-a4b094ca82e9</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up early, like every day, and go to work at the NGO where I help poor women with clean water. I eat fish stew with sukuma wiki and a bit of ugali. My brother says it's good for me, but I don’t know if it helps my body when I feel tired. I don’t check my blood sugar, and I don’t think it matters. I dance Ohangla every weekend, but I don’t know if it helps me stay strong. One day, I had to stop work because I felt dizzy and weak. I didn’t tell anyone. I just sat down and cried. I thought, 'Why am I like this? Is it because I eat too much or too little?' I didn’t know what to do.\n\nAt the clinic, a nurse named Amina asked me about my diet and how I feel. She said, 'Akinyi, your body needs balance — not too much sugar, not too little protein. Fish and greens are good, but you need to eat slowly and not skip meals.' She gave me a simple plan: eat grilled fish twice a week, add more vegetables, and eat small portions of ugali. She said, 'You can still dance, but only after eating.' I didn’t believe it at first. I thought, 'I’ve been doing this for years. Why change?' But she smiled and said, 'Your body will thank you. And your work will be better too.' I agreed to try.\n\nI tried to eat fish before dancing, but my first time I felt full and sleepy. I didn’t want to stop dancing. I missed the music and the joy. One day, I forgot to eat before dancing and felt shaky. I fell on the floor. My friend saw me and said, 'Akinyi, you’re not okay.' I cried. I didn’t want to stop. But the next day, I remembered Amina’s words. I started eating a small bowl of brown rice and a piece of grilled fish before dancing. It took a week, but I felt stronger. I knew I had to keep going — because next week, I have to lead a dance session for young women in the community. I can’t fail them.\n\nNow, every morning I eat a small portion of brown ugali with grilled fish and greens. I drink water and check my blood sugar once a week. I dance Ohangla with joy, and I feel strong. I even invited two young women to join me. They said, 'We want to learn too!' I feel proud. I know my body is getting better. I don’t have to hide my health anymore. I can work, dance, and live with peace. I know I can keep going — because my body is strong, and I am strong too.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4c9479a4-79d7-4154-a9f9-a4b094ca82e9_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4c9479a4-79d7-4154-a9f9-a4b094ca82e9_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4c9479a4-79d7-4154-a9f9-a4b094ca82e9_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/4c9479a4-79d7-4154-a9f9-a4b094ca82e9_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4c9479a4-79d7-4154-a9f9-a4b094ca82e9_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4c9479a4-79d7-4154-a9f9-a4b094ca82e9_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4c9479a4-79d7-4154-a9f9-a4b094ca82e9_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/4c9479a4-79d7-4154-a9f9-a4b094ca82e9_3.mp3}	How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:20:07.001507+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Akinyi Odhiambo is a 55-64 year old, \\nCulture: Luo female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Fish processor, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Kisumu. Disability: she has none. Religion: Christianity (other). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Ohangla dancing. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healt