         <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3–4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Close friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">bcfe3b9f-1f05-4883-ab54-a87e4d925747</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I'm Vuyolwethu Mkhize, a young teacher living in the Eastern Cape. My daily routine is busy, and I often grab whatever food is quick and available. I love playing football, but lately, I've been feeling really tired after games. I brush it off as stress from work, but deep down, I know I need to make some changes. My diet consists of a lot of traditional Xhosa dishes like umngqusho and imifino, which I love, but I'm not sure if they're the best for my health. I've been noticing that my blood sugar levels have been all over the place, and I'm starting to worry that it might be affecting my work.\n\nOne day, I decided to visit my local clinic to get some advice on managing my blood sugar levels. The nurse was really helpful and explained that I need to make some changes to my diet and exercise routine. She told me that I should be eating more fruits and vegetables, and reducing my intake of sugary drinks and refined carbohydrates. She also recommended that I start taking regular walks and doing some light exercise to help manage my stress levels. I was a bit resistant at first, but she assured me that it would be worth it in the long run. She gave me some personalized advice and told me to come back in a few weeks to check on my progress.\n\nI tried to follow the nurse's advice, but it wasn't easy. I had to make some big changes to my routine, and it took some time to get used to. I started by replacing my usual sugary drinks with water, and I began taking short walks during my lunch break. I also tried to incorporate more fruits and vegetables into my meals, but it was hard to resist the temptation of my favorite traditional dishes. I had a bit of a setback when I accidentally ate a big plate of umngqusho with a lot of sugar, but I didn't give up. I knew that I had to keep trying if I wanted to feel better and perform better at work.\n\nAfter a few weeks of making these changes, I started to notice a big difference. I had more energy, and I wasn't feeling as tired after games. My blood sugar levels were also more stable, and I felt more confident in my ability to manage my health. I realized that taking care of my health wasn't just about me, but also about being able to do my job to the best of my ability. I'm grateful for the advice and support I received from the clinic, and I'm excited to continue making healthy changes to my lifestyle. I know that it won't always be easy, but I'm ready for the challenge.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bcfe3b9f-1f05-4883-ab54-a87e4d925747_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bcfe3b9f-1f05-4883-ab54-a87e4d925747_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bcfe3b9f-1f05-4883-ab54-a87e4d925747_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bcfe3b9f-1f05-4883-ab54-a87e4d925747_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bcfe3b9f-1f05-4883-ab54-a87e4d925747_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bcfe3b9f-1f05-4883-ab54-a87e4d925747_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bcfe3b9f-1f05-4883-ab54-a87e4d925747_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bcfe3b9f-1f05-4883-ab54-a87e4d925747_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:02:27.077018+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "Llama-3.3-70B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Siyabulela Nkosi is a 18–24 year old, \\nCulture: IsiXhosa male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Teacher, lives in a Rural (small community or countryside) in Eastern Cape. Disability: he has none. Religion: Christianity (Presbyterian). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling (iintsomi) and praise poetry (izibongo). Activities: Socialising wi