nter. She's holding a bowl of chopped spinach, her brow furrowed in thought. Warm, natural light from the window illuminates dust motes dancing in the air.", "Medium shot of Bokamoso Dlamini, 42, smiling confidently while reviewing a document on a computer screen in her office. A small plate of fruit sits beside her keyboard. She is wearing a colourful headwrap, and the office is now noticeably more organised. Sunlight streams through the window, casting a warm glow on her face."], "language_code": "en-ZA", "avg_time_taken": 84.23266913340642, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some IsiXhosa-inspired, kosher-friendly meals suitable for a suburban working woman with type 2 diabetes in the Eastern Cape?\\",\\n  \\"Which local Eastern Cape grocery stores or markets near suburban areas offer kosher options and diabetic-friendly healthy foods?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any traditional dancing groups or umxhentso classes for adult women in the suburban areas of the Eastern Cape?\\",\\n  \\"What physical activity recommendations are best for women aged 35–44 managing type 2 diabetes and living in a suburban area with easy access to exercise facilities?\\",\\n  \\"How do I manage high tobacco use while on metformin and insulin for type 2 diabetes, specifically with resources available in the Eastern Cape?\\",\\n  \\"What are some family-support resources for suburban IsiXhosa families supporting a member with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there healthcare clinics or specialists in the Eastern Cape familiar with kosher diets, atheism, and type 2 diabetes concerns?\\",\\n  \\"What sample daily routines balance administrative office work, regular exercise (3–4 days/week), and traditional dance practice for urban IsiXhosa women?\\",\\n  \\"Which nearby parks or recreational facilities in suburban Eastern Cape are suitable for physical activities compatible with a diabetes management plan?\\",\