         \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5d832d63-b3f0-4cfa-8bc1-6d136d6cfba1</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	You know, sometimes I get caught up in my trading, selling fabrics in the busy market here in Kano. I just assume moving around the stalls and talking to customers is enough exercise for me. But honestly, I never really thought about how important it is to keep active in a focused way for my diabetes. One day, I tried to manage everything without any real plan, believing I could just walk a bit when I had time. But when I felt tired and my sugar was high, work just didn’t go well. My customers noticed I was off, and I wasn’t my sharp self. Who knew a little exercise done right would make such a difference?\n\nThen I went to the local health clinic where the nurse explained things clearly in Hausa, just like talking to a friend. She said walking briskly for at least 30 minutes five times a week is perfect and showed me some simple exercises I can do at home, like using water bottles as weights or stretching after prayer times. She reminded me these are ways I can keep modest and still be active, even without a gym. I was a bit unsure at first, wondering if I could fit this into my busy routine, but she encouraged me to start small and be consistent, and always keep my sugar snacks handy just in case.\n\nI tried to follow her advice the very next week. I started walking in the morning before the market opened, carrying empty jerry cans to do some lifting exercises in my compound, and stretching after reading Qur’an. But it wasn’t easy. Some days I felt lazy or worried about preparing for the market or study. One morning, I skipped my walk and felt sluggish all day. But I reminded myself of the big trader event coming soon—a chance to show my best self—and that pushed me to keep going. It wasn’t perfect, but I knew my health mattered for this bigger goal.\n\nLittle by little, things got better. I felt stronger walking around the market and had more energy in my Islamic study groups. At the big trader event, I was more confident than before and even shared some exercise tips with my friends. Now I understand that staying active with simple steps helps me control my diabetes better and keeps my life balanced. I’m even planning to start a small walking group with other women from my mosque. Who would have thought, just a few changes at home could open the door to a healthier and happier me?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5d832d63-b3f0-4cfa-8bc1-6d136d6cfba1_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5d832d63-b3f0-4cfa-8bc1-6d136d6cfba1_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5d832d63-b3f0-4cfa-8bc1-6d136d6cfba1_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5d832d63-b3f0-4cfa-8bc1-6d136d6cfba1_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5d832d63-b3f0-4cfa-8bc1-6d136d6cfba1_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5d832d63-b3f0-4cfa-8bc1-6d136d6cfba1_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5d832d63-b3f0-4cfa-8bc1-6d136d6cfba1_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5d832d63-b3f0-4cfa-8bc1-6d136d6cfba1_3.mp3}	I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:29:32.013834+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "gpt-4.1-mini", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Amina Bello is a 18-24 year old, \\nCulture: Hausa female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Trader, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Katsina. Disability: she has none. Religion: Islam. Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling. Activities: Socialising with family or friends. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: None. Diet restrictions: Halal. Smoking: No. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 0 days. Support network: Family (parents, siblings, children). Health goals: Eating healt