 on dusty ground punctuate the quiet. Her tone mixes frustration with resolve during the workout attempt.", "Late afternoon park ambiance with birds singing softly, light wind rustling leaves, and occasional distant voices of families enjoying the space. Amina Suleiman's voice is lively and warm as she chats naturally with a female friend walking alongside her. Their footsteps tap lightly on the paved path, creating a calm, uplifting soundscape. Amina's voice shows growing confidence and contentment, filled with hopeful energy about future health journeys."], "image_prompts": ["Amina Suleiman stands inside her busy Kano market stall, surrounded by colorful traditional fabrics and baskets. Her posture shows slight fatigue as she talks with a customer, mid-shot, natural lighting highlighting the textures of the textiles. The market is vibrant and bustling around her, capturing the urban trading atmosphere. The candid photo captures Amina's thoughtful expression as she balances work and health.", "Amina Suleiman listens attentively to a female nurse in a local healthcare clinic room in Kano. The nurse, mid-30s woman, is sitting nearby explaining with gentle hand gestures, while Amina sits upright on a plastic chair holding a pamphlet about diabetes exercise. Soft daylight filters through a window, illuminating the ethnic details of their clothes and the clinical setting. The medium shot shows a respectful and supportive interaction in a culturally familiar environment.", "Amina Suleiman attempts home exercises outside her simple compound, wearing modest, comfortable clothes. She carries a plastic water bottle acting as a weight, her expression focused but slightly tired mid-action. The background shows a dusty yard with a few trees and a wall painted in faded colors, under the warm Kano sunlight. The wide shot captures her commitment to change and the daily realities of balancing exercise with work and study.", "Amina Suleiman smiles confidently while walking with another young female friend from her mosque in a green, well-maintained Kano park during late afternoon. Both wear brightly colored hijabs and casual modest clothing, walking side by side on a paved path lined with trees and benches. Sunlight filters warmly through the leaves, and Amina stands upright with relaxed shoulders, embodying health and social support. The medium shot captures this candid, joyful moment of progress and community."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 3.40064914226532, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are the best types of physical activities for a 25-34 year old urban Hausa Muslim woman in Kano managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there exercise groups or female-only fitness centers in Kano city that respect Islamic and cultural norms?\\",\\n  \\"How do local Kano hospitals or clinics support female traders with diabetes who need flexible healthcare schedules?\\",\\n  \\"What traditional Hausa foods available in urban Kano are both Halal and suitable for managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What are local Hausa community perspectives on women participating in regular outdoor walking for exercise?\\",\\n  \\"How might daily alcohol consumption impact type 2 diabetes and are there community support groups for reducing alcohol intake in Kano?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any spiritual or Islamic study groups in Kano that include physical activities, like group walks, as part of their gatherings?\\",\\n  \\"What are the safest public spaces or parks in urban Kano where women can walk or exercise regularly?\\",\\n  \\"How can a working female trader in Kano integrate blood sugar monitoring into a busy city lifestyle?\\",\\n  \\"What advice do Kano-based dietitians give on balancing work, Qurâ€™an study, and healthy eating for women with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there culturally appropriate, indoor exercise options in Kano for Muslim women, especially during hot weather or during Ramadan?\\",\\n  \\"What is the local perception in the Hausa community regarding the use of herbal or traditional remedies along with prescribed diabetes medications?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Relevant fields for Amina Suleiman include: female gender; age 25-34; urban Hausa Muslim female living in Kano; works as a trader; managing type 2 diabetes with insulin injections; daily routine balancing work and Islamic study; access to local healthcare clinics regularly; no disability; restricted to halal diet; no smoking or alcohol; physically active 5-7 days per week; supported by community and religious groups; health goal to understand what types of exercise can be done at home or using everyday items without gym access.", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
