d>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Only when necessary</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegetarian</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5446d0cf-c221-43f7-b290-1656b50e340a</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	As a young female trader, I wake up early, feeling a mix of excitement and stress. Today is a big day; I have orders to fulfill for customers across the city. I quickly get dressed in my worn but comfortable clothes and rush out the door to start my day. My diet consists mainly of street food and whatever I can afford at the local market. I've never really thought much about what I eat or how it affects my body, as long as I feel okay. My daily routine is hectic, and I often skip meals or grab whatever is readily available, which can be high in sugar and unhealthy fats. I've always been active, but with the demands of my work, I've noticed my energy levels dropping, and I've started to feel a bit more sluggish than usual. I try to push through, but it's getting harder. I need a way to manage my energy levels and stay focused throughout the day.\n\nI decided to visit the local health clinic to see if they could offer any advice on how to improve my health. The nurse practitioner there was kind and listened attentively to my concerns. She explained that my diet and lack of exercise were contributing to my fatigue and suggested a few simple changes I could make to my daily routine. I was skeptical at first, but she assured me that these changes would make a big difference in how I felt. She recommended that I start by eating smaller, more frequent meals throughout the day, including plenty of fruits and vegetables. She also suggested that I try to incorporate some light exercise, like walking or yoga, into my daily routine. I was hesitant to make these changes, but she encouraged me to give it a try.\n\nI tried to implement the nurse practitioner's suggestions, but it wasn't easy. I found it hard to adjust to eating smaller meals throughout the day, and I missed the rush of energy I used to get from grabbing a quick snack or meal. I also struggled to find the time to exercise, especially with my busy schedule. But I was determined to make this work, not just for my health but also because I had a bigger goal in mind - to start my own business and become financially independent. I knew that if I could just get my health under control, I'd be better equipped to handle the demands of entrepreneurship. So, I persisted, even when it felt like giving up. I started small, taking short walks during my breaks or doing a few yoga poses in the morning. It wasn't much, but it was a start.\n\nAs the days went by, I started to notice a difference in how I felt. My energy levels were higher, and I was able to focus better throughout the day. I still had my busy moments, but I was better equipped to handle them. I realized that taking care of my health wasn't just about feeling good; it was also about being more productive and successful in my work. With my newfound energy and focus, I was able to tackle my bigger goal - starting my own business. It wasn't easy, but I was determined to make it happen. And as I looked back on the journey, I realized that taking care of my health had been the key to unlocking my potential. I was no longer just a young female trader; I was a entrepreneur, ready to take on the world.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5446d0cf-c221-43f7-b290-1656b50e340a_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5446d0cf-c221-43f7-b290-1656b50e340a_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5446d0cf-c221-43f7-b290-1656b50e340a_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/5446d0cf-c221-43f7-b290-1656b50e340a_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5446d0cf-c221-43f7-b290-1656b50e340a_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5446d0cf-c221-43f7-b290-1656b50e340a_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5446d0cf-c221-43f7-b290-1656b50e340a_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/5446d0cf-c221-43f7-b290-1656b50e340a_3.mp3}	I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday