 <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5–7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Close friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0e4b8351-3f7d-4aff-9d78-b8e6badfa615</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I'm Siphosethu, a teacher from the Eastern Cape. My day starts early, and I'm always on the go. I love my job, but sometimes I forget to take care of myself. I've been feeling tired lately, and I know it's because I'm not eating well. I grab whatever is quick and easy, even if it's not the healthiest option. For example, I love traditional umxhentso dancing, but I don't always make time for it. I'm supposed to perform at a big event next month, but I'm worried I won't be ready. I need to start taking care of my health so I can do my best.\n\nI went to see my doctor at the local clinic, and she told me that as a vegan, I need to make sure I'm getting enough protein and fiber. She recommended that I start taking supplements and eating more plant-based foods. I was a bit skeptical at first, but she explained everything in a way that made sense. She even gave me some recipe ideas that I could try at home. I felt more confident after the visit, and I knew I could make some changes.\n\nI started trying to incorporate more plant-based foods into my diet, but it was harder than I thought. I would forget to pack snacks for work, or I would get lazy and order takeout. Last week, I had a minor setback when I forgot to take my insulin shot, but I remembered to take it the next day. I'm still adjusting to my new routine, but I know it's worth it in the end.\n\nI'm glad I took the time to see the doctor and make some changes to my diet. I feel more energetic and focused now. I know I still have a lot to learn, but I'm excited to continue improving my health. I'm looking forward to performing at the event next month, and I know I'll be able to do my best because I took care of myself.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0e4b8351-3f7d-4aff-9d78-b8e6badfa615_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0e4b8351-3f7d-4aff-9d78-b8e6badfa615_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0e4b8351-3f7d-4aff-9d78-b8e6badfa615_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0e4b8351-3f7d-4aff-9d78-b8e6badfa615_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0e4b8351-3f7d-4aff-9d78-b8e6badfa615_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0e4b8351-3f7d-4aff-9d78-b8e6badfa615_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0e4b8351-3f7d-4aff-9d78-b8e6badfa615_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0e4b8351-3f7d-4aff-9d78-b8e6badfa615_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:02:27.467068+00	{"label": "GOOD", "model": "Llama-3.1-8B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Luyanda Mkhuseli is a 35–44 year old, \\nCulture: IsiXhosa male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Business owner, lives in a Urban (city or town) in Eastern Cape. Disability: he has none. Religion: Christianity (Apostolic). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling (iintsomi) and praise poetry (izibongo). Activities: Socialising with family or friends. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: Anxiety or depression. Diet restrictions: Kosher. Smoking: Yes. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 3–4 days. Support network: Community or religious group. Health goals: I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?. his food access Easy access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Luyanda Mkhuseli and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes 