n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">7e5c6a1f-5400-49ad-b74c-bd31ab57f0af</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Let me tell you, my days are always full. Sun up, and there I am, tending the goats, watering the little garden by the house, making sure everything is in its place before I head to work. I eat well too—fresh vegetables, maize meal, chicken when I have it. But you know, I never really thought about how my body feels until the other day. There was a broken fence post near the chicken coop. I tried to fix it fast, just like before, but eish, my arms got tired so quickly! I gave up and left it for later. I thought to myself, 'What’s the use trying hard if I just get tired?'\n\nThe next day, when I went for my usual check-up at the local clinic, I tried not to mention my tiredness. But Nurse Lydia, she noticed. She asked, 'Amara, you look a bit worn out—what's wrong?' I shrugged and shook my head, unsure. She smiled, sat me down, and said, 'You don’t need a gym. Use the things around you, even at home or the farm. Lift water buckets a few times more, stretch when you feed your goats, dance when you listen to music. Every small thing helps your body get stronger.' I listened, but at first I thought, 'Can these small things really make a difference?'\n\nI decided, maybe it's worth a try. The next morning, I added a few extra trips carrying water, and swung my arms when walking to the shed. But changing how I do things felt strange, almost silly—my shoulders ached, and I wanted to stop. Then I remembered the bigger job waiting: the old gate needs fixing before the next rains, and I need to be strong. That made me keep going, even if it was tough at first.\n\nA week passed and, slow-slow, I started feeling better. My arms lifted the buckets a bit easier each day. At last, it was time to fix that big gate. I didn’t feel like stopping because I was tired—I finished the work, stood up tall, and smiled. Can you believe it? I felt proud for sticking with it. Now, even though there’s no gym, I see how little changes help me at my work and at home. I think, maybe I’ll keep looking for new ways to move and stay strong!	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/s