ating bright patches on the wooden floor, showing a warm atmosphere of accomplishment and camaraderie. Wide shot, candid, natural and unposed."], "language_code": "en-KE", "avg_time_taken": 3.10124871134758, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are recommended exercise routines for a 35-44 year old male sorghum farmer with type 2 diabetes in rural Kisumu, Kenya?\\",\\n  \\"What traditional Luo foods available in rural Kisumu are both healthy, halal, and suitable for someone with limited access to healthy foods and diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can I stay physically active as a farmer in a rural Kenyan community when I already do farming and animal keeping but struggle to exercise more than 1-2 days per week?\\",\\n  \\"What types of physical activities are culturally popular among Luo Christian men in Kisumu that can help manage type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any community or religious support programs in rural Kisumu for diabetes management among Methodist Christians?\\",\\n  \\"Given my daily smoking and weekly alcohol consumption, what specific risks should I be concerned about managing diabetes as a Luo rural resident?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find halal, diabetes-friendly foods in rural Kisumu with my limited access to healthy food sources?\\",\\n  \\"What lifestyle changes have helped other male farmers in western Kenya successfully manage type 2 diabetes without relying solely on medication?\\",\\n  \\"How do local clinics or hospitals in Kisumu support medication management for diabetes, especially for people who also use herbal or traditional medicine?\\",\\n  \\"What advice do health experts in rural Kenya give to men like me who work physically but still need to exercise more for diabetes health?\\",\\n  \\"How does participating in Methodist or community events in rural Kisumu impact my ability to manage diabetes as part of my social and religious life?\\",\\n  \\"Are ther