 class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5–7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No Restrictions</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">b20121d0-3c7c-4349-bab3-f889ced84747</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up every morning at 5 am to start my day as a livestock keeper. My daily routine is quite busy, and I often find myself eating whatever is available, without thinking about how it affects my health. I love playing rugby, but lately, I've been feeling tired and sluggish on the field. I've been taking insulin injections and oral medication to manage my condition, but I know I need to make some lifestyle changes. My question is, can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too? I've been trying to walk every day, but I'm not sure if it's enough.\n\nOne day, I visited our local healthcare clinic because I wasn't feeling well. The nurse told me that I need to start taking care of my health, not just my livestock. She explained that walking is a great start, but I should also incorporate other types of exercise, like strength training and flexibility exercises. She gave me some simple and practical advice on how to improve my diet and exercise routine. I was a bit resistant at first, but she assured me that it's never too late to make a change. She said, "Lwandle, you take care of your animals, now it's time to take care of yourself."\n\nI tried to follow the nurse's advice, but it wasn't easy. I had to adjust my routine and make time for exercise and healthy eating. I struggled at first, and I had a minor setback when I missed a day of exercise. But I knew I had to persist because I have a big task coming up - a rugby tournament. I want to be able to play without feeling tired and sluggish. So, I kept going, and I started to see some improvements. I had more energy, and I was able to run faster and longer without getting tired.\n\nAs the days went by, I started to feel more confident. I was able to do my daily tasks without feeling exhausted, and I was able to play rugby without struggling. I realized that taking care of my health is not just about me, it's also about being able to do my job and enjoy my hobbies. I'm grateful for the nurse's advice, and I'm open to continuing to learn and improve my health. I know it's a journey, and I'm willing to take it one step at a time.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b20121d0-3c7c-4349-bab3-f889ced84747_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b20121d0-3c7c-4349-bab3-f889ced84747_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b20121d0-3c7c-4349-bab3-f889ced84747_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/b20121d0-3c7c-4349-bab3-f889ced84747_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b20121d0-3c7c-4349-bab3-f889ced84747_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b20121d0-3c7c-4349-bab3-f889ced84747_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b20121d0-3c7c-4349-bab3-f889ced84747_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/b20121d0-3c7c-4349-bab3-f889ced84747_3.mp3}	Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?	exercise	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:02:25.660651+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "Llama-3.3-70B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: \\nCulture: None female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. Religion: None. Hobbies: Traditional dancing (e.g. umxhentso, intlombe). Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine. Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 5–7 days. Support network: Healthcare provider or counsellor. Tone of the output: classic_change.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Asanda Mbeki and understanding the persona's needs (\\"Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?\\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that