erstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "social_support", "audio_prompts": ["The sound of a bustling office can be heard in the background, with the hum of computers and the murmur of coworkers chatting. Lwazi Mbenyane's voice is heard, sounding stressed and overwhelmed. He is speaking to himself, trying to prioritize his tasks and make sense of his workload.", "The sound of a doctor's office can be heard, with the rustling of papers and the gentle tone of the doctor speaking. Lwazi Mbenyane's voice is heard, sounding unsure and nervous. He is asking the doctor questions and taking notes on her advice.", "The sound of nature can be heard, with the chirping of birds and the rustling of leaves. Lwazi Mbenyane's voice is heard, sounding relaxed and calm. He is speaking to himself, reflecting on his experiences and feelings.", "The sound of a busy office can be heard, with the hum of computers and the murmur of coworkers chatting. Lwazi Mbenyane's voice is heard, sounding confident and motivated. He is speaking to himself, feeling proud of his accomplishments and looking forward to the future."], "image_prompts": ["Lwazi Mbenyane, a 20-year-old administrator, sits at his desk, staring blankly at his work, with a can of soda and a packet of microwaveable noodles in front of him. His workspace is cluttered and messy, with papers and files scattered everywhere. In the background, a cityscape can be seen through the window, representing his busy and stressful work life.", "Lwazi Mbenyane sits in a doctor's office, looking unsure and nervous. The doctor, a middle-aged woman with a kind face, is speaking to him in a gentle tone. Lwazi is holding a small notebook and pen, taking notes on the doctor's advice. In the background, a calendar and some medical equipment can be seen, representing the doctor's office.", "Lwazi Mbenyane is seen taking a walk during his lunch break, enjoying the fresh air and sunshine. He is wearing a casual outfit and has a relaxed expression on his face. In the background, a park or garden can be seen, representing his attempt to make healthier choices.", "Lwazi Mbenyane is seen sitting at his desk, looking confident and motivated. He is surrounded by papers and files, but his workspace is now tidy and organized. In the background, a cityscape can be seen, representing his successful completion of tasks and his ability to tackle bigger projects."], "language_code": "en-ZA", "avg_time_taken": 7.16295344073598, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What traditional isiXhosa dances like umxhentso can help manage type 2 diabetes for a young male in the Eastern Cape?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find diabetes-friendly halal food options near suburban areas in the Eastern Cape, South Africa?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community groups or events for traditional dancing in suburban Eastern Cape that support young adults with diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How safe and accessible are suburban parks or walking routes in the Eastern Cape for regular physical activity for men aged 18–24?\\",\\n  \\"What are common diabetes management resources available at local healthcare clinics in the Eastern Cape for young male administrators?\\",\\n  \\"How do isiXhosa c