 thoughtful, saying 'Is this good for my body?' as he holds a white bread in his hands. A faint hum of a refrigerator in the background. The sound of a clock ticking. A distant football match in the street. The volume is moderate, with a slight pause before he says 'I just eat because I’m hungry.'", "Mrs. Nkosi, a middle-aged woman with a calm and gentle voice, says 'You’re doing good, but some foods can make your blood sugar go up fast.' Lutho replies, 'But what about my football game?' in a hesitant tone. The clinic has soft background sounds of a fan and a distant phone ringing. The audio is clear and natural, with a moderate pace and slight pauses.", "Lutho Makhanya breathing deeply, saying 'I felt dizzy and my hands shook' as he looks down at a bowl of chips. A soft kitchen sound of a spoon tapping on a bowl. His voice is shaky, then slows down. A distant classroom bell rings. The volume is soft, with a rising tone at the end.", "Lutho Makhanya speaking clearly and confidently, saying 'Lutho Makhanya once didn’t know what food was good for his body. Now he knows. And so can you.' Students in the background whisper and clap. A soft classroom hum. The tone is warm and inviting, with a steady pace and a slight rise at the end."], "image_prompts": ["Lutho Makhanya sitting on a wooden chair in a small kitchen, holding a white loaf of bread with butter, looking at his hands as if wondering if they are shaking. The kitchen has a red tile floor, a cracked sink, and a hanging light bulb. A banana lies on the table beside a plastic bowl. Sunlight comes from the window, casting long shadows. The room is warm and slightly dusty.", "Lutho Makhanya sitting across from Mrs. Nkosi, a middle-aged woman with glasses and a soft voice, in a small clinic room. She is pointing at a picture of brown rice and beans on a white plate. Lutho leans forward, one hand on his knee, eyes wide with curiosity. The walls are painted light blue, with a single poster of a healthy diet. Natural morning light filters through a window. A small fan hums in the background.", "Lutho Makhanya standing in a kitchen, wearing a teacher’s uniform, holding a bowl of lentils and spinach, a spoon in his hand. He is looking down at the food, slightly unsure, with a small frown. The kitchen has a wooden table, a stove with a pot of boiling water, and a green plant on the shelf. The lighting is soft, warm, and slightly yellow from a kitchen lamp.", "Lutho Makhanya standing in front of a classroom, holding a poster titled 'Eat Brown Rice, Beans, and Greens — They Keep Your Energy Strong!' The poster shows a football player eating beans with a smile. Students are sitting in the back, some looking at him with interest. Lutho is smiling, one hand on his chest, the other holding a notebook. The classroom has chalkboards, desks, and a whiteboard with a drawing of a banana and a bean."], "language_code": "en-ZA", "avg_time_taken": 59.339460287338646, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What vegetarian isiXhosa-inspired meal options are available in urban areas of Eastern Cape that help manage type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can attending Zion Christian Church in an Eastern Cape city help Lutho Makhanya find community support for diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local Eastern Cape football clubs or adult soccer leagues that accept 18-24 year olds who want regular physical activity with diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What are the health guidelines for safe alcohol consumption for young men with type 2 diabetes in South African urban areas?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find diabetes education workshops at clinics or hospitals in East London or other major Eastern Cape cities?\\",\\n  \\"How does daily tobacco smoking affect insulin effectiveness and blood sugar control in young South African men with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What evening routine changes can help a male teacher with high physical activity who sometimes eats late at night regulate blood sugar better?\\",\\n  \\"What vegetarian-friendly isiXhosa recipes are quick to prepare after teaching and suitable for people with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there support groups for young isiXhosa male adults with diabetes in urban Eastern Cape cities?\\",\\n  \\"How does working as a teacher in an urban Eastern Cape school impact meal planning and diabetes management for someone on both medication and lifestyle changes?\\",\\n  \\"What football training schedules in Eastern Cape urban centers are compatible with diabetes routines and healthcare accessibility?\\",\\n  \\"How does the combination of high alcohol consumption and daily tobacco use affect diabetes management for someone with Lutho Makhanya’s lifestyle?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "occupation", "hobbies", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_frequency", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
