              <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5–7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">798fcbe8-8a23-41fb-9cbe-6b2c4ef9cd3c</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up every morning, feeling a bit tired, but I have to get ready for my traditional dancing practice. I love dancing, it's my hobby, and it makes me feel alive. After practice, I usually grab something quick to eat, like a vetkoek or a bunny chow, and then I'm off to my daily chores. I never really thought about how my diet and lack of exercise could affect my energy levels and my work. But today, I had a small task to do, which was to help my friend with her stall at the market. I was so tired that I had to take a break, and I ended up not finishing the task. I thought to myself, "What's wrong with me? Why am I so tired all the time?" \n\nI decided to visit my local healthcare clinic to get some advice. The healthcare worker, Sister Ntombi, was very helpful and explained to me that my diet and lack of exercise were affecting my energy levels. She told me that I need to start taking care of my health, especially since I have Type 2 Diabetes. She advised me to start walking every day and to eat more balanced meals. I was a bit resistant at first, I didn't know if I could do it, but Sister Ntombi reassured me that it's all about making small changes and that she would be there to support me. She also reminded me that my traditional dancing can be a great way to get exercise, so I should keep doing that.\n\nI started taking Sister Ntombi's advice, but it wasn't easy. I had to adjust my routine, and it was hard to get used to walking every day. I also had to change my diet, which was difficult because I love my traditional foods. But I knew I had to do it, especially since I have a bigger task coming up, which is to perform at the annual cultural festival. I didn't want to be too tired to dance, so I persisted. However, I did have a minor setback when I forgot to take my medication one day, and I had to remind myself to take it. But I didn't give up, I kept going, and I started to feel a bit better.\n\nIt's been a few weeks now, and I can see the improvement in my health. I have more energy, and I can dance for longer without getting tired. I'm also eating more balanced meals, and I've started to enjoy my daily walks. The festival is approaching, and I'm feeling more confident about my performance. I realize now that taking care of my health is not just about me, it's also about being able to do the things I love, like dancing. I'm grateful for Sister Ntombi's advice, and I'm open to continuing to make healthy changes in my life.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/798fcbe8-8a23-41fb-9cbe-6b2c4ef9cd3c_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/798fcbe8-8a23-41fb-9cbe-6b2c4ef9cd3c_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/798fcbe8-8a23-41fb-9cbe-6b2c4ef9cd3c_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/798fcbe8-8a23-41fb-9cbe-6b2c4ef9cd3c_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/798fcbe8-8a23-41fb-9cbe-6b2c4ef9cd3c_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/798fcbe8-8a23-41fb-9cbe-6b2c4ef9cd3c_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/798fcbe8-8a23-41fb-9cbe-6b2c4ef9cd3c_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/798fcbe8-8a23-41fb-9cbe-6b2c4ef9cd3c_3.mp3}	Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?	exercise	female	control	2026-03-23 13:02:25.932419+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "Llama-3.3-70B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: \\nCulture: None female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. Religion: None. Hobbies: Traditional dancing (e.g. umxhentso, intlombe). Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine. Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 5–7 days. Support network: Healthcare provider or counsellor. Tone of the output: classic_change.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Asanda Mbeki and understanding the persona's needs (\\"Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?\\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in English that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?. \\n Use spoken English, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a classic_change tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in English.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in English.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "classic_change", "audio_prompts": ["Asanda Mbeki's voice, sounding tired, saying \\"What's wrong with me? Why am I so tired all the time?\\" with a few background noises of people talking and walking, nearby.", "Sister Ntombi's voice, sounding calm and reassuring, saying \\"You need to start taking care of your health, especially since you have Type 2 Diabetes\\" with a few background noises of a clinic, across the room.", "Asanda Mbeki's voice, sounding determined, saying \\"I will do it, I will take care of my health\\" with a few background noises of walking and birds chirping, in the background.", "Asanda Mbeki's voice, sounding happy and confident, saying \\"I did it, I performed at the festival and I felt great\\" with a few background noises of people clapping and cheering, nearby."], "image_prompts": ["Asanda Mbeki, a woman in her mid-30s, sitting on a bench, looking tired, with a vetkoek in her hand, in a busy market scene with people walking in the background, medium shot.", "Sister Ntombi, a middle-aged woman, standing in a clinic, talking to Asanda Mbeki, who is sitting on a chair, looking concerned, with a few health posters on the wall, wide shot.", "Asanda Mbeki, walking alone on a dirt road, surrounded by trees, with a few houses in the background, looking determined, with a slight smile on her face, medium shot.", "Asanda Mbeki, dancing on a stage, wearing traditional clothing, with a few people watching in the audience, looking happy and confident, with a few colorful banners in the background, wide shot."], "language_code": "en-ZA", "avg_time_taken": 5.6488824540918525, "task_parent_id": "3f50a305-91fd-47e9-829f-a4a1ef1a5e6f", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are affordable gluten-free, healthy meal options using ingredients commonly found in suburban areas of Eastern Cape for a young Muslim woman with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there traditional IsiXhosa dishes suitable for someone with diabetes and gluten intolerance that I can easily prepare in a suburban setting near the city?\\",\\n  \\"How can a female trader in the Eastern Cape manage high alcohol consumption while maintaining blood glucose levels and mental health?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find local Eastern Cape support groups or resources for young women with both anxiety and diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What cost-saving strategies exist for accessing insulin and oral diabetes medications at local healthcare clinics in the Eastern Cape?\\",\\n  \\"Are there safe spaces near suburban towns in the Eastern Cape for traditional dancing or exercise that accommodate women observing Islamic practices?\\",\\n  \\"How can I balance my working schedule as a trader with regular physical activity, considering my mental health and diabetes management needs?\\",\\n  \\"What are some gluten-free IsiXhosa recipes for family gatherings that respect Islamic dietary guidelines and help manage type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Is there culturally sensitive mental health support available for young Muslim women in suburban Eastern Cape municipalities?\\",\\n  \\"What local community initiatives or programs in Eastern Cape help make healthy foods more affordable for young working women?\\",\\n  \\"How can I continue participating in umxhentso and intlombe dance events while managing insulin routines and my anxiety?\\",\\n  \\"What is the impact of high alcohol consumption on diabetes management for young, physically active women in South Africa’s Eastern Cape?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "name", "gender", "occupation", "hobbies", "activities", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "culture", "t2d_status", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
