<tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">1–2 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">ca7f00a9-6c23-4427-a1b6-066fd54df0e2</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I'm Noluthando Mbali, a 35-year-old teacher living in Port Elizabeth, Eastern Cape. I've been working in the education sector for over a decade, and I love my job. However, I've noticed that my diet and exercise routine have been suffering lately. I often find myself relying on convenience foods and takeaways, which I know are not good for me. I've tried to make healthier choices, but I keep putting it off, thinking that I'll get to it eventually. Little do I know that my health is affecting my work, making it harder for me to focus and be productive. I've been getting tired easily, and my mood swings are becoming more frequent. I'm starting to feel like I'm not performing my best at work, and it's causing me stress. I know I need to make a change, but I'm not sure where to start.\n\nI decided to visit my local clinic to get some advice on how to improve my health. The nurse was very friendly and understanding. She explained that my diet and exercise habits were affecting my blood sugar levels and causing my fatigue. She recommended that I start by making small changes to my diet, such as eating more fruits and vegetables, and reducing my intake of sugary foods. She also suggested that I start exercising regularly, even if it's just a short walk each day. I was a bit skeptical at first, but she assured me that it would make a big difference. I left the clinic feeling a bit more hopeful, but still uncertain about how to make these changes.\n\nI tried to start making the changes the nurse suggested, but it was harder than I thought it would be. I found myself reaching for my old habits when I got tired or stressed. I had a setback when I accidentally ate a whole pizza by myself one evening, feeling terrible the next morning. I was about to give up, but then I remembered the larger task I had coming up at work and how I wanted to perform well. I decided to push through and not let my health hold me back. I started with small, achievable goals, like taking a short walk each day and preparing healthy meals in advance. It wasn't easy, but I was determined to make it work.\n\nIt's been a few weeks now, and I can see a significant improvement in my health and well-being. I've started feeling more energetic and focused, and my mood swings have reduced. I've even started enjoying healthy foods and finding new recipes online. The nurse was right; making small changes has added up to make a big difference. I'm proud of myself for sticking to it, and I'm excited to see how I can continue to improve my health. I know it won't be easy, but I'm ready for the challenge. I'm looking forward to continuing on this journey and making healthy choices a part of my daily life.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ca7f00a9-6c23-4427-a1b6-066fd54df0e2_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ca7f00a9-6c23-4427-a1b6-066fd54df0e2_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ca7f00a9-6c23-4427-a1b6-066fd54df0e2_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ca7f00a9-6c23-4427-a1b6-066fd54df0e2_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ca7f00a9-6c23-4427-a1b6-066fd54df0e2_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ca7f00a9-6c23-4427-a1b6-066fd54df0e2_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ca7f00a9-6c23-4427-a1b6-066fd54df0e2_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ca7f00a9-6c23-4427-a1b6-066fd54df0e2_3.mp3}	I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?	diet	female	consistency	2026-03-23 13:02:28.002083+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "Llama-3.1-8B", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Luyanda Mkhuseli is a 35–44 year old, \\nCulture: IsiXhosa male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Business owner, live