 working adult who lives alone in South Africa use to maintain motivation for healthy eating and regular exercise?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any government or NGO programs in Eastern Cape providing meal planning resources for diabetic, vegetarian individuals with limited support networks?\\",\\n  \\"What local Eastern Cape vegetables and legumes are recommended for a diabetic vegetarian to include in their daily menu according to South African dietary guidelines?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
0e0ef3c3-8918-42a9-940c-bd49304b664e	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b816-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Eastern Cape</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Christianity (Baptist)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Lwandle Nqweniso</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Male</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">45–54</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Business owner</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Traditional dancing (e.g. umxhentso, intlombe)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">IsiXhosa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">1–2 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Lactose-free</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0e0ef3c3-8918-42a9-940c-bd49304b664e</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">What kinds of exercises are safe and helpful for someone with diabetes?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Lwandle, and I run a little shop selling spices and herbs down in Khayelitsha. It’s a good life, you know? Lots of people come to me for good ingredients. But lately, my legs have been feeling funny, like they’re tired all the time. I just put it down to being busy, always running around, shouting at the delivery guys, and making sure I have enough stock. I eat what I can – sometimes a quick braai, sometimes just some pap and beans. It’s easy to grab something quick when you’re busy, isn’t it? I don't really think about how it’s affecting me, you know? Just get on with things.  Yesterday, I was trying to unload a big crate of turmeric, and I nearly tripped! It was embarrassing, and I had to ask Thando, my assistant, to help me. It made me think, ‘Lwandle, you need to take care of yourself, man!’\n\nThe clinic down the road, the one Dr. Zola runs, it’s a proper place. Clean, bright, and everyone is nice. I went in because my sister, Nomusa, she’s always telling me to get checked. I wasn’t sure why, honestly. I thought it was just an old man’s thing. But Dr. Zola looked at me and said, ‘Lwandle, your blood sugar is a bit high. You need to start moving more, and eat a bit lighter.’ He gave me a little card with some pictures – fruits and vegetables, things like that. He said, ‘Even a short walk every day can make a big difference.’ It sounded a bit scary, to be honest. Walking? I’m used to running around my shop all day! But he said it's important, and he seemed like a good man. He told me to take my insulin properly and to talk to my pharmacist about my medication.  It felt… a little overwhelming, to be honest.\n\nI tried walking, I really did. I started with just ten minutes after closing up the shop. It felt so hard! My legs still ached, and I kept wanting to just sit down and have a cold drink. Then, my cousin, Siyabonga, he’s a fitness trainer, he saw me struggling. He said, ‘Lwandle, you gotta push yourself! Think about the big order coming in next week – Mr. Nkosi wants a huge shipment of chilli peppers. You need to be strong enough to carry those crates!’ That helped a little. But then I had a lekker biltong sandwich for lunch, and my legs felt even worse.  It’s so hard to change, you know?  Everything feels easier when you’re tired. I almost gave up, but I kept thinking about Mr. Nkosi and those chilli peppers.  It's a big order, and I need to be able to handle it.\n\nSlowly, though, things started to feel a bit better. I started taking little walks during my lunch break, just around the shop. I even started adding a few more vegetables to my meals – some spinach in my pap, a bit of tomato with my braai. And guess what? I managed to carry those chilli peppers to Mr. Nkosi without even thinking about my legs! He was really pleased, and I felt proud of myself. It wasn’t easy, but I did it. I think I'm starting to understand that taking care of myself isn’t just about being strong for work; it’s about feeling good, about being able to enjoy life.  And you know what?  I’m even thinking about maybe joining that traditional dancing group down the street. It might be a good way to get some exercise, and it would be fun too!	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0e0ef3c3-8918-42a9-940c-bd49304b664e_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0e0ef3c3-8918-42a9-940c-bd49304b664e_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0e0ef3c3-8918-42a9-940c-bd49304b664e_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0e0ef3c3-8918-42a9-940c-bd49304b664e_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0e0ef3c3-8918-42a9-940c-bd49304b664e_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0e0ef3c3-8918-42a9-940c-bd49304b664e_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0e0ef3c3-8918-42a9-940c-bd49304b664