counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">22a0f9b7-48eb-4ec7-ae8a-08c7aa17ec24</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Hello, my name is Amina Bello, and let me tell you, being a business owner in the busy city can make you forget about your own health! Every morning, I like to eat white bread with jam and quickly rush out to open my little shop. The city never waits for anyone, you know? Last Tuesday, I had a pile of receipts to check, a small but important task before the big monthly report. But what happened? By ten in the morning I felt so tired and a bit dizzy, I mixed up all the numbers and had to start over. I even wondered, 'How come something so simple was so difficult today?'\n\nLater that day, I decided to visit the local clinic nearby for a check-up. The nurse greeted me with a warm smile and said, 'Amina, maybe your food choices are making your blood sugar go up and down.' At first, I laughed and said, 'But I don’t eat sweets all the time!' The nurse patiently explained, 'It’s not just sweets—try to swap white bread for whole grain, add more vegetables, and walk a bit each day. These small changes help your body keep energy steady, so you don’t feel so tired at work.' Her advice sounded simple, but could I really do it every day?\n\nThe next morning, I tried making brown bread with avocado and took a short walk before opening my shop. I felt a bit silly walking around the block and missed my fast breakfast. At lunchtime, I nearly grabbed my normal fizzy drink, but I remembered the nurse’s words. Still, I felt grumpy and nearly gave up—old habits can be tough to break, hey! But I kept reminding myself of the big monthly report I needed to finish well this time. That made me push through the day with the healthier choices.\n\nDay by day, I started feeling less tired in the mornings, and I noticed fewer mistakes in my work. When the big monthly report came, I finished it with a clear head and even impressed my business partner with my neat records. Could you believe it, I felt proud of myself for trying new foods and a bit of exercise! Now, I’m not scared to keep learning new things for my health—maybe next week I’ll even try a dance class for fun!	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/22a0f9b7-48eb-4ec7-ae8a-08c7aa17ec24_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.s