ionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "classic_change", "audio_prompts": ["Inside her small urban shop, Amina Bello is heard shuffling receipts on her counter, her voice slightly breathless as she mutters numbers, then sighs in frustration. There's the faint rustle of paper and distant city traffic sounds through the window. Her tone is puzzled as she says, 'Why am I struggling so much today?'", "Female nurse nearby greets Amina Bello with a welcoming, mid-range voice in clear South African English. The nurse explains simple dietary tips, her voice soft and friendly. Amina responds with a surprised laugh and a mildly skeptical tone. Background includes the low hum of clinic activity and muffled voices.", "On a city street, Amina Bello's footsteps echo on the pavement. She breathes steadily but sounds uncertain. Packaging crinkles in her shopping bag. She pauses, sighs, and murmurs, 'Let me just try today,' before continuing her slow walk. The city’s mild morning noises and distant cars are audible.", "Inside her shop, Amina Bello types on a calculator, her voice light and cheerful as she says, 'I did it!' Her business partner, a young man standing nearby, chuckles softly in genuine surprise. Sunlight streams in, and the environment feels warm and optimistic, with the faint hum of midday city life."], "image_prompts": ["Amina Bello, a woman in her late twenties, sits at a cluttered shop counter in an urban city, wearing a neat business dress, holding a half-eaten slice of white bread with jam, receipts scattered around her. She looks confused and a bit tired, rubbing her head with her free hand. The city street glows in the morning sun through the window. (medium shot)", "Amina Bello stands inside a clean, bright clinic, facing a friendly female nurse in uniform. The nurse gestures gently towards a colourful food chart, while Amina holds her handbag against her chest, listening with raised eyebrows, slightly defensive but curious. Clinic posters about healthy food are on the wall. (medium shot)", "Amina Bello is outside on a city sidewalk in the morning, carrying a small brown paper bag of groceries. She walks slowly, looking unsure, glancing down the street while adjusting her bag strap. The city shopfronts and parked cars stretch into the distance. (medium shot)", "Amina Bello sits at her business counter, carefully typing on a calculator with a stack of tidy receipts next to her, a big smile on her face. Sunlight highlights her determined posture. Her business partner, a young man, stands nearby, looking pleasantly surprised at her work. (medium shot, business partner standing nearby)"], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 1.9408850491046905, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some traditional Hausa vegan meals available in Kano that are suitable for someone managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find fresh, healthy, and affordable vegan foods in urban Kano city for my daily meals?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local Nigerian snacks or meals that won't raise my blood sugar and fit a vegan diet?\\",\\n  \\"How does being a Hausa Muslim woman in Kano influence vegan food choices during Ramadan while managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What social activities are popular among female business owners in Kano for staying physically active 5-7 days a week?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any community events or support groups in urban Kano for women with diabetes looking for healthy lifestyle advice?\\",\\n  \\"Can you suggest practical ways to incorporate traditional Hausa storytelling into my daily routine while balancing diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"What urban restaurants or food vendors in Kano offer vegan and diabetic-friendly meal options?\\",\\n  \\"How can I adapt Hausa culinary practices to follow a vegan diet and keep my blood glucose stable?\\",\\n  \\"Are there reputable local healthcare professionals or clinics in Kano who specialize in diabetes management for women my age?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best ways to stay social with friends and family in Kano while adhering to vegan and diabetic dietary restrictions?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any Islamic or Hausa cultural practices in Kano that influence healthy eating habits for women with diabetes?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Relevant fields: Business owner, Urban residence, Female, Age 25-34, Storytelling hobby, Regular healthcare access, No disability, No smoking or alcohol, Basic knowledge gap about everyday foods and exercise for blood sugar, Feels fatigue and discouragement, Motivated by work tasks.", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "disability", "occupation", "hobbies", "healthcare_access", "tobacco", "alcohol", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
