en)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">18f70b87-7347-480f-b7cc-abc0540cc519</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Hayi bo, life, isn't it something? I'm Aminu Bello, and I’m a carpenter, a good one if I do say so myself. I build those lovely wooden window frames you see in the newer houses around here in Soweto. But lately, things haven't been so smooth. I always start my day with a nice strong cup of tea and a vetkoek from Mama Rose's stall – they're just so good, you know? Then I work, work, work. But I find myself getting tired quickly these days. Just last week, I promised old Mr. Dlamini I'd fix his kitchen cupboard door by Friday. I thought, easy peasy! But by Thursday evening, I was so sleepy, I just couldn't focus. Ended up leaving it unfinished. Mr. Dlamini wasn't happy, and honestly, I wasn't either. I just kept thinking, what’s happening to me?\n\nMy wife, Aisha, she saw I was worried. She took me to the clinic, you know, the one near the taxi rank. The sister, she was very kind. She checked my sugar levels and said, 'Aminu, you have diabetes, and it looks like you're eating too much sugar, especially late at night.' I was a bit surprised, to be honest. I didn’t think late-night snacks were such a big deal! She explained that when I eat sweet things before bed, my body struggles to deal with the sugar while I'm sleeping, and that makes me tired. She told me to try and have a small plate of pap and some fish instead of those koeksisters I love. She said, 'It won't be easy, but it will help you feel stronger and work better.' I thought, pap and fish? Instead of something sweet? It sounded…difficult.\n\nOkay, so I tried the pap and fish. First night, I was dreaming about those koeksisters, I tell you! It was hard, really hard. I even sneaked a small piece of chocolate one evening, thinking, 'Just one won't hurt.' But the next day, I felt sluggish again. And I had a big job coming up – building a whole set of doors for a new house in Diepkloof. It was a good job, a lot of money, and I *needed* to be at my best. That's what kept me going. I reminded myself that if I wanted to finish those doors properly, I had to stick to the sister’s advice. I started having a small glass of milk with my pap too, Aisha suggested it. It helped a little.\n\nSlowly, things started to change. The tiredness wasn't as bad. I found myself waking up feeling a bit more rested. I still missed my late-night sweets, but I started finding other things to enjoy – a nice cup of rooibos tea, for example. And those doors in Diepkloof? I finished them on time, and Mr. Nkosi, the owner, was very pleased! He even gave me a bonus. I felt so proud, not just of the doors, but of myself. I realised that taking care of my health wasn't just about avoiding sickness, it was about being able to do the things I love, and provide for my family. Maybe, just maybe, this healthy eating thing isn’t so bad after all. I'm even thinking about asking the sister for some tips on getting more exercise. What do you know, maybe I can even start running again!	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/18f70b87-7347-480f-b7cc-abc0540cc519_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/18f70b87-7347-480f-b7cc-abc0540cc519_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/18f70b87-7347-480f-b7cc-abc0540cc519_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/18f70b87-7347-480f-b7cc-abc0540cc519_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/18f70b87-7347-480f-b7cc-abc0540cc519_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/18f70b87-7347-480f-b7cc-abc0540cc519_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/18f70b87-7347-480f-b7cc-abc0540cc519_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/18f70b87-7347-480f-b7cc-abc0540cc519_3.mp3}	I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? 	diet	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 13:29:36.275898+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gemma-3-27b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Amina Bello is a 18-24 year old, \\nCulture: Hau