c – muffled conversations, beeping medical equipment, the shuffling of papers – create a background ambiance. Nurse X says, 'It's important to manage your sugar levels, Aminu. Try swapping those sweets for something healthier.'", "Aminu Bello, speaking quietly to himself, almost a whisper. The sound of a spoon scraping against a plate. He sounds conflicted and frustrated. A faint sound of a television playing in the background. 'Pap and fish… instead of koeksisters… It’s just…so hard.' A small, defeated sigh. A brief rustling sound, like unwrapping a chocolate wrapper.", "Aminu Bello, speaking with a noticeably more energetic and confident tone. The sound of hammering and sawing, but now it’s rhythmic and purposeful. A friendly voice, Mr. Nkosi X, is heard in the background, offering praise. Aminu Bello says, with a laugh, 'I finished them on time! And Mr. Nkosi, he was very pleased! Maybe, just maybe, this healthy eating thing isn’t so bad after all.'"], "image_prompts": ["Medium shot of Aminu Bello, a middle-aged man with a weathered face, sitting on a stool in his small carpentry workshop in Soweto. He's looking down at a half-finished wooden window frame, his brow furrowed in concentration. Dust motes dance in the shafts of sunlight filtering through the corrugated iron roof. He is slightly slumped, holding a measuring tape loosely in his hand, a half-eaten vetkoek sits on a nearby workbench. Aminu Bello's expression suggests fatigue and frustration.", "Wide shot of Aminu Bello sitting in a brightly lit, but slightly crowded clinic waiting room in Soweto. He’s looking at a nurse, a young woman X with a kind expression, who is explaining something to him, pointing at a chart. Aminu Bello is leaning forward slightly, listening intently, but his body language suggests a degree of skepticism. The background shows other patients waiting, and posters about health awareness on the walls.", "Medium shot of Aminu Bello in his kitchen, looking somewhat dejectedly at a plate of pap and fish. He’s holding a small piece of chocolate in his other hand, seemingly wrestling with a decision. The kitchen is simply furnished, with a few pots and pans visible. Dim lighting from a single overhead bulb. Aminu Bello's face reflects internal conflict and temptation.", "Medium shot of Aminu Bello standing proudly in front of a newly constructed set of wooden doors in Diepkloof. He’s smiling broadly, and his posture is upright and confident. Mr. Nkosi, a man X, is shaking his hand. The background shows the partially built house, bathed in the warm light of the late afternoon sun. Aminu Bello's expression is one of accomplishment and satisfaction."], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 83.51873853267767, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are the best vegetarian Hausa dishes available in Kano city that are suitable for someone with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How do young male traders in urban Kano balance their work and blood sugar management with regular exercise schedules?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local support groups or diabetes education programs in inner-city Kano for Hausa Muslim adults aged 18-24?\\",\\n  \\"What is the cultural perception of weekly alcohol consumption among Hausa Muslims in Kano, and does it impact diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"Which physical activities are most popular and accessible for urban youth in Kano that help control type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How do public transportation and city layout in Kano affect opportunities for regular physical activity for working adults like me?\\",\\n  \\"Does the local healthcare clinic in Kano offer diabetes management resources tailored to vegetarian diets?\\",\\n  \\"What are the challenges young male traders in Kano face in maintaining a healthy lifestyle, and what coping strategies are common in the Hausa community?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any traditional Hausa herbal remedies used in Kano for type 2 diabetes, and how effective are they compared to modern medication?\\",\\n  \\"What storytelling or social community events in urban Kano can help promote health awareness among young adults?\\",\\n  \\"How can I incorporate regular physical activity into my daily routine as a market trader in Kano city, given my responsibilities and environment?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any Muslim-friendly gyms or sports centers in Kano where I can work out 3-4 days a week without compromising my religious values?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "name", "gender", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "health_conditions", "healthcare_access", "t2d_status", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
