      </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">1-2 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Close friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">f9970f6c-6492-498c-b399-6c0a0310e15e</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gymâ€”what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Chinedu, and I sell grains here in Kano. It’s a good job, keeps a roof over my head and food on the table. Most days, I start early, sorting millet and rice, making sure it’s good for the market. I eat a lot of rice, you know? Just a big plate, every meal. Sometimes, I’ll throw in some beans, if I have the money. My wife, Fatima, she makes sure we have some vegetables, but honestly, sometimes it’s just too much rice. I don't really think about my blood sugar much, to be honest. My uncle told me about it once, but it felt like a long time ago.  Do I really need to worry about that when I’m just trying to work and provide for my family?\n\nYesterday, I was helping my brother, Musa, load a truck with sacks of sorghum. It was a hot day, and we were moving fast. I was sweating, and I felt a bit dizzy, but I just pushed through. I thought, ‘Chinedu, you need to be strong for Musa.’ But halfway through, my legs just felt weak, and I almost dropped a sack. Musa shouted at me, saying I was being careless. I felt embarrassed, and my head started to spin worse. It was a proper mess, and we had to stop for a bit. I just grabbed a cold bottle of Zobo and tried to think about something else. I was worried, not about the sacks, but about feeling like this again.\n\nDr. Ibrahim at the clinic explained things to me. He said my body was telling me something – that the rice and beans weren’t agreeing with my blood sugar. He showed me a picture of a sugar test, and he said it was important to check it regularly. He told me to eat smaller portions of rice, and to add more vegetables and fruits to my meals. He even suggested some Hausa dishes like Tuwo Shinkafa with a bit of okra – that sounds good, doesn’t it? He said a little bit of sweetness from the fruits and vegetables would help.  It felt a bit strange, changing things I’d done for so long, but he said it was for my health, and for Musa too.  I promised to try, really try.\n\nIt hasn’t been easy	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f9970f6c-6492-498c-b399-6c0a0310e15e_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f9970f6c-6492-498c-b399-6c0a0310e15e_1.png,htt