be8aadcb-4c70-40bc-b9ea-e903417f5edc	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b819-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Culture (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hausa</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which province do you live in? (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kano</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your religion?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Islam</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Name</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Chinelo Okafor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gender  (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Female</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Age (select 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">25-34</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How would you describe access to food in your local community or area?    (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have a disability? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What is your current occupation?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Trader</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What best describes your daily routine right now?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What hobbies or interests do you enjoy regularly? (select all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Farming-related activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Which activities or routines are most important to you? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you currently have other health conditions besides diabetes? (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">E â€” Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently taking medication or following a treatment for diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What kind of healthcare resources do you regularly access or use?  </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you have regular access to healthcare services?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How often do you access healthcare services?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Are you currently living with Type 2 Diabetes</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you smoke tobacco products? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Do you consume alcohol beverages? </td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">How many days per week do you participate in moderate to vigorous physical activity?  (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Select any dietary preferences or restrictions you may have (choose 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Who forms part of your regular support network?  (check all that apply)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Study Number</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">be8aadcb-4c70-40bc-b9ea-e903417f5edc</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">What are your main personal health goals? (You may select more than one)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I wake up early like every day, before the sun even shows. I go to my shop near the market, and I sell dried fish and plantain. My body feels heavy, like it’s carrying all the work. I don’t think much about my blood sugar — I just eat what’s on hand. I eat late at night because I have to finish my work. But why do I feel tired? Why can’t I move when I go to the shop? I don’t know. I just do it. I tell myself, ‘One more day, then I’ll rest.’ But the next day, I feel worse. I don’t even want to walk to the market. I just sit and watch the sun go down. What if I could feel strong again? What if I could walk without my legs shaking? I don’t know how to fix it, but I know I need to try something new.\n\nLast month, I went to the health clinic. I told the nurse about my tiredness. She listened, and then she said, ‘Chinelo, your blood sugar is high, and your blood pressure is also high. That’s why you feel tired. You need to eat better and move your body.’ I said, ‘But I don’t have time. I have to sell fish every day.’ She smiled and said, ‘You don’t need to stop selling. You just need to eat small meals, like before the sun rises. And you can walk with your basket to the market — just 10 minutes a day. It helps your blood sugar go down.’ I said, ‘Can I do that?’ She said, ‘Yes. And you can start tomorrow.’ I didn’t believe it at first. But I thought — if I can walk just 10 minutes, maybe I can feel better. Maybe I can do more for my family.\n\nI tried walking with my basket. But on the first day, I was so tired. I didn’t even make it to the market. I sat under the tree near the mosque and cried. I said to myself, ‘I can’t do this. I am not strong like before.’ My husband said, ‘Chinelo, you don’t have to be strong all the time. Just walk a little. You will feel better.’ I tried again the next day. I walked to the market and back. I didn’t eat much, just a small bowl of rice and a little salad. I felt weak, but I didn’t stop. I told myself, ‘I have a big task coming — I have to grow a small garden for my family. If I can grow vegetables, I can feed them with halal food. That means I need to be healthy.’ So I kept walking. I kept eating small meals. I didn’t feel strong, but I felt like I was trying.\n\nNow, I walk every morning. I walk with my basket, and I carry a small pot of water. I eat a small meal before I go to the market. I feel better. My blood sugar is not as high. I don’t feel tired when I go to work. I even talk to my neighbours and say, ‘Chinelo walked today. She feels strong.’ I still have a big task — to grow a garden. But now I know I can do it. I know that walking helps my body. I know that small changes make a big difference. I don’t need to be perfect. I just need to keep trying. And every day, I feel a little stronger. Maybe one day, I will grow enough vegetables to feed my whole family. And I will be proud of how I took care of my body.\n\nI used to think that being tired was just part of life. Now I know it’s not. My body is like a car — if you don’t take care of it, it breaks down. But if you drive it gently, it lasts longer. I don’t have to stop working. I just need to move a little. I don’t need to eat big meals. I just need to eat small, healthy food. And I don’t need to walk far — just 10 minutes a day. I am not a doctor, but I am learning. I am learning to listen to my body. And every time I walk, I feel a little more like myself. I feel like I can do more. I feel like I can grow. I feel like I can help my family. And that makes me happy.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/be8aadcb-4c70-40bc-b9ea-e903417f5edc_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/be8aadcb-4c70-40bc-b9ea-e903417f5edc_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/be8aadcb-4c70-40bc-b9ea-e903417f5edc_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/be8aadcb-4c70-40bc-b9ea-e903417f5edc_3.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/be8aadcb-4c70-40bc-b9ea-e903417f5edc_4.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supa