:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "en", "story_arc": "iteration", "audio_prompts": ["Chinelo Okafor sitting on a wooden bench, breathing slowly and deeply, her voice soft and tired, saying 'I don’t know why I feel like this…', background sound of distant market calls, wind rustling dry leaves, low hum of a nearby motorbike, Chinelo Okafor’s voice slightly muffled by the fabric of her dress, volume low, pacing slow, pauses between sentences", "Nurse and Chinelo Okafor speaking in a clinic room, nurse saying 'You just need to walk a little', Chinelo responding 'Can I do that?', both voices clear and calm, moderate speed, soft background of a clock ticking and distant radio music, Chinelo’s voice slightly rising at the end of her question, natural breathing between words", "Chinelo Okafor sitting on a stone wall, breathing heavily, her voice shaky and low, whispering 'I can’t do it… I am not strong anymore', wind blowing her hair, distant children laughing from the market, Chinelo’s voice slightly strained, breaths irregular, volume soft and fading into silence", "Chinelo Okafor walking slowly along a dusty path, her footsteps light and steady, voice steady and calm, saying 'I will walk today, even if I feel tired', background sound of birds chirping, distant market noise, wind in the trees, Chinelo’s voice clear and smooth, moderate pace, natural pauses between sentences", "Chinelo Okafor planting seeds in a clay pot, her voice warm and proud, saying 'I can grow this. I can feed my family', soft background of soil being turned, birds chirping, light breeze, Chinelo’s voice clear and full of hope, volume steady, emotion warm and genuine"], "image_prompts": ["Chinelo Okafor sitting on a wooden bench under a large baobab tree in the early morning, her hands resting on her knees, eyes closed, looking tired, with the dusty market path behind her, sunlight filtering through the leaves, dry soil texture visible, soft golden light, morning haze, Chinelo Okafor’s face showing fatigue and quiet resignation", "Medium shot of Chinelo Okafor standing in front of a small health clinic with a white sign that says 'Health Clinic Kano', holding a small notebook, her hands slightly trembling, a nurse in a white uniform talking to her, both facing the camera, warm indoor lighting with natural window light, clean white walls, Chinelo Okafor looking hopeful but uncertain", "Chinelo Okafor sitting on a low stone wall near a mosque, her feet dangling, basket in her lap, eyes closed, breathing slowly, a small pot of water beside her, sunlight hitting her face from the side, dusty ground with dry grass, wind moving her hair slightly, Chinelo Okafor looking sad and defeated", "Wide shot of Chinelo Okafor walking with a small basket on her arm, carrying a pot of water, walking along a dusty market path in Kano, sunlight shining on her face, her hands slightly raised to balance the basket, her feet moving steadily, green plant leaves visible in the background, texture of worn sandals and dry soil, Chinelo Okafor looking determined and focused", "Chinelo Okafor standing in a small backyard garden, planting seeds in a clay pot, her hands working the soil, sunlight bright, green leaves growing beside her, a small wooden table with a notebook open, her face showing pride and calm, soft natural light, dirt texture visible on her hands, Chinelo Okafor smiling gently"], "language_code": "en-NG", "avg_time_taken": 52.271640586853025, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are healthy and affordable lactose-free Nigerian meals that are commonly available in urban Kano for someone with diabetes and hypertension?\\",\\n  \\"How can a female trader in Kano city balance a busy work schedule with recommended exercise routines to help manage type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there traditional Hausa farming activities or social events in Kano that count as physical activity for diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"What is the impact of occasional late-night eating, especially of Hausa urban foods, on blood sugar levels in people with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find support groups or counselling for young women with diabetes in Kano city, Nigeria?\\",\\n  \\"Are there specific Hausa herbal or traditional remedies used in Kano for managing hypertension and diabetes, and are they safe to use with insulin or metformin?\\",\\n  \\"What are common breakfast options in Kano that are lactose-free and suitable for people with diabetes and hypertension?\\",\\n  \\"How does rare tobacco smoking affect blood pressure and blood sugar control in Nigerian women with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there government or NGO programs in Kano that help women traders access affordable diabetes medications and regular healthcare?\\",\\n  \\"How can I include physical activity into my routine as a trader in urban Kano when I have no free days for formal exercise?\\",\\n  \\"What cultural practices among Hausa women in Kano support healthier eating habits for managing diabetes and hypertension?\\",\\n  \\"Is it safe for me to fast during Ramadan as a Nigerian Muslim woman with type 2 diabetes and hypertension, and what precautions should I take?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "culture", "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent