creveria o acesso a alimentos em sua comunidade ou área local? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem alguma deficiência? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Qual é a sua ocupação atual?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Maize farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">O que melhor descreve sua rotina diária atualmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais hobbies ou interesses você pratica regularmente? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Football (soccer)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais atividades ou rotinas são mais importantes para você?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você possui atualmente outras condições de saúde além do diabetes? (selecione todas as que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente tomando medicamentos ou seguindo algum tratamento para diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Que tipo de recursos de saúde você acessa ou utiliza regularmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem acesso regular a serviços de saúde?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Com que frequência você acessa serviços de saúde? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Occasionally (less than once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Cultura (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Xichangana</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente vivendo com Diabetes Tipo 2?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você fuma produtos de tabaco?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você consome bebidas alcoólicas?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quantos dias por semana você pratica atividade física de intensidade moderada a vigorosa? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">1–2 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Selecione quaisquer preferências ou restrições alimentares que você possa ter (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quem faz parte da sua rede regular de apoio? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Número do Estudo</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">6979bab4-c012-4c24-8ad7-741706d4787d</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais são seus principais objetivos pessoais de saúde? (você pode selecionar mais de um)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">What kinds of exercises are safe and helpful for someone with diabetes?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Eita, a vida não é fácil, né? Eu sou o Nuru Salimo, e trabalho como ajudante de pedreiro aqui em Maputo. Acordo cedo, tomo um café forte com pão doce – porque, vamos ser sinceros, quem tem tempo para cozinhar um café da manhã saudável? – e já saio correndo para o trabalho. Hoje, o mestre pediu para eu carregar uns sacos de cimento para o segundo andar. Parecia fácil, mas, ai, ai, no meio do caminho, senti um cansaço danado, a cabeça girando… quase deixei os sacos caírem! Que vergonha!\n\nFui lá na clínica perto da minha casa, a enfermeira, a Dona Emilia, me examinou e disse: 'Nuru, você tem pressão alta e diabetes, sabia?'. Eu fiquei surpreso! Nunca tinha pensado que comer tanto pão doce e não fazer exercício podia me fazer mal. Ela explicou que eu precisava começar a caminhar, pelo menos 30 minutos por dia, e comer mais vegetais, menos açúcar. Confesso que pensei: 'Caminhar? Com todo o trabalho que eu tenho?'. Mas ela disse que se eu não cuidasse da minha saúde, ia ficar cada vez mais cansado e não conseguiria nem carregar os sacos de cimento. Isso me assustou.\n\nTentei seguir o conselho da Dona Emilia. Comecei a caminhar depois do trabalho, mas no primeiro dia, só consegui uns 10 minutos. As pernas doíam, o suor escorria… e eu ainda tinha que preparar o jantar para a família! Quase desisti, pensando no grande trabalho que o mestre me pediu: ajudar a levantar uma parede inteira no sábado. Se eu estivesse fraco como da última vez, não ia conseguir. Mas lembrei do olhar preocupado da enfermeira e continuei, um dia de cada vez.\n\nCom o tempo, a caminhada foi ficando mais fácil. Comecei a sentir menos cansaço e até a dormir melhor. Troquei o pão doce por frutas e legumes, e o café forte por chá. No sábado, quando fui ajudar o mestre, levantei a parede sem problemas! Senti um orgulho danado de mim mesmo. O mestre até me elogiou! Agora, estou pensando em fazer aulas de ginástica na praça perto de casa. Quem sabe, né? A saúde é a gente que constrói, tijolo por tijolo.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6979bab4-c012-4c24-8ad7-741706d4787d_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6979bab4-c012-4c24-8ad7-741706d4787d_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6979bab4-c012-4c24-8ad7-741706d4787d_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6979bab4-c012-4c24-8ad7-741706d4787d_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6979bab4-c012-4c24-8ad7-741706d4787d_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6979bab4-c012-4c24-8ad7-741706d4787d_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6979bab4-c012-4c24-8ad7-741706d4787d_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6979bab4-c012-4c24-8ad7-741706d4787d_3.mp3}	Que tipos de exercícios são seguros e benéficos para alguém com diabetes?	exercise	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 14:15:26.974668+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gemma-3-27b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Luzia Mavota is a 45–54 year old, \\nCulture: Xichangana female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Small-scale trader, lives in a Suburban (near city or town) in Maputo. Disability: she has none. Religion: Atheism. Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Traditional dancing. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: Hypertension (high blood pressure). Diet restrictions: Kosher. Smoking: No. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 3–4 days. Support network: Close friends. Health goals: I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?. her food access Easy access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Luzia Mavota and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in Portuguese that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken Portuguese, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in Portuguese.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in Portuguese.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "pt", "story_arc": "crisis_avoidance", "audio_prompts": ["Nuru Salimo's voice, slightly breathless and strained, describing his fatigue after attempting to carry cement bags. Sounds of construction in the background – hammering, shouting, the scraping of tools. He sighs heavily at the end of the sentence. Nuru's voice conveys a sense of frustration and embarrassment. 'Eita, a vida não é fácil, né?'", "Dona Emilia, a woman in her 50s, speaking with a calm and reassuring tone, explaining Nuru Salimo's health condition. Her voice is nearby and clear. Nuru Salimo responds with a hesitant 'Ah, tá…' after each explanation, his voice soft and slightly confused. Background sounds of a quiet clinic – muffled conversations, the whir of a fan. Nuru's voice has a questioning tone.", "Nuru Salimo's labored breathing and footsteps on a dusty road. He's muttering to himself, 'Preciso continuar… preciso continuar…' His voice is strained and determined, but also filled with discomfort. Sounds of distant traffic and children playing in the background. Nuru’s breathing gets heavier with each step.", "Nuru Salimo's voice, now stronger and more confident, laughing with X, a young man, as they work on the construction site. Sounds of hammering and bricklaying. X responds with a cheerful 'Isso aí, Nuru!' Nuru's voice is filled with pride and satisfaction. Background noise of a busy construction site."], "image_prompts": ["Medium shot of Nuru Salimo, a middle-aged man with a weathered face, leaning heavily against a stack of cement bags on a construction site in Maputo, Mozambique. He is visibly fatigued, forehead beaded with sweat, eyes slightly closed. The background shows unfinished brickwork and other construction workers. Lighting is harsh midday sun, creating strong shadows. Nuru's posture is slumped, shoulders rounded.", "Wide shot of Nuru Salimo sitting in a brightly lit but simple healthcare clinic in Maputo, Mozambique. He's looking at a nurse, Dona Emilia, a woman in her 50s with a kind expression, who is holding a chart. Nuru's hands are clasped in his lap, and he has a slightly hesitant expression. The clinic walls are painted a pale blue. The lighting is fluorescent and slightly sterile.", "Candid shot of Nuru Salimo walking slowly along a dusty road in Maputo, Mozambique, during sunset. He's wearing worn work boots and simple clothing. His face shows a mix of determination and discomfort. In the background, you can see modest houses and people returning home from work. Nuru's shoulders are slightly hunched, but his gaze is forward.", "Medium shot of Nuru Salimo smiling and confidently lifting a brick into place on a wall at a construction site in Maputo, Mozambique. He is working alongside another construction worker, X, a young man in his 20s, who is offering support. The lighting is bright and sunny. Nuru's posture is upright and strong, his face radiating pride."], "language_code": "pt-PT", "avg_time_taken": 79.50005376033293, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are common physical activities suitable for a 35-44 year old male maize farmer with type 2 diabetes and hypertension living in urban Maputo, Mozambique, following Islamic and Xichangana cultural practices?\\",\\n  \\"Are there culturally appropriate, diabetes-friendly football (soccer) clubs or groups in Maputo city?\\",\\n  \\"How can an urban maize farmer with occasional healthcare visits and limited social support manage high blood pressure and type 2 diabetes in Maputo?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find local resources in Maputo for healthy, Kosher-compliant meals that fit Xichangana and Islamic traditions for someone with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What exercises are popular and safe in Maputo for adult men with hypertension and diabetes who attend a local healthcare clinic occasionally?\\",\\n  \\"How do traditional Xichangana or Mozambican herbal remedies for diabetes interact with insulin or oral medications?\\",\\n  \\"Are there diabetes education or support groups in Maputo for men who live alone and have limited family support?\\",\\n  \\"What is the best way for a busy working adult in Maputo with easy access to healthy foods to plan weekly exercise with only 1–2 days available per week?\\",\\n  \\"How can I incorporate physical activity into my routine as a maize farmer in an urban area, considering the climate and local infrastructure in Maputo?\\",\\n  \\"Which football facilities or exercise centers in Maputo are welcoming to practicing Muslims and Xichangana community members with health conditions like mine?\\",\\n  \\"What are the typical blood pressure and diabetes management strategies used by men of the Xichangana culture in Maputo's urban areas who live alone?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local healthcare professionals in Maputo who specialize in diabetes care for adult men following Islamic dietary laws and Kosher restrictions?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "disability", "activities", "health_conditions", "healthcare_resources", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
cf29c0db-d403-4983-93a1-4a564b6caa1f	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b815-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Em qual província você vive? (selecione 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Maputo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Qual é a sua religião?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Atheism</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Nome</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Anabela Tivane</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gênero (selecione 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Female</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Idade (selecione 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">25–34</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Como você descreveria sua comunidade ou área local? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Como você descreveria o acesso a alimentos em sua comunidade ou área local? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem alguma deficiência? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Qual é a sua ocupação atual?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Subsistence farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">O que melhor descreve sua rotina diária atualmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais hobbies ou interesses você pratica regularmente? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Farming &amp; gardening (often more than a hobby, but also a leisure activity)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais atividades ou rotinas são mais importantes para você?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você possui atualmente outras condições de saúde além do diabetes? (selecione todas as que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente tomando medicamentos ou seguindo algum tratamento para diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Que tipo de recursos de saúde você acessa ou utiliza regularmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem acesso regular a serviços de saúde?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Com que frequência você acessa serviços de saúde? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Cultura (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Xichangana</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente vivendo com Diabetes Tipo 2?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você fuma produtos de tabaco?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você consome bebidas alcoólicas?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quantos dias por semana você pratica atividade física de intensidade moderada a vigorosa? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5–7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Selecione quaisquer preferências ou restrições alimentares que você possa ter (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quem faz parte da sua rede regular de apoio? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Número do Estudo</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">cf29c0db-d403-4983-93a1-4a564b6caa1f</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais são seus principais objetivos pessoais de saúde? (você pode selecionar mais de um)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Eu acordei cedo como sempre, pronta para regar o jardim. Será que você já tentou puxar a mangueira quando está a pensar noutras coisas? Eu só estava a pensar no mercado—tinha de separar as melhores cenouras para vender amanhã! Peguei logo uma fatia de pão branco com bastante manteiga, porque é o que sempre comi antes de trabalhar. Mas, logo no meio do pequeno trabalho, fiquei tonta e cansada. O que será que eu fiz de errado?\n\nMais tarde, fui ao posto de saúde. Enfermeira Tanya, que já me conhece, sorriu para mim. “Anabela, esse pão branco vai te levantar o açúcar,” ela disse devagar. Eu fiquei desconfiada, mexendo as mãos sem jeito. Ela explicou: ‘Troque o pão por uma fatia de pão integral, coma pepino e tomate, use ovos, prefere frutas inteiras. Sempre pense: isso vai me deixar forte o dia todo?’ Parecia estranho, mas e se funcionasse mesmo?\n\nNo dia seguinte tentei comer só ovos cozidos, pão integral e iogurte natural, como a enfermeira sugeriu. Queria sentir-me animada, mas meu corpo parecia pedir o velho café doce e bolo frito. Quase desisti! Mas lembrei: amanhã vou colher batatas para toda a vila. Não posso ficar de cama, preciso ficar bem.\n\nFui tentando cada dia, devagar. Aos poucos, minhas manhãs no jardim ficaram mais leves, o cansaço foi sumindo. No grande dia da colheita, consegui carregar meus cestos e mostrar para todos. Sabe, agora já penso duas vezes antes de comer algo, e fiquei aberta a testar mais dessas dicas para ficar firme sem crise.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/cf29c0db-d403-4983-93a1-4a564b6caa1f_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/cf29c0db-d403-4983-93a1-4a564b6caa1f_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/cf29c0db-d403-4983-93a1-4a564b6caa1f_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/cf29c0db-d403-4983-93a1-4a564b6caa1f_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/cf29c0db-d403-4983-93a1-4a564b6caa1f_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/cf29c0db-d403-4983-93a1-4a564b6caa1f_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/cf29c0db-d403-4983-93a1-4a564b6caa1f_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/cf29c0db-d403-4983-93a1-4a564b6caa1f_3.mp3}	Quais alimentos do dia a dia posso comer que não façam a minha glicemia subir rapidamente?	diet	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 14:15:21.486865+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gpt-4.1", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Célio Mavundza is a 18–24 year old, \\nCulture: Rhonga male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Subsistence farmer, lives in a Suburban (near city or town) in Maputo. Disability: he has none. Religion: Christianity (Zion Christian Church). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Only when necessary. Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: None. Diet restrictions: Kosher. Smoking: Yes. Alcohol drinking: Yes. Physical activity: 3–4 days. Support network: Close friends. Health goals: Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?. his food access Easy access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Célio Mavundza and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the mos