anaging type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can I incorporate my love for traditional games like Ntxuva and damas into regular physical activity to help control my blood sugar?\\",\\n  \\"Where in Maputo can I find support groups or community resources for young women living alone and managing type 2 diabetes with limited social support?\\",\\n  \\"How does working as a cassava farmer in Maputo affect my dietary choices and diabetes management, and are there specific local foods I should prioritize or avoid?\\",\\n  \\"What is the recommended snacking frequency for a female adult with type 2 diabetes who does physical activity 5–7 days a week and has easy access to healthy foods in Maputo?\\",\\n  \\"Are there resources at local clinics or hospitals in Maputo that provide culturally tailored diabetes dietary counseling for Xichangana-speaking patients?\\",\\n  \\"What are the best ways for weekly tobacco smokers with type 2 diabetes to reduce their health risks, specifically for women in Mozambique?\\",\\n  \\"How can attending local Zion Christian Church events impact my diabetes management, especially regarding communal meals or fasting traditions?\\",\\n  \\"Are there Halal-certified stores or markets in Maputo where I can easily find diabetic-friendly snack foods?\\",\\n  \\"What are the advantages and disadvantages of using herbal or traditional medicines for diabetes alongside insulin and oral medications in Mozambique?\\",\\n  \\"How do socializing patterns in urban Maputo affect healthy eating habits for people living alone with type 2 diabetes?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "su