e waiting to greet her, Tariro Chisango.", "Tariro Chisango, in her kitchen, chopping fresh vegetables and fruits, with a look of determination on her face, Tariro Chisango.", "A medium shot of Tariro Chisango, dancing with a group of friends, with a big smile on her face, Tariro Chisango."], "language_code": "pt-PT", "avg_time_taken": 5.3813682416590245, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are effective home-based physical activities suitable for a female fish processor living in urban Maputo who has type 2 diabetes and no gym access?\\",\\n  \\"Are there Xichangana traditional dance routines that can be adapted as daily exercise for adults with diabetes in Maputo city?\\",\\n  \\"How can I maintain a vegan diet with easy access to healthy foods in Maputo, Mozambique, especially for diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"What local Maputo foods are both vegan and supportive for type 2 diabetes control?\\",\\n  \\"Are there safe ways to quit daily tobacco smoking and reduce high alcohol consumption, specifically for young adult women in urban Mozambique?\\",\\n  \\"How does diabetes care in Maputo health clinics address the needs of urban female fish processors who live an inactive lifestyle?\\",\\n  \\"What household items commonly found in urban Maputo can I use to create a simple exercise routine at home tailored for my condition?\\",\\n  \\"Are there social or community support groups for vegan adults with diabetes in Maputo who also enjoy traditional dancing?\\",\\n  \\"What are the risks of being physically inactive with type 2 diabetes, considering I work long hours processing fish in Maputo city?\\",\\n  \\"Can herbal or traditional medicines from Xichangana culture in Mozambique help with managing diabetes alongside insulin or oral medications?\\",\\n  \\"Which exercises can I do at home that won’t disrupt my daily routine as a fish processor and are suitable for someone who is not