: ["Close-up, Celestino Nhacete, 50s, male, sitting at a wooden table, drinking strong coffee, sunlight streaming through a window, rural Mozambican kitchen, simple, worn furniture, expression of quiet determination.", "Medium shot, Celestino Nhacete, 50s, male, talking with Dona Maria, a friendly-looking nurse, in a simple clinic waiting room, bright but slightly worn walls, medical charts on a table, a concerned but hopeful expression on Celestino’s face.", "Wide shot, Celestino Nhacete, 50s, male, struggling to pull a heavy wooden plow through a field, sweat on his brow, a slightly blurred background of the African landscape, a sense of effort and strain.", "Close-up, Celestino Nhacete, 50s, male, walking slowly along a dirt path, a gentle smile on his face, a bright blue sky overhead, a sense of contentment and well-being."], "language_code": "pt-PT", "avg_time_taken": 8.3145438402127, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some recommended physical activities suitable for a 45–54-year-old male with type 2 diabetes living in a suburban area near Maputo, Mozambique?\\",\\n  \\"What locally available foods in suburban Maputo support a Kosher diet and help manage type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can I incorporate social storytelling and family gatherings into my physical activity routine given my Rhonga cultural background?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any weekly exercise groups or community activities for middle-aged Muslim men in Maputo that I could join to improve my health while socializing?\\",\\n  \\"What exercise guidelines should a subsistence farmer with easy access to healthy foods follow to lower blood sugar levels, especially if he exercises only 1–2 days a week?\\",\\n  \\"How does the climate and environment in suburban Maputo affect outdoor exercise options for people with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Are there culturally appropriate diabetes education resources or support groups in the Rhonga community around Maputo?\\",\\n  \\"What traditional forms of physical activity practiced by the Rhonga culture near Maputo are beneficial for managing type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"Is there guidance from the local healthcare clinic in Maputo on combining insulin injections and oral medication with increased physical activity?\\",\\n  \\"How can someone with limited social support build motivation to exercise more regularly in suburban Maputo?\\",\\n  \\"What are some healthy, Kosher recipes using foods commonly found near Maputo that are good for subsistence farmers with type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What are the prayer and fasting considerations for a Muslim adult with type 2 diabetes in Mozambique when planning an exercise routine?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
bce083fd-1819-4e49-bc73-c17daf4e196c	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b815-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Em qual província você vive? (selecione 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Maputo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Qual é a sua religião?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Christianity (Roman Catholic)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Nome</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Daliso Matola</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gênero (selecione 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Male</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Idade (selecione 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">25–34</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Como você descreveria sua comunidade ou área local? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Urban (city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Como você descreveria o acesso a alimentos em sua comunidade ou área local? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem alguma deficiência? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Qual é a sua ocupação atual?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Subsistence farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">O que melhor descreve sua rotina diária atualmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais hobbies ou interesses você pratica regularmente? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Farming &amp; gardening (often more than a hobby, but also a leisure activity)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais atividades ou rotinas são mais importantes para você?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você possui atualmente outras condições de saúde além do diabetes? (selecione todas as que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente tomando medicamentos ou seguindo algum tratamento para diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Que tipo de recursos de saúde você acessa ou utiliza regularmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem acesso regular a serviços de saúde?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Com que frequência você acessa serviços de saúde? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Cultura (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Xichangana</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente vivendo com Diabetes Tipo 2?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você fuma produtos de tabaco?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você consome bebidas alcoólicas?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quantos dias por semana você pratica atividade física de intensidade moderada a vigorosa? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Selecione quaisquer preferências ou restrições alimentares que você possa ter (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Gluten-Free</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quem faz parte da sua rede regular de apoio? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Número do Estudo</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">bce083fd-1819-4e49-bc73-c17daf4e196c</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais são seus principais objetivos pessoais de saúde? (você pode selecionar mais de um)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Eu acordo cedo, faço meu chá de manhã e como meu pão sem glúten. Depois, trato logo de ir regar a horta, como faço quase todos os dias. O trabalho é leve hoje: só preciso juntar as folhas secas, mas já no meio da tarefa comecei a sentir cansaço nas pernas. Pensei, será que isso é normal ou só estou cansado porque fiquei ontem quase o dia todo sentado? Sempre imaginei que, por mexer com terra e planta, já fazia exercício suficiente. Mas hoje não consegui terminar de varrer o quintal. Fiquei pensando, será só por causa do meu açúcar no sangue?\n\nNo dia seguinte, fui ao centro de saúde do bairro buscar meu remédio. A enfermeira, Dona Lúcia, perguntou se eu estava me sentindo bem. Eu hesitei, mas contei do meu cansaço. Ela riu e disse: 'Daliso, cuidar da horta é ótimo, mas nosso corpo precisa de movimento diferente também! Sabe varrer a casa? Subir e descer degraus? Até carregar dois baldes de água ajuda.' Achei estranho—precisa mesmo fazer mais essas coisas? Mas ela explicou que, mudando um pouco minha rotina e usando o que tenho em casa, posso melhorar minha energia e controlar a diabetes melhor.\n\nDe volta a casa, tentei fazer como Dona Lúcia falou. Peguei as garrafas de água e subi uns degraus, mas logo fiquei ofegante. Senti vontade de parar, pois não parecia fácil como mexer com enxada. Quando quase desisti, lembrei que o fim de semana chegava, e ia precisar carregar muitos cestos de mandioca com meu irmão. Isso me deu uma força, porque não queria ficar para trás nessa tarefa maior.\n\nCom o tempo, faço um pouco mais desses exercícios em casa. Nas primeiras vezes, a família riu de mim subindo e descendo do degrau, mas depois até minha mãe quis tentar. Assim, no sábado, quando chegou a hora de carregar mandioca, senti menos cansaço. Agora, penso diferente: toda pequena atividade ajuda um pouco. Fico motivado para manter minha saúde, porque quero sempre estar pronto para o trabalho e os deveres lá fora.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bce083fd-1819-4e49-bc73-c17daf4e196c_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bce083fd-1819-4e49-bc73-c17daf4e196c_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bce083fd-1819-4e49-bc73-c17daf4e196c_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bce083fd-1819-4e49-bc73-c17daf4e196c_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bce083fd-1819-4e49-bc73-c17daf4e196c_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bce083fd-1819-4e49-bc73-c17daf4e196c_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bce083fd-1819-4e49-bc73-c17daf4e196c_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bce083fd-1819-4e49-bc73-c17daf4e196c_3.mp3}	Não tenho ginásio — o que posso fazer em casa ou com objetos do dia a dia para me manter ativo?	diet	male	overlapped	2026-03-23 14:15:22.134742+00	{"label": "GOOD", "model": "gpt-4.1", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Célio Mavundza is a 18–24 year old, \\nCulture: Rhonga male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Subsistence farmer, lives in a Suburban (near city or town) in Maputo. Disability: he has none. Religion: Christianity (Zion Christian Church). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling. Activities: Exercise or physical activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Only when necessary. Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: None. Diet restrictions: Kosher. Smoking: Yes. Alcohol drinking: Yes. Physical activity: 3–4 days. Support network: Close friends. Health goals: Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?. his food access Easy access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Célio Mavundza and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in Portuguese that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken Portuguese, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in Portuguese.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in Portuguese.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "pt", "story_arc": "iteration", "audio_prompts": ["Daliso Matola is alone in his backyard in Maputo. You hear soft footsteps on dry leaves, Daliso breathing slightly heavier than normal. As he sweeps, he mutters to himself in a low, puzzled voice, ‘Aish, will I even finish this today?’ There’s the distant hum of city traffic and a rooster crowing far off.", "A middle-aged female nurse named Dona Lúcia sits across from Daliso Matola in a small, echoey clinic room. Dona Lúcia’s voice is warm and clear, slightly raised for encouragement: ‘Daliso, até balde serve de peso, sabias?’ Daliso hesitates, then softly chuckles and asks a question. The faint beeping of clinic devices and quiet footsteps pass in the corridor nearby.", "Daliso Matola is outside his kitchen, climbing steps. You hear his labored breathing and the slosh of water inside plastic bottles as he climbs, occasionally pausing with a soft grunt. A playful child giggles in the background, and Daliso encourages himself quietly with a tired, determined whisper: ‘Só mais uma vez, Daliso.’ Soft city noises linger in the background.", "Daliso Matola laughs with his mother nearby in their Maputo backyard. You hear upbeat laughter, rustling leaves, and Daliso’s relaxed, confident voice celebrating their hard work: ‘Viu mãe, foi fácil desta vez!’ The basket thumps gently on the ground, chickens cluck in the distance, and a light breeze stirs leaves, all captured closely and naturally."], "image_prompts": ["Daliso Matola stands in his modest Maputo backyard, one hand holding a broom, midway through sweeping up dry leaves as sunlight filters through the lush green of his small urban garden. His body is slightly hunched from exertion and his face betrays mild fatigue and surprise, looking down at his legs. Texture emphasis on his work-worn hands, dusty ground, and morning light reflecting off tin-roofed houses in the background.", "A medium shot showing Daliso Matola seated on a wooden bench inside a Maputo local clinic, with a smiling, middle-aged female nurse (Dona Lúcia) in a simple white uniform speaking kindly to him. Daliso listens with arms folded, head tilted in uncertainty, faint sunlight coming through old windows, posters about diabetes and exercise on faded walls.", "Daliso Matola at home, gripping two large plastic water bottles, carefully climbing up and down concrete steps outside his kitchen. His posture is slightly unsteady, with shoulders tensed and mouth parted as he breathes heavily, a neighbor’s child watching from a short distance with amusement. Emphasis on worn clothes, cracked steps, late afternoon shadows.", "A wide shot in the backyard: Daliso Matola standing upright and smiling, holding a heavy basket of cassava on his hip, his mother (older woman, Xichangana features) beside him, both laughing. The garden is tidier now, clothes flutter in the breeze, and a sense of accomplishment shows in Daliso’s relaxed stance and cheerful eyes in the bright midday light."], "language_code": "pt-PT", "avg_time_taken": 1.8214844286441803, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_q