 what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in Portuguese that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken Portuguese, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in Portuguese.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in Portuguese.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "pt", "story_arc": "social_support", "audio_prompts": ["Nhlanhla Matola's voice, sounding concerned and uncertain, talking about his diabetes diagnosis, with a gentle background noise of a city street.", "A health worker's voice, calm and reassuring, explaining diabetes management to Nhlanhla Matola, with a soft background noise of a clinic.", "Nhlanhla Matola's voice, sounding determined and motivated, talking about his efforts to change his habits, with a background noise of a park with people playing sports.", "Nhlanhla Matola's voice, sounding happy and confident, talking about his progress and improved health, with a gentle background noise of a kitchen with cooking sounds."], "image_prompts": ["Nhlanhla Matola, a young man in his early 20s, sitting on a couch, looking concerned and holding a bag of traditional snacks, with a cityscape in the background, medium shot.", "A health worker, a middle-aged woman with a kind smile, talking to Nhlanhla Matola in a clinic, with a whiteboard with diabetes information in the background, wide shot.", "Nhlanhla Matola, wearing a sports jersey, running in a park, with a few people playing soccer in the background, medium shot.", "Nhlanhla Matola, sitting at a table, looking at a cookbook, with a kitchen counter with healthy food ingredients in the background, medium shot."], "language_code": "pt-PT", "avg_time_taken": 5.3813682416590245, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are affordable meal plans for young adults with type 2 diabetes living in urban Maputo with easy access to healthy foods?\\",\\n  \\"Can I still eat Xichangana traditional dishes like xigugu and xicutsi while managing type 2 diabetes on a subsistence farmer's income?\\",\\n  \\"Which local Maputo markets offer the best prices on fresh produce and healthy staples suitable for diabetics?\\",\\n  \\"Are there urban farming or community gardening initiatives in Maputo that support young men with diabetes seeking low-cost healthy foods?\\",\\n  \\"How do other Zion Christian Church members in Mozambique approach balancing cultural dietary traditions with diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"What are examples of physical activities commonly done by young men in Maputo city that match my routine of exercising 3–4 days a week?\\",\\n  \\"Are traditional games like Ntxuva and damas considered good for mental or physical health management for type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What resources exist for support groups or diabetes education in Xichangana communities in Maputo province?\\",\\n  \\"How harmful is weekly alcohol and tobacco use for young adult men with type 2 diabetes in urban Mozambique?\\",\\n  \\"What local recipes in Xichangana cuisine are both affordable and suitable for people with type 2 diabetes who do not have dietary restrictions?\\",\\n  \\"Is it possible to manage type 2 diabetes in an urban Mozambican setting using a mix of oral medication, insulin, and herbal medicines safely?\\",\\n  \\"How can I involve my family in Maputo in supporting my diabetes care, especially during traditional community gatherings and church events?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restricti