ss="p-2 font-bold">Como você descreveria o acesso a alimentos em sua comunidade ou área local? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem alguma deficiência? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Qual é a sua ocupação atual?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Subsistence farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">O que melhor descreve sua rotina diária atualmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais hobbies ou interesses você pratica regularmente? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Storytelling</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais atividades ou rotinas são mais importantes para você?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você possui atualmente outras condições de saúde além do diabetes? (selecione todas as que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente tomando medicamentos ou seguindo algum tratamento para diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Que tipo de recursos de saúde você acessa ou utiliza regularmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem acesso regular a serviços de saúde?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Com que frequência você acessa serviços de saúde? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Only when necessary</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Cultura (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Rhonga</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente vivendo com Diabetes Tipo 2?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você fuma produtos de tabaco?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você consome bebidas alcoólicas?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quantos dias por semana você pratica atividade física de intensidade moderada a vigorosa? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Selecione quaisquer preferências ou restrições alimentares que você possa ter (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quem faz parte da sua rede regular de apoio? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Número do Estudo</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">51adf2dd-13b3-49f7-972c-96d2f3031069</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais são seus principais objetivos pessoais de saúde? (você pode selecionar mais de um)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">What kinds of exercises are safe and helpful for someone with diabetes?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Sabia que a minha vida de agricultora é cansativa, mas será que isso conta como exercício suficiente para controlar o meu diabetes? Eu sempre pensei que cuidar da terra já era meu jeito de me mexer e estar ativa. Mas quando veio a vez de preparar um banquete para a família, percebi que o cansaço me derrubava antes mesmo de começar. Será que eu estava errando algo? Eu comia muito piri-piri e legumes frescos da horta, mas sentia que meu corpo não ajudava no que eu precisava. No fim, quase desisti da tarefa, achando que aquele era o meu limite.\n\nNo posto de saúde, a enfermeira me explicou com calma que o trabalho na agricultura não substitui a necessidade de movimentos diferentes e específicos para ajudar a controlar o diabetes. Ela mostrou exercícios simples que eu posso fazer dentro de casa, até usando um balde d’água ou um saco de milho como pesos. 'E se você fizer só uns minutos por dia, Inhaca, isso já vai ajudar', ela disse com um sorriso. No início, confessei que fiquei com dúvidas, será que funcionaria mesmo? Mas o jeito claro e simples dela me deu coragem pra tentar.\n\nA primeira semana foi dura, admito. No meio da arrumação da casa e das tarefas da roça, esquecia dos exercícios, ou me sentia cansada demais para fazer todos. Até escorreguei e comi um pouco do que não devia, achando que não faria mal. Mas lembrei daquele grande encontro comunitário que eu prometi ajudar a organizar. Se eu quisesse estar ali de pé com força, tinha que continuar. Respirei fundo, alinhei meu foco, e segui tentando, mesmo com tropeços no caminho.\n\nAgora, com o passar dos dias, sinto que meu corpo responde a esses esforços simples. Aquele encontro passou, e eu estava firme, mesmo no sol da tarde, contando histórias e ajudando naquilo que sei. Me sinto mais disposta, e até meus filhos notaram que estou diferente. Sei que é só o começo, e quero continuar melhorando devagarinho. Afinal, quem disse que sem academia não dá para cuidar da saúde? Só precisamos achar o nosso jeito aqui em casa mesmo.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/51adf2dd-13b3-49f7-972c-96d2f3031069_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/51adf2dd-13b3-49f7-972c-96d2f3031069_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/51adf2dd-13b3-49f7-972c-96d2f3031069_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/51adf2dd-13b3-49f7-972c-96d2f3031069_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/51adf2dd-13b3-49f7-972c-96d2f3031069_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/51adf2dd-13b3-49f7-972c-96d2f3031069_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/51adf2dd-13b3-49f7-972c-96d2f3031069_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/51adf2dd-13b3-49f7-972c-96d2f3031069_3.mp3}	Não tenho ginásio — o que posso fazer em casa ou com objetos do dia a dia para me manter ativo?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 14:15:24.672129+00	{"label": "GOOD", "model": "gpt-4.1-mini", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Candido Nhantumbo is a 65+ year old, \\nCulture: Rhonga male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Subsistence farmer, lives in a Rural (small community or countryside) in Maputo. Disability: he has none. Religion: Christianity (Presbyterian). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling. Activities: Socialising with family or friends. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Occasionally (less than once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: Hypertension (high blood pressure). Diet restrictions: Halal. Smoking: No. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 3–4 days. Support network: I live alone or have limited support. Health goals: I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?. his food access Limited access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Candido Nhantumbo and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in Portuguese that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken Portuguese, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in Portuguese.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in Portuguese.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "pt", "story_arc": "iteration", "audio_prompts": ["Sounds of Inhaca Langa breathing heavily with tiredness, soft rustling of leaves and distant birds in a suburban garden, her voice slow and reflective as she talks about her daily struggles, moderate volume, natural outdoor ambiance, Inhaca's voice near mic.", "Inhaca's voice curious but hesitant, mixed with a gentle, clear female nurse explaining simple exercises nearby in a quiet clinic room, soft shuffling of paper and mild echo of tiled walls, light background murmurs of other patients distant, moderate volume, conversation across a small table.", "Inhaca breathing with mild exertion, a faint sigh of frustration, ambient sounds of household activity such as dishes clinking and distant street noises, her voice moderate and steady expressing determination despite setbacks, moderate volume, near mic with background sounds slightly muffled.", "Inhaca's joyful, confident voice telling a story outdoors, laughter and light chatter from family and friends in the background, sounds of natural afternoon breeze and a distant dog barking, moderate volume, wide acoustic space capturing social environment, Inhaca's voice central and clear."], "image_prompts": ["Inhaca Langa standing tired next to a small vegetable garden in a suburban Maputo backyard, sunlight casting warm natural light on her face, her posture shows weariness confronting pile of fresh vegetables, rustic wooden fence and simple house in background, medium shot.", "Inhaca Langa sitting with a friendly female health worker inside a small, bright local clinic room in Maputo, health worker showing gestures demonstrating light exercise with household items like buckets, soft daylight through window highlights their natural expressions, medium shot.", "Inhaca Langa struggling to do simple exercises holding a heavy maize sack in her small living room, slightly frustrated but determined expression, modest furniture and items around reveal her suburban home life, morning soft light filtering through curtains, medium shot.", "Inhaca Langa smiling confidently while telling a story at a community gathering outside in the afternoon, surrounded by attentive family members and friends, vibrant fabrics and natural sunlight highlight the warm atmosphere, wide shot including community setting."], "language_code": "pt-PT", "avg_time_taken": 3.6766370713710783, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What traditional Rhonga foods available in suburban Maputo are suitable for a lactose-free diabetes-friendly diet?\\",\\n  \\"How can a female subsistence farmer in her late 30s living near Maputo manage type 2 diabetes with minimal physical activity?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community support groups or non-religious spiritual gatherings in Maputo province that help with diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"What local Maputo resources can help someone quit daily tobacco smoking while managing diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How do other women subsistence farmers in Mozambique balance socialising with family and friends and staying on track with diabetes lifestyle changes?\\",\\n  \\"What types of physical activities are accessible and culturally appropriate for Rhonga women with type 2 diabetes who live in suburban areas with easy access to healthy foods?\\",\\n  \\"Are there any lactose-free, traditional herbal remedies in Mozambique that are safe for type 2 diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"How can someone integrating oral medication, insulin, and traditional medicine optimize their diabetes care using local healthcare clinics in Maputo?\\",\\n  \\"What are the risks of weekly alcohol consumption for a female with type 2 diabetes in Mozambique, particularly among non-religious spiritualists?\\",\\n  \\"Are there safe exercise routines that can be done at home for people with diabetes who do not exercise regularly and have no disabilities?\\",\\n  \\"How does the Rhonga community in suburban Maputo practice non-religious spirituality for well-being alongside medical treatment for diabetes?\\",\\n  \\"What are some storytelling activities or themes used in Mozambique to promote diabetes awareness and healthy living in suburban communities?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Campos relevantes: rotina diária de Inhaca Langa como agricultora de subsistência, o fato de viver em uma área suburbana perto da cidade de Maputo, o uso de Insulina para o diabetes tipo 2, o acesso esporádico ao serviço de saúde local, o hábito de fumar, a dieta koscher e a falta de atividade física, além do interesse em socializar e contar histórias, e a busca por exercícios seguros para sua condição sem precisar ir à academia.", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity"