<td class="p-2 font-bold">Como você descreveria o acesso a alimentos em sua comunidade ou área local? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Limited access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem alguma deficiência? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Qual é a sua ocupação atual?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Subsistence farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">O que melhor descreve sua rotina diária atualmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais hobbies ou interesses você pratica regularmente? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Traditional ceremonies &amp; rituals</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais atividades ou rotinas são mais importantes para você?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Spiritual or religious activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você possui atualmente outras condições de saúde além do diabetes? (selecione todas as que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente tomando medicamentos ou seguindo algum tratamento para diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Que tipo de recursos de saúde você acessa ou utiliza regularmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem acesso regular a serviços de saúde?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Com que frequência você acessa serviços de saúde? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Cultura (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Rhonga</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente vivendo com Diabetes Tipo 2?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você fuma produtos de tabaco?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você consome bebidas alcoólicas?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quantos dias por semana você pratica atividade física de intensidade moderada a vigorosa? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5–7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Selecione quaisquer preferências ou restrições alimentares que você possa ter (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quem faz parte da sua rede regular de apoio? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Número do Estudo</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">fb280de7-6899-4d24-9daa-afb43a4751d9</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais são seus principais objetivos pessoais de saúde? (você pode selecionar mais de um)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Acordo cedo todo dia para cuidar da minha pequena roça aqui na comunidade do Maputo, sabe? A vida é dura, mas é o que nós temos. Como sou vegano, meu prato é simples: mandioca, feijão, umas folhas de couve e às vezes um pouco de batata-doce. A gente não pensa muito em como isso afeta a saúde, né? Fico o dia todo plantando e colhendo, mas outro dia tentava correr um pouco na roça para me exercitar, achando que ia melhorar o diabetes rápido. Só que acabei cansado demais, e no final não consegui colher nem perto do que precisava. Fiquei me perguntando, será que estão certos esses exercícios que falam por aí? Parece que meu corpo não aguenta, e o trabalho só fica atrasado.\n\nFoi quando eu fui à clínica rural perto do vilarejo e conversei com a enfermeira. Ela me explicou, com calma, que o trabalho na roça já é uma atividade física, mas que eu precisava fazer caminhadas aceleradas, uns dois a três dias na semana, e também fortalecer meu corpo com alguns agachamentos usando ferramentas de fazenda. Falou que não precisa ser correndo igual no mundo grande, mas sim constante, tipo meia hora, cinco vezes por semana. Disse ainda para eu Fazer alongamentos simples todo dia para o corpo não ficar preso. No começo eu fiquei meio desconfiado, pensando se ia dar conta. Mas ela falou que com calma, eu ia ver que ajuda muito a controlar o açúcar no sangue e melhorar minha disposição para trabalhar mais forte e melhor.\n\nVoltei pra casa com a ideia na cabeça, decidido a tentar. Comecei a fazer uma caminhada rápida pela estrada perto da comunidade, mas no segundo dia senti o corpo meio travado, cansado, e quase desisti. Também tentei fazer os agachamentos com o saco de milho, e foi difícil no começo. Pensei até que isso podia atrapalhar o meu trabalho. Mas lembrei do conselho da enfermeira e que eu teria que estar preparado para uma grande colheita próxima. Então continuei, tentando ajustar aos poucos, mesmo quando o corpo reclamava. Foi um desafio adaptar a rotina, mas o pensamento naquele trabalho maior me dava ânimo para persistir e não desistir.\n\nPassaram-se algumas semanas e comecei a sentir o corpo mais forte e a mente mais clara. As caminhadas foram ficando mais fáceis, e eu conseguia fazer os agachamentos com menos esforço. No último dia da colheita, percebi que estava mais confiante e com energia para terminar tudo sem me esgotar. Foi uma grande vitória para mim, porque entendi que cuidar do corpo ajuda mesmo no trabalho de todo dia. Agora quero continuar assim, encontrando jeitos simples de me movimentar e cuidar melhor da minha saúde, pra viver mais tempo e com força suficiente para tudo aquilo que eu precisar fazer na roça e na vida.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fb280de7-6899-4d24-9daa-afb43a4751d9_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fb280de7-6899-4d24-9daa-afb43a4751d9_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fb280de7-6899-4d24-9daa-afb43a4751d9_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fb280de7-6899-4d24-9daa-afb43a4751d9_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fb280de7-6899-4d24-9daa-afb43a4751d9_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fb280de7-6899-4d24-9daa-afb43a4751d9_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fb280de7-6899-4d24-9daa-afb43a4751d9_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fb280de7-6899-4d24-9daa-afb43a4751d9_3.mp3}	Que tipos de exercícios são seguros e benéficos para alguém com diabetes?	exercise	male	consistency	2026-03-23 14:15:25.260525+00	{"label": "EXCELLENT", "model": "gpt-4.1-mini", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Candido Nhantumbo is a 65+ year old, \\nCulture: Rhonga male. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. he is a Subsistence farmer, lives in a Rural (small community or countryside) in Maputo. Disability: he has none. Religion: Christianity (Presbyterian). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Storytelling. Activities: Socialising with family or friends. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Occasionally (less than once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: Hypertension (high blood pressure). Diet restrictions: Halal. Smoking: No. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 3–4 days. Support network: I live alone or have limited support. Health goals: I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?. his food access Limited access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Candido Nhantumbo and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in Portuguese that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken Portuguese, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in Portuguese.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in Portuguese.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "pt", "story_arc": "social_support", "audio_prompts": ["Sounds of early morning in a rural Mozambique farm near Maputo: faint bird calls, rustling leaves, and distant animal noises. Celso Matavele's moderate-pitch, slightly gravelly voice narrates with a slow, thoughtful pacing about daily farming work and tiredness. Occasional soft sighs as if reflecting on the day's challenges. Ambient wind and footsteps on dry earth are audible.", "Outdoor setting near a rural health clinic with ambient village sounds like talking in the distance and children playing softly. Celso Matavele's voice, moderate volume with clear articulation, hesitantly asks questions. The female nurse speaks calmly with warm, inviting tone from a nearby position, explaining exercise gently. Voices overlap occasionally with natural pauses and subtle background breeze.", "Celso Matavele's steady breathing and footsteps on dusty gravel during a brisk walk along a village road. His voice sounds determined but tired, slightly lowering after a small laugh, describing his struggle and persistence. Background noises include distant calls, faint traffic sounds, and wind rustling through sparse trees, creating an immersive rural atmosphere.", "Bright daytime farm sounds: buzzing bees, birds sing, and Celso Matavele's confident voice sharing progress and hope, moderately paced with warm and inviting tone. Occasional rustle of leaves and the shifting weight of a sack on his shoulder heard. Nearby, soft chatter from two farming neighbors (one Rhonga male), blending naturally into the environment. Medium volume levels with clear spatial separation."], "image_prompts": ["Celso Matavele, a young Rhonga male farmer, standing tired with hands on hips in a small rural farm field near Maputo, under bright morning sunlight. He is dressed in worn, simple farming clothes with dirt-stained hands, looking contemplative and weary. The background shows dry earth, sparse crops, and traditional rural housing. Medium shot capturing textures of his skin, rough fabric of clothes, and dusty ground.", "Celso Matavele seated outside a small rural health clinic in Maputo province, speaking with a female nurse wearing a white uniform and headscarf. Celso looks slightly hesitant but attentive, leaning forward with hands resting on knees, while the nurse gestures gently, explaining something. The setting is a shaded clinic yard with local plants and simple benches. Medium shot with natural lighting highlighting their expressions and surroundings.", "Celso Matavele walking briskly along a dusty village road near his farm, arms swinging with effort, wearing a simple t-shirt and shorts. His face shows mild fatigue but determination, with slight sweat visible. The rural landscape includes scattered huts, trees, and distant farmland under soft afternoon light. Medium shot captures movement and surrounding environment with detailed textures of the dusty path and foliage.", "Celso Matavele working confidently in his farm field during harvest, bending slightly while carrying a sack of harvested crops on one shoulder. He smiles gently, showing pride and strength. The background shows lush green plants, a bright blue sky, and neighboring traditional homesteads. Medium shot emphasizing his posture, the texture of the sack, and natural sunlight highlighting the vibrant scene."], "language_code": "pt-PT", "avg_time_taken": 3.6766370713710783, "task_parent_id": "13ac5e7b-f862-4a75-a32e-454d4ba4eeaf", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are the most effective exercise routines for a 20-year-old male subsistence farmer with type 2 diabetes living in rural Maputo province, Mozambique?\\",\\n  \\"How do traditional Rhonga ceremonies and Anglican Christian practices in rural Maputo influence healthy eating and diabetes management?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find lactose-free or diabetes-friendly foods in small rural communities in X - Maputo province?\\",\\n  \\"Are there local support groups or diabetes education programs near Maputo for young men living alone with limited support?\\",\\n  \\"What are common challenges faced by subsistence farmers with type 2 diabetes in rural Mozambique when accessing diabetes care and medication?\\",\\n  \\"How do spiritual activities or participation in traditional ceremonies affect blood sugar control for Rhonga Christians in Mozambique?\\",\\n  \\"Are there culturally accepted herbal or traditional treatments for type 2 diabetes in rural Rhonga communities?\\",\\n  \\"What affordable, healthy local foods can I grow or access in the countryside of Maputo that fit a lactose-free, diabetes-friendly diet?\\",\\n  \\"How can I balance daily physical labor on my farm with additional exercise to manage diabetes more effectively?\\",\\n  \\"What advice do healthcare clinics in rural Maputo give to young male diabetes patients regarding alcohol and rare consumption?\\",\\n  \\"Are there mobile health services or outreach programs in rural Maputo province that help with regular diabetes monitoring?\\",\\n  \\"How can I improve my emotional well-being and diabetes self-management when living alone in a small community far from family?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "Campos relacionados à rotina de Celso Matavele que são relevantes para a história incluem: ele é um homem jovem, entre 18 e 24 anos, faz agricultura de subsistência em uma comunidade rural pequena. Ele vive sozinho ou com pouco apoio, tem diabetes tipo 2 e tem acesso regular a cuidados de saúde mínimos, fazendo suas consultas ao menos uma vez por ano. Celso tem uma dieta vegana, mas acesso limitado a alimentos saudáveis, e sua rotina diária envolve trabalho físico intenso na agricultura e atividades religiosas. Ele toma insulina e medicamentos orais, mas busca entender qual tipo de exercício é seguro e útil para melhorar sua saúde e controlar o diabetes. A lacuna no conhecimento sobre exercícios apropriados e a dificuldade de balancear o trabalho agrícola com atividades físicas extras são essenciais.", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "t2d_status", "tobacco", "alcohol", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "health_goals", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
