2a147ef2-2e41-4aad-8bd3-3ef1343bf84a	e321ff7d-3b01-4a85-b815-000000006000			<div>\n    <div class="mt-6">\n\n        <div class="overflow-x-auto border rounded-lg">\n            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">\n                <thead class="bg-slate-50 font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase">\n                    <tr>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Column</th>\n                        <th class="p-2 border-b">Value</th>\n                    </tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">\n                    \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">None</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">40</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Em qual província você vive? (selecione 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Maputo</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Qual é a sua religião?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Christianity (Zion Christian Church)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Nome</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Helena Chauke</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Gênero (selecione 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Female</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Idade (selecione 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">35–44</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Como você descreveria sua comunidade ou área local? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Suburban (near city or town)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Como você descreveria o acesso a alimentos em sua comunidade ou área local? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Easy access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem alguma deficiência? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Qual é a sua ocupação atual?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Cassava farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">O que melhor descreve sua rotina diária atualmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais hobbies ou interesses você pratica regularmente? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Traditional dancing</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais atividades ou rotinas são mais importantes para você?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você possui atualmente outras condições de saúde além do diabetes? (selecione todas as que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente tomando medicamentos ou seguindo algum tratamento para diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Que tipo de recursos de saúde você acessa ou utiliza regularmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem acesso regular a serviços de saúde?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Com que frequência você acessa serviços de saúde? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Cultura (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Xichangana</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente vivendo com Diabetes Tipo 2?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você fuma produtos de tabaco?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você consome bebidas alcoólicas?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quantos dias por semana você pratica atividade física de intensidade moderada a vigorosa? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">5–7 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Selecione quaisquer preferências ou restrições alimentares que você possa ter (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quem faz parte da sua rede regular de apoio? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Número do Estudo</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">2a147ef2-2e41-4aad-8bd3-3ef1343bf84a</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais são seus principais objetivos pessoais de saúde? (você pode selecionar mais de um)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	O sol já estava alto quando eu acordei. A casa era simples, sabe? Uma casinha de alvenaria perto da cidade, mas com um pequeno quintal cheio de bananeiras. Eu preciso cuidar das minhas plantações de mandioca, é o meu trabalho. Mas, confesso, às vezes me sinto cansada, sabe? Não como muito bem, só um pouco de arroz e feijão, e um pouco de mandioca crua. A minha saúde não é a melhor, às vezes me sinto fraca, e não sei bem o que fazer para ficar mais forte. Será que comer mais frutas ajudaria?\n\nHoje o chefe me pediu para colher uma grande quantidade de mandioca para o mercado. Eu sabia que tinha que fazer bem, porque se eu não cumprisse o prazo, ia ter problemas. Mas eu estava tão cansada, e com fome, que não consegui me concentrar. Acabei colhendo menos do que o esperado, e o chefe ficou muito bravo. Ele disse que eu precisava estar mais atenta, e que minha saúde era importante para o trabalho. Será que ele tem razão?\n\nA enfermeira da clínica me explicou que preciso me exercitar um pouco todos os dias, e comer coisas saudáveis. Ela disse que, se eu me esforçasse um pouco, eu ia me sentir melhor, e teria mais energia para o trabalho. Ela me deu algumas dicas simples, como caminhar um pouco pela manhã, e comer mais frutas e verduras. Mas é difícil, sabe? Eu estou acostumada a trabalhar muito, e não tenho tempo para fazer exercícios. Será que eu consigo mudar?\n\nComecei a caminhar um pouco todos os dias, e a comer mais frutas. No começo foi difícil, mas aos poucos eu comecei a me sentir melhor. A minha energia aumentou, e eu me senti mais forte. Quando chegou a hora de colher a mandioca para o mercado, eu consegui fazer tudo com mais facilidade e confiança. O chefe ficou muito satisfeito, e me elogiou pelo meu trabalho. Eu me senti muito feliz e orgulhosa de mim mesma. Agora eu sei que cuidar da minha saúde é importante, e que eu posso fazer a diferença na minha vida.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2a147ef2-2e41-4aad-8bd3-3ef1343bf84a_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2a147ef2-2e41-4aad-8bd3-3ef1343bf84a_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2a147ef2-2e41-4aad-8bd3-3ef1343bf84a_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2a147ef2-2e41-4aad-8bd3-3ef1343bf84a_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2a147ef2-2e41-4aad-8bd3-3ef1343bf84a_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2a147ef2-2e41-4aad-8bd3-3ef1343bf84a_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2a147ef2-2e41-4aad-8bd3-3ef1343bf84a_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2a147ef2-2e41-4aad-8bd3-3ef1343bf84a_3.mp3}	Com que frequência e por quanto tempo devo fazer exercício para realmente melhorar a minha saúde?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-03-23 14:15:29.034937+00	{"label": "BAD", "model": "gemma-3-4b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: \\nCulture: None female. she is a Cassava farmer, lives in a Suburban (near city or town) in None. Disability: she has none. Religion: None. Daily routine: Working adult. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Diet restrictions: Kosher. Physical activity: 5–7 days. Support network: Healthcare provider or counsellor. Tone of the output: classic_change.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Helena Chauke and understanding the persona's needs (\\"How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?\\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in Portuguese that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?. \\n Use spoken Portuguese, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a classic_change tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in Portuguese.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in Portuguese.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "pt", "story_arc": "classic_change", "audio_prompts": ["Sound of a rooster crowing, followed by the quiet murmur of a woman's voice – Helena Chauke, a woman in her late 40s, speaking in a slightly hesitant, rural South African accent. 'O sol já está alto...' (The sun is already high...) Background sounds include birds chirping and the distant sound of farm machinery.", "Sound of a frustrated sigh, followed by the gruff voice of a man – the boss, a middle-aged man. 'Helena, você precisa prestar mais atenção!' (Helena, you need to pay more attention!). Helena Chauke's voice, slightly strained, replies with a mumbled, 'Eu sei, senhor' (I know, sir).  Subtle sounds of shuffling feet and the rustling of leaves.", "The gentle, reassuring voice of a nurse – a young woman, explaining something in clear, simple Portuguese. 'É importante se exercitar um pouco todos os dias...' (It's important to exercise a little every day...). Helena Chauke’s voice, hesitant and questioning, asks, 'Mas como, enfermeira?' (But how?). Background sounds include the quiet hum of a medical device and the soft clinking of instruments.", "Sound of Helena Chauke's footsteps on a dirt path, accompanied by a gentle, rhythmic breathing. She’s speaking to herself, a sense of quiet determination in her voice. 'Um pouco a cada dia...' (A little each day...).  The sound of birds chirping and the distant murmur of a village increases in volume, signifying progress and a sense of accomplishment."], "image_prompts": ["Helena Chauke, a woman in her late 40s, standing in a small, simple kitchen in a rural South African home. She is wearing a patterned headscarf and a modest dress. She is holding a bowl of slightly bruised bananas, looking thoughtfully at them. Sunlight streams in through a small window, illuminating dust motes in the air. The kitchen is sparsely furnished with a wooden table and a few basic appliances.", "Helena Chauke, a woman in her late 40s, kneeling in a muddy field, surrounded by rows of young cassava plants. She is wearing worn overalls and a sun hat. She is struggling to lift a heavy sack of harvested cassava, her face etched with effort and a slight grimace. The field is vast and stretches out towards the horizon, with a few distant huts visible.", "Helena Chauke, a woman in her late 40s, sitting in a brightly lit clinic room. She is speaking to a friendly-looking nurse, a younger woman with a clipboard. Helena is holding her hands together, a slightly hesitant expression on her face. The nurse is smiling reassuringly, pointing to a chart on the wall. The room is clean and modern, with pastel-colored walls.", "Helena Chauke, a woman in her late 40s, walking along a dirt road outside of her village. She is wearing comfortable sandals and a light dress. She is smiling confidently as she walks, a small backpack slung over her shoulder. The landscape is rural and lush, with rolling hills and a few scattered trees. A warm, golden light bathes the scene."], "language_code": "pt-PT", "avg_time_taken": 76.73263001441956, "task_parent_id": "", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are the best types of physical exercises for a 35–44-year-old woman with type 2 diabetes living in suburban Maputo and practicing traditional Xichangana dancing?\\",\\n  \\"How can a cassava farmer in Maputo province adapt a gluten-free diet using local foods available near urban areas?\\",\\n  \\"What specific guidelines exist for Zion Christian Church members in Mozambique regarding managing diabetes with both modern and traditional herbal medicines?\\",\\n  \\"Are there group exercise programs or community activities for women with type 2 diabetes in suburban neighborhoods close to Maputo?\\",\\n  \\"How does regular traditional dancing impact blood sugar levels for adults with type 2 diabetes in Mozambique?\\",\\n  \\"Where can I find a support group for women managing type 2 diabetes who speak Xichangana in the Maputo area?\\",\\n  \\"What are the most recommended local healthcare clinics in suburban Maputo for regular diabetes check-ups and insulin administration?\\",\\n  \\"How does easy access to healthy suburban foods in Maputo province influence recommended meal planning for gluten-free diabetic diets?\\",\\n  \\"Are there common challenges for cassava farmers in Mozambique following a gluten-free and diabetes-friendly diet?\\",\\n  \\"What exercises can be done safely five to seven days a week by working women over 35 who already do a lot of physical activity through farming?\\",\\n  \\"How can my daily farm work and traditional dancing be balanced to prevent low blood sugar episodes while on insulin and Metformin?\\",\\n  \\"Are there typical health risks or considerations for female Xichangana cassava farmers with type 2 diabetes who do not consume alcohol or tobacco?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": ["city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "describe_location", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "medication", "healthcare_frequency", "culture", "physical_activity", "diet_restrictions", "support_network", "Question", "generated_queries", "Category", "study_number", "output_format", "label", "story_arc", "type", "parent", "output_tone"]}
