        <td class="p-2 font-bold">Como você descreveria o acesso a alimentos em sua comunidade ou área local? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Limited access to healthy foods</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem alguma deficiência? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Qual é a sua ocupação atual?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Subsistence farmer</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">O que melhor descreve sua rotina diária atualmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais hobbies ou interesses você pratica regularmente? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Traditional ceremonies &amp; rituals</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais atividades ou rotinas são mais importantes para você?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Spiritual or religious activities</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você possui atualmente outras condições de saúde além do diabetes? (selecione todas as que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente tomando medicamentos ou seguindo algum tratamento para diabetes?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Que tipo de recursos de saúde você acessa ou utiliza regularmente?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você tem acesso regular a serviços de saúde?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Com que frequência você acessa serviços de saúde? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Cultura (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Rhonga</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você está atualmente vivendo com Diabetes Tipo 2?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você fuma produtos de tabaco?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Você consome bebidas alcoólicas?</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">No</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quantos dias por semana você pratica atividade física de intensidade moderada a vigorosa? (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">1–2 days</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Selecione quaisquer preferências ou restrições alimentares que você possa ter (escolha 1)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quem faz parte da sua rede regular de apoio? (selecione todos os que se aplicam)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Número do Estudo</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">317f872b-7288-41fd-997b-a1d95745c0e8</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                <tr>\n                    <td class="p-2 font-bold">Quais são seus principais objetivos pessoais de saúde? (você pode selecionar mais de um)</td>\n                    <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n                </tr>\n            \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	O sol já estava a nascer, pintando o céu de laranja e rosa, quando eu acordei. A minha casa, bem simples, era no meio do campo, perto de onde planto minhas bananas.  Eu adoro comer um pedaço de massa com mel antes de começar a trabalhar, sabe? É um prazer pequeno, mas faz-me sentir forte.  Mas às vezes, quando o trabalho está difícil, e o sol já está alto, eu como uma fruta doce, ou até um pedaço de bolo que a minha irmã faz.  Não penso muito no açúcar, sabe?  Só quero ter energia para trabalhar, e para ajudar a minha família.\n\nHoje, eu tinha que colher as bananas para o mercado. É um trabalho duro, carregar as cestas pesadas, mas preciso vender para comprar os remédios.  Eu estava tão concentrada em colher, em levar as bananas para o carro, que esqueci de comer alguma coisa.  Quando cheguei ao mercado, o meu carrinho estava quase vazio!  O vendedor, o António, olhou para mim com preocupação. ‘Felismina, você parece cansada,’ disse ele. ‘Precisa comer algo, para ter energia.’ Eu apenas sorri e disse que estava bem, mas, na verdade, eu estava um pouco fraca.  Eu não sabia que era importante comer a cada poucas horas, sabe?\n\nA enfermeira da clínica, a Maria, explicou-me que comer tarde à noite pode fazer o meu açúcar subir muito. Ela disse que preciso de comer um pouco sempre, mesmo que seja uma fruta ou um pedaço de pão. Ela me mostrou um gráfico, com desenhos de bananas e de melão, e disse que era importante comer coisas que não faziam o açúcar subir muito rápido.  Eu perguntei: ‘Mas e se eu estiver com muita fome à noite?’ Ela sorriu e disse: ‘Pode comer um pouco de fruta, Felismina. E beba água!’  Eu prometi que ia tentar, mas às vezes é difícil, sabe? É tão tentador comer algo doce quando estou cansada.\n\nNa semana passada, eu tinha que ajudar a preparar um bolo para a festa de casamento da minha prima. Era um trabalho grande, e eu precisava de estar forte para ajudar a minha mãe.  Eu me forcei a comer um pouco de fruta e a beber água durante todo o dia, e consegui ajudar a fazer o bolo sem me sentir muito cansada.  Agora, quando penso em comer algo doce à noite, lembro-me da enfermeira e do gráfico.  E lembro-me de que preciso de estar forte para ajudar a minha família e para fazer o meu trabalho.  Eu estou a tentar fazer escolhas melhores, e sinto-me mais feliz e com mais energia.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/317f872b-7288-41fd-997b-a1d95745c0e8_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/317f872b-7288-41fd-997b-a1d95745c0e8_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/317f872b-7288-41fd-997b-a1d95745c0e8_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/317f872b-7288-41fd-997b-a1d95745c0e8_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/317f872b-7288-41fd-997b-a1d95745c0e8_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/317f872b-7288-41fd-997b-a1d95745c0e8_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/317f872b-7288-41fd-997b-a1d95745c0e8_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/317f872b-7288-41fd-997b-a1d95745c0e8_3.mp3}	Às vezes como tarde da noite. Como isso afeta a minha glicemia e o que posso fazer em vez disso?	diet	female	consistency	2026-03-23 14:15:29.331942+00	{"label": "GOOD", "model": "gemma-3-4b-it", "prompt": "Our persona has the following profile: Felismina Nhantumbo is a 35–44 year old, \\nCulture: Rhonga female. \\nType 2 Diabetes status: Yes. she is a Subsistence farmer, lives in a Rural (small community or countryside) in Maputo. Disability: she has none. Religion: Christianity (Methodist). Daily routine: Working adult. Hobbies: Traditional ceremonies & rituals. Activities: Spiritual or religious activities. Currently taking Medication?: Insulin injections, B — Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), C — Lifestyle changes only (no medication), D — Herbal or traditional medicine. Regular healthcare access: Yes. how often: Regularly (at least once a year). Health resources accessed: Local healthcare clinic or hospital. Other Healthcare conditions: None. Diet restrictions: Vegan. Smoking: No. Alcohol drinking: No. Physical activity: 1–2 days. Support network: Healthcare provider or counsellor. Health goals: Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?. her food access Limited access to healthy foods. Tone of the output: default.\\n\\nUsing the profile of Felismina Nhantumbo and understanding the persona's needs (\\"I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? \\"), identify the most relevant information of the persona's profile that can be leveraged to create an engaging story aimed at inspiring behavior change. List of relevant fields.\\nThen, Generate a five-paragraph health story written in Portuguese that centers around the needs of our persona, which is based on the following question: I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? . \\n Use spoken Portuguese, story-telling style, rhetorical question, with simple primary school vocabulary.  \\nThe story will have a small work task that foreshadows a larger work task. This will serve as external motivation for the persona to make health changes. The generated story should be in a default tone.\\n\\nUse only this medical ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start medical ground truth> \\n \\n<end medical ground truth> \\n\\nUse only this cultural ground truth to inform all story decisions and outcomes: \\n<start cultural ground truth> \\n \\n<end cultural ground truth> \\n\\nOutput Requirements\\n- Return only paragraphs written entirely in Portuguese.\\n- story should first person account\\n- Do not include explanations or any other language.\\n- All story paragraphs must be in Portuguese.\\n- The image prompts should be written entirely in English.\\n\\n\\n- **Paragraph 0:** Select persona fields related to routine, work responsibilities, and basic health knowledge gaps.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 1:**\\n  Introduce daily life and diet habits that reflect **limited awareness** of how health affects work.\\n  The small work task fails due to misunderstanding or neglect of health needs.\\n\\n- **Paragraph 2:**\\n  Help comes from a **formal health source** (clinic or health worker).\\n  Resistance is mild and based on uncertainty.\\n  Advice is clear, simple, personalized, culturally relevant, actionable, and practical.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 3:**\\n  The persona attempts the advice but struggles with **adjusting routines**.\\n  A minor setback occurs due to habit change.\\n  They persist because of the upcoming larger task.\\n  {max_word_count}\\n\\n- **Paragraph 4:**\\n  Gradual, realistic improvement occurs.\\n  The larger task is accomplished with more confidence.\\n  The persona becomes open to continued health improvement.\\n  {max_word_count}", "language": "pt", "story_arc": "default", "audio_prompts": ["Sound of birds chirping at dawn, mixed with the gentle rustling of leaves. Felismina's voice, a slightly raspy South African English accent, speaks slowly and deliberately: ‘O sol já está a nascer… Eu adoro comer um pedaço de massa com mel… é um prazer pequeno…’  A quiet, peaceful atmosphere.", "Sound of busy market activity: chatter of vendors, sounds of carts, and distant music. Felismina's voice, slightly hurried and stressed, saying: ‘O António olhou para mim com preocupação… Precisa comer algo…’ A sense of urgency and slight anxiety.", "Sound of a gentle, reassuring voice – Maria’s voice – speaking clearly and patiently in Portuguese. Felismina's voice responds hesitantly: ‘Mas e se eu estiver com muita fome à noite?’ A quiet, contemplative atmosphere.", "Sound of happy chatter and music from a wedding celebration. Felismina's voice, warm and joyful, saying: ‘Eu estou a tentar fazer escolhas melhores…’  The sounds of laughter and celebration create a vibrant and uplifting atmosphere."], "image_prompts": ["Felismina Nhantumbo, a 38 year old woman, standing in a field of ripe bananas at dawn, wearing a simple cotton dress, holding a woven basket filled with bananas, looking towards the rising sun with a determined expression. The field is lush and green, with a traditional mud house in the background, showing a rural Mozambican setting. Soft, golden light.", "Felismina Nhantumbo, 40 year old woman, struggling to carry a heavy basket of bananas on a dusty road, her face etched with effort, sweat glistening on her forehead. She is wearing a brightly colored headscarf and a simple dress. A small, weathered truck is visible in the distance. A sense of exhaustion and determination.", "Felismina Nhantumbo, 39 year old woman, sitting across from a kind-faced healthcare worker, Maria, in a small, brightly lit clinic room. Maria is pointing to a colorful chart with pictures of fruits and vegetables. Felismina is looking at the chart with a thoughtful expression, holding a small notebook. The clinic is clean and organized, with medical equipment visible in the background.", "Felismina Nhantumbo, 41 year old woman, smiling and holding a freshly baked cake, surrounded by family members at a wedding celebration. The cake is decorated with colorful fruit. She is wearing a traditional African dress. The room is filled with music and laughter, creating a warm and joyful atmosphere."], "language_code": "pt-PT", "avg_time_taken": 8.3145438402127, "task_parent_id": "b0162ecf-3cb0-48a4-ab52-c2e0a87f59a9", "audio_gen_model": "Azure Speech", "image_gen_model": "flux", "generated_queries": "[\\n  \\"What are some traditional Rhonga foods grown or available in rural X - Maputo that are safe for a diabetic woman my age to eat?\\",\\n  \\"How can I manage my Type 2 diabetes as a 35–44 year old female subsistence farmer in rural Mozambique with limited access to healthy foods?\\",\\n  \\"What low-cost, locally available foods in rural Maputo can help control blood sugar spikes for Methodist women?\\",\\n  \\"Are there specific fruits or vegetables native to the Maputo countryside that won't raise blood sugar and are in season now?\\",\\n  \\"Which breakfast foods commonly eaten in Rhonga communities are best for someone with Type 2 diabetes taking insulin and metformin?\\",\\n  \\"How can I prepare traditional Mozambican meals for family ceremonies that are healthier for my diabetes without losing cultural meaning?\\",\\n  \\"What are safe ways to include traditional herbs or remedies with my diabetes medications—like insulin or metformin—in rural Mozambique?\\",\\n  \\"What exercises or physical activities can a subsistence farmer woman with Type 2 diabetes do in rural areas with limited leisure time?\\",\\n  \\"How does daily alcohol consumption affect blood sugar for diabetic women in rural Maputo and what culturally appropriate ways are there to reduce it?\\",\\n  \\"Are there community support groups or Methodist church programs for diabetic women in small villages around X - Maputo?\\",\\n  \\"What are best local snack options available in my rural community that I can eat during traditional ceremonies to help avoid blood sugar spikes?\\",\\n  \\"How often should I check my blood sugar if I am physically active only 1–2 days a week and use both medication and traditional herbs in Mozambique?\\"\\n]", "relevant_profile_info": "", "selected_profile_info": [null, "city_town", "religion", "name", "gender", "age", "describe_location", "describe_food", "disability", "occupation", "daily_routine", "hobbies", "activities", "health_conditions", "medication", "healthcare_resources", "healthcare_access", "healthc